gin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>816</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n              </tbody>\n          </table>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A well-stocked library is essential to facilitate better student learning. As a focal access point for information, teaching, learning, and research, a college library is expected to provide standard information resources that would help the academic community members for their self-development, to fulfill the curriculum requirements, and to promote studies and research. We believe that access to Information is one of the most fundamental concerns of the library. It is our prime objective to keep our clientele up-to-date in their areas of interest and we strive to deliver all of our services with efficiency and dynamism and in the best interest of the University.</span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To fulfill the above-mentioned statement and to comply with the recommendations set by the evaluators both AACCUP and CHEDRO, the library acquired additional 581 titles/816 Volumes of books for the six programs offered in SDSSU Tagbina. - Ronie Sajelan-</span></p>\n          \n          <table class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n              <thead>\n                  <tr>\n                      <th colspan=\"3\" scope=\"col\">\n                      <p><strong>SDSSU Cagwait Campus Books Acquired<br />\n                      for A.Y.2018-2019</strong></p>\n                      </th>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>Program</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>Title</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>Volumes</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">BSHM</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">28</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">30</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">BSIT</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">60</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">67</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Gen.ed.</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">47</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">202</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Gen.ref</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">5</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">134</span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>Total</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>140</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td>\n                      <p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>433</strong></span></span></span></p>\n                      </td>\n                  </tr>\n              </thead>\n          </table>', NULL, 'University Library', 10, 'news', 0, '2018-08-22 09:29:18', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-1cf8-42d6-be0a-26860a064be6', 'SDSSU Linkaged with the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) - Knowledge Resource Collection (KRC)', 'sdssu-linkaged-with-the-bangko-sentral-ng-pilipinas-bsp-knowledge-resource-collection-krc', '<p>Last July 11, 2018, SDSSU Library in partnership with the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) Knowledge Resource Collections (KRCs) launched the BSP publications such as books, journals, reports, guides, manuals, primer brochures &amp; online databases.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Last July 11, 2018, SDSSU Library in partnership with the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) Knowledge Resource Collections (KRCs) launched the BSP publications such as books, journals, reports, guides, manuals, primer brochures &amp; online databases. The said program shall tap public and private libraries nationwide as venues to promote greater public understanding of essential economic and financial concepts and issues. The Network shall be composed of libraries of local government units (LGUs), national government agencies, and universities/colleges located nationwide.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The program was attended by the key officials of SDSSU headed by Dr. Gerry B. Estrada, VPAA &amp; Chairman, Library Board Committee, Mr. Roel T. Lim, HRMO, Mrs. Catherine F. Salomon, BOR secretary, Mrs. Glizriel Rose Z. Quijada, Bank Officer II-BSP Butuan, Deans of the different colleges, faculty and library personnel headed by the Director of Libraries Mrs. Aida C. Osorio, MSLS.&nbsp; Mr. Roel T. Lim formally opened the program with his warm welcome message. Followed by the brief discussion of Mrs. Glizriel Rose Z. Quijada about what KRN is all about and its implementation. After that, Dr. Gerry B. Estrada gives a message about the event, followed by the ribbon cutting and turn-over ceremony. Mrs. Aida C. Osorio, the head librarian formally closed the program by her closing message. It was a quite well accomplished activity. </span></span></span></p>', 'IMG_3784.jpg', 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2018-08-22 09:39:35', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-2085-4301-a20f-2163e3bed917', 'Dr. Dayao and Mr. Dumaran take seats in the Board', 'dr-dayao-and-mr-dumaran-take-seats-in-the-board', '<p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">Dr. Rosalyn C. Dayao , faculty President of SDSSU Main Campus &nbsp;is the new Federation President of the Faculty Club Associations. Dr. Dayao &nbsp;was instituted by Commissioner Alibin on July 27, 2018 Special Meeting of the Board.</span></span></span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Dr. Rosalyn C. Dayao , faculty President of SDSSU Main Campus&nbsp; is the new Federation President of the Faculty Club Associations. Dr. Dayao&nbsp; was instituted by Commissioner Alibin on July 27, 2018 Special Meeting of the Board.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/FB_IMG_1534468281467.jpg\" /></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:black; font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In the meantime, the new Federation President of Supreme Student Government is the SSG President of Lianga Campus, Hon. Jeanar H. Dumaran. Hon. Dumaran took his oath as new member of the Board during the second quarter meeting on June 14, 2018 at Park Inn Hotel, Davao City.</span></span></p>', 'IMG_20180727_09124467886.jpg', 'SDSSU Board of Regents', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-22 10:54:13', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-23cb-42d2-933d-da89f91d20ac', 'Pres. Estal is re-appointed for another term', 'pres-estal-is-re-appointed-for-another-term', '<p>On July 27, 2018, Rev. Fr. John Christian U. Young reported to the Board the result of the evaluation of the accomplishments of Dr. Baceledes R. Estal.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">On July 27, 2018, Rev. Fr. John Christian U. Young reported to the Board the result of the evaluation of the accomplishments of Dr. Baceledes R. Estal.&nbsp; In his report, Fr. Young articulated all the accomplishments of Dr. Estal as President from July 2014 to June 2018. These accomplishments were validated through on-site evaluation, document evaluation and interviews. He emphasized that the whole academic community of Surigao del Sur State University are one in supporting the re-appointment of DR. Baceledes R. Estal.&nbsp; The interview with various stakeholders&rsquo; representatives, faculty, staff, students and middle-level managers was done in the afternoon of June 28, 2018. These groups were interviewed as grouped. During the interview, common question thrown as to what rating would they gave to Dr. Estal from a rating of 1-10. Surprisingly, they gave a rating of 9 and the remaining 1 point remains to be accomplished by the President. Hence, they all vouched for the re-appointment of Dr. Estal.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">In addition, the interviewees described Dr. Estal as hands-on president, makatao, maloloy-on sa mga kabus, makatao, visible, approachable, action man, supportive, dedicated, open-minded, flexible, positive attitude, fatherly, and good adviser.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">On the other hand, the faculty representatives when asked of what is that 1 point that they wanted the President to focus. Their answer was planning and strengthen his foresight especially in conducting activities. They also wanted him to focus on the faculty development referring to the long-term development plan for the faculty to avert competition among themselves. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Generally, all the members of the academic community present during the interview have one and common want: TO RENEW DR. ESTAL AS PRESIDENT OF SDSSU.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Given this recommendation of the Evaluation Committee, the Board through the motion of Congressman Prospero B. Pichay, Jr, unanimously voted for the RE-APPOINTMENT OF DR. BACELEDES R. ESTAL as President of Surigao del Sur State University from the period covering July 27, 2018 to June 26, 2022.</span></span></p>', 'IMG_20180727_101528.jpg', 'SDSSU Board of Regents', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-22 11:42:54', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-270d-452f-a604-802e73075b19', 'Duty calls of the Evaluation Committee ….', 'duty-calls-of-the-evaluation-committee', '<p>When President Estal decided to extend his term of office for another four years, the Board through Board Resolution No. 47, series of 2018 created the Evaluation Committee chaired by FSSU President, Rev. Fr. John Christian U. Young. Working with Fr. Young in the evaluation of the performance and accomplishments of President in his four-year term of office were: Dr. Ma. Luisa Soliven, CMU President, Director Maricar Cascuejo, CHED Regional Director, Dr. Rosalyn C. Dayao, Faculty Representative and Dr. Josefina Prado, Private Sector Representative.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">When President Estal decided to extend his term of office for another four years, the Board through Board Resolution No. 47, series of 2018 created the Evaluation Committee chaired by FSSU President, Rev. Fr. John Christian U. Young. Working with Fr. Young in the evaluation of the performance and accomplishments of President in his four-year term of office were: Dr. Ma. Luisa Soliven, CMU President, Director Maricar Cascuejo, CHED Regional Director, Dr. Rosalyn C. Dayao, Faculty Representative and Dr. Josefina Prado, Private Sector Representative.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/36283428_1821944864518395_3321105138331942912_o.jpg\" /></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Duty bound to their commitments, the Evaluation Committee did due diligence in their evaluation as the fate of the re-appointment of President Estal was on their hands pursuant to Sec. 11 of CHED Memorandum No. 16 series of 2009 in titled Reappointment. The evaluation included the following activities:</span></span></p>\n          \n          <ul>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Review of reports and other documents</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">The incumbent&rsquo;s vision, mission, goals, plans and programs during his first term in office.</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Annual reports and accomplishment reports, mid-term and end-of term reports, reports on student performance in licensure examinations.</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Financial reports.</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">COA reports covering the period of the president&rsquo;s term.</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Copies of official student publication during the incumbency of the president.</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Copies of research journals and other publications</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Among other documents</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Interview with representatives from various sectors of the academic community</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Visits to other campuses or university/college projects</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Interview with the president</span></span></li>\n              <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Evaluation Committee&rsquo;s Assessment of the President using the BOT approved evaluation instrument. Evaluated using Numerical Ratings according to the following criteria: 1) the president as an academic leader, 2) the president as an institution builder, and 3) the president as a resource mobilizer or fundraiser.</span></span></li>\n          </ul>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">On that note, validation of the claims of the accomplishments was done tediously from ocular visits in the campuses to the interviews of various stakeholders. </span></span></p>', '36270606_1821945014518380_1225766744107253760_o.jpg', 'SDSSU Board of Regents', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-22 13:42:52', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-29c1-4739-a866-80b5ce821d54', 'Assessment on MTDP And Strategic Planning', 'assessment-on-mtdp-and-strategic-planning', '<p>The Key Officials of the University concluded the 3-day Assessment of the Medium Term Development Plan 2015-2019 and the Strategic Planning for 2020-2024 at Libona Bukidnon on October 21-25, 2018.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">The Key Officials of the University concluded the 3-day Assessment of the Medium Term Development Plan 2015-2019 and the Strategic Planning for 2020-2024 at Libona Bukidnon on October 21-25, 2018. Among the issues tackled were the accomplishments of the University in the Fourfold function: Instruction, Extension, Research, and Production. The vision of the University was also revisited prompting the officials to enhance the vision to fit with the new direction of the University. Dr. Roberto Padua, former CHED Commissioner, spearheaded the activity as the University consultant.</span></span></p>', '44510862_2265868243442410_8544053273147998208_o.jpg', 'Abundio C. Miralles', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-11-05 15:01:48', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-2bf9-4ec6-9452-3bd3b3e28831', 'Root Cause Analysis and Corrective Action Workshop', 'root-cause-analysis-and-corrective-action-workshop', '<p>Pursuant to CMO 46 s 2012 entitled Policy Standard to Enhance Quality Assurance in Philippine Higher Education, the Surigao Del Sur State University engaged in a 2-day workshop on October 26 and 29, 2018 at SDSSU-AVC.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Pursuant to CMO 46 s 2012 entitled Policy Standard to Enhance Quality Assurance in Philippine Higher Education, the Surigao Del Sur State University engaged in a 2-day workshop on October 26 and 29, 2018 at SDSSU-AVC. The workshop aimed to analyze the findings of the comprehensive internal audit conducted in the six (6) campuses of the University to provide an avenue for feed backing with the members of four (4) mandatory committees for ISO 9001: 2015. Participants to the workshop were tasked to present their findings for proper disposition of the management review before submission to the actual certification audit by the external certifying body. BCJA consultants facilitated the workshop with the direct supervision of the Quality Assurance Office of the University.</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Abundio C. Miralles', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-11-05 15:13:26', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-2dfb-4705-8b69-36c43c546bbb', 'Gis Training Workshop for New Breed Faculty of SDSSU', 'gis-training-workshop-for-new-breed-faculty-of-sdssu', '<p>The Research and Development Office held another GIS Training Workshop for new breed of faculties of the university last September 13-14, 2018 at the second floor building of the Research Office.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The Research and Development Office held another GIS Training Workshop for new breed of faculties of the university last September 13-14, 2018 at the second-floor building of the Research Office. The said activity was attended by participants from the six campuses, with the GIS consultant and speaker Dr. Alejandro F. Tongco.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">During the activity, orientation to GIS has been delivered by Dr. Tongco, followed with the workshop. Participants were trained on the simple basic GIS and able to present their outputs on the second day.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>', 'GIS TRAINING WORKSHOP FOR NEW BREED FACULTY.jpg', 'Flordeliza P. Torrico', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 14:35:16', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-2fcc-470a-9d3b-3778c20c572e', 'Theory Development Seminar-Workshop with Dr. Roberto N. Padua', 'theory-development-seminar-workshop-with-dr-roberto-n-padua', '<p>Selected faculties from the six campuses of the university joined the Theory Development Seminar-workshop at Libona Bukidnon on September 10-12, 2018.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Selected faculties from the six campuses of the university joined the Theory Development Seminar-workshop at Libona Bukidnon on September 10-12, 2018. Dr. Roberto N. Padua, resource speaker, emphasized that the Commission on Higher Education (CHED) has raised the requirements for graduate students to employ development and validation of new theories/models in their dissertation while theory validation/verification/contextualization for the master&rsquo;s thesis. Participants were oriented on the strategies of formulating and validating theories for research application.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">In addition, our university president Dr. Baceledes R. Estal with the Vice President for Administration and Finance Dr. Florife O. Urbiztondo visited our consultant and able to exchange discussions on plans and updates for the SDSSU.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Research And Development Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 14:45:08', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('987727bc-31d2-4789-9971-0e2e563bc9dc', 'GIS Brainstorming Activity at SDSSU Cagwait Campus', 'gis-brainstorming-activity-at-sdssu-cagwait-campus', '<p>SDSSU Faculty with the DOST Balik Scientist Dr. Alejandro F. Tongco conducted the One-day Brainstorming activity on GIS based program on Environmental Sustainability Plan for Surigao del Sur using Interdisciplinary Geospatial Approach at SDSSU Cagwait Campus on August 31, 2018.&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">SDSSU Faculty with the DOST Balik Scientist Dr. Alejandro F. Tongco conducted the One-day Brainstorming activity on GIS based program on Environmental Sustainability Plan for Surigao del Sur using Interdisciplinary Geospatial Approach at SDSSU Cagwait Campus on August 31, 2018. </span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Research And Development Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 14:49:51', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-344f-435e-800e-16abbbf88cf3', 'Packaging of Proposals on DOST’s Scientist Program', 'packaging-of-proposals-on-dosts-scientist-program', '<p>DOST Regional Director, Dir. Dominga D. Mallonga invited SDSSU for 2018 DOST Annual Regional Science and Technology Week.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">DOST Regional Director, Dir. Dominga D. Mallonga invited SDSSU for 2018 DOST Annual Regional Science and Technology Week. In response to the said invitation, SDSSU administration sent faculty researchers such as Dr. Ana Marie T. Acevedo, Dr. Jocelyn B. Panduyos, Dr. Roxan G. Eupena, Amor Salinas, Liaflora Orcullo and Dr. Bernardita Quevedo to participate and witness the celebration of the department.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Dr. Quevedo of SDSSU Lianga Campus presented her project proposal during the celebration. The participants accepted her proposal and made some corrections for enhancement of her paper.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">In the end, the celebration of the department has been memorable since it was attended by known and steamed guests from agencies nationwide. </span></span></span></p>', 'Packaging of Proposals on DOST’s Scientist Program.jpg', 'Research And Development Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 15:00:41', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-36ed-4ccb-8754-3976c0136c08', 'SDSSU Group of Researchers Participated in the 1st Blue Carbon Networking Workshop', 'sdssu-group-of-researchers-participated-in-the-1st-blue-carbon-networking-workshop', '<p>Every organization has its creative process of innovating and integrating individual&rsquo;s potential that can illustrate the process of their works.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Every organization has its creative process of innovating and integrating individual&rsquo;s potential that can illustrate the process of their works. &ldquo;Working Together Make Sense!&rdquo; was the theme for the 1st National Blue Carbon Network (BCNet) Workshop held on September 22, 2018 at Philippine Red Cross Logistic and Training Center, Subic Zambales. The main objective of the said workshop was to bring together more researchers, policy makers, coastal entrepreneurs and other stakeholders primarily to present the different perspectives and applications of coastal blue carbon and its ecosystem in climate change mitigation.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The SDSSU group of researchers headed by Dr. Jocely B. Panduyos, actively participated and converged around with the Mindanao group of researchers from various higher institutions to contribute and formulate arguments on Blue Carbon Network. Series of presentations before the delivery of the detailed workshop agenda were conveyed. Dr. Anthony Sales, DOST Region IX Director, warmed-up the event with his opening remarks. Prof. Zazuo Nadaoka, Chief Technical Adviser of BlueCares, presented the highlights of the Blue Cares Project. Along with his presentation were the updates on the different activities conducted by different leaders under the Blue Cares Project. Aided by their respective projects, a number of experts in the same field, substantiated the talk of Prof. Nadaoka and also shared the progress of their projects focusing on the role of BCNet. Dr. Miguel D. Fortes, Blue Carbon Program Specialists, delivered some tips for successful network on Blue Carbon. Subsequently, on the later part, the three clusters (Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao) were asked to head up the workshop proper through sharing of relevant ideas with regards BCNet. Idea-storming among clusters sparked as they convene and complete the tasks. The Mindanao Cluster, which is mainly composed of MSU-Naawan, MSU-Tawi-tawi, MSU-IIT, SDSSU Campus, Xavier University, Ateneo De Davao University, USTP and University of Mindanao, decided to productively work together on Blue Carbon Network. It was truly a successful brainstorming activity where respectful and healthy agreement was observed.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">After the workshop time, Dr. Fortes handled the presentation of each cluster&rsquo;s output. He even encouraged the participants to provide feedback and comment on the output presented. He emphasized that contextualization of whatever issues observed in respective locality should be raised because he believes that big change starts from doing small things. Dr. Fortes ended up his facilitation with the famous line of Henry Ford, which states &ldquo;coming together is a beginning, keeping together is progress, and working together is success.&rdquo; The SDSSU group has not just impressed the cluster with its active participation, but indeed, has even realized the importance of conserving and protecting Blue Carbon. SDSSU always care!</span></span></span></p>', '1st Blue Carbon Networking Workshop.jpg', 'Odinah C. Enteria', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-28 15:13:10', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-39ca-4c95-9191-1102849b341f', '1st National Blue Carbon Symposium (NCBS-1) at Subic Freeport Zone, Zambales', '1st-national-blue-carbon-symposium-ncbs-1-at-subic-freeport-zone-zambales', '<p>SDSSU responded the call and accepted the challenged to participate in achieving nature based solutions in mitigating climate change issues last September 19-22, 2018 at Philippine Red Cross Logistics and Training Center, Subic Freeport Zone, Zambales.&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>SDSSU </strong>responded the call and accepted the challenged to participate in achieving nature-based solutions in mitigating climate change issues last September 19-22, 2018 at Philippine Red Cross Logistics and Training Center, Subic Freeport Zone, Zambales.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">DOST PCIEERD, UPD, Iam BLUECECAM, BLUECARES, spearheaded the activity to bring together experts and practitioners from around the Philippines to better understand the Blue Carbon ecosystem to mitigate climate and human impacts to the coastal ecosystem.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Nine (9) participants coming from different campuses of SDSSU actively joins the scientific discussions, two (2) from SDSSU-Lianga were poster presenters.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The Symposium highlighted the latest information on how the coastal domain in the country is changing and how to respond to it and promote collaborations to various government and non-government sectors to bridge the gap in knowledge, policy and practice of the blue carbon ecosystem.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The half-day trip to Triboa Mangrove Park on September 19,2018 sponsored by Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority (SBMA) was a team activity, were each team is on a rotation basis for mangrove DBH measurement, drone survey, spectroscopy, laser scanning and core sampling.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Sheila Kylene A. Tawas', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-28 15:34:31', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-3cc2-48ca-b6b4-32179656f6b1', 'R and D Office Spearheads a Seminar-Workshop on Writing a Publishable Research Paper', 'r-and-d-office-spearheads-a-seminar-workshop-on-writing-a-publishable-research-paper', '<p>The University with its Research roadmap is earnestly preparing its research workforce for the requirement of the 21st century creator of knowledge, imbued with the characteristics of innovation, adaptation and discovery.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The University with its Research roadmap is earnestly preparing its research workforce for the requirement of the&nbsp;21</span></span><sup>st&nbsp;</sup><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">century creator of knowledge, imbued with the characteristics of innovation, adaptation and discovery. This is important because the world is becoming more and more connected. With this interconnectivity, the need to be competitive is a necessity. Thus, with this, the R and D Office spearheaded a seminar-workshop on writing a publishable&nbsp;&nbsp; paper with its novice faculty as the participants of the said huddle last July 19-20, 2018, held at the SDSSU Old Library Main Campus. An international speaker from the University of Hawaii in the person of Dr. Francisco P. Dumanig was invited to talk on the topic. Rookies in the research aspect were taught on how to refine their paper so that it will be acceptable for publication. With this output, it is envisioned that there will be an increased utilization of the research productivity and so doing, there will be an attainment of the Vision and Mission of the University as a whole.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-16 15:50:29', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-3f73-4b94-99b1-b91bbe832120', 'RESEARCHERS’ PLIGHT IN LIBONA', 'researchers-plight-in-libona', '<p>Despite hectic schedules of the researchers in their university routinary tasks, thy tried their best to cope up with the expected research outputs in Libona.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Despite hectic schedules of the researchers in their university routinary tasks, thy tried their best to cope up with the expected research outputs in Libona. Series of lectures were made by Dr. Roberto N. Padua, the research resource trainer:&nbsp; June 20 &ndash; 22, 2018 &ndash; Data Mining and Big Data Analytics 1, July 16 &ndash; 18, 2018 &ndash; Data Mining and Big Data Analytics 2. In the seminar &ndash; workshop the university researchers were grouped into three with three members each group. Each group has to come up with three publishable research articles based the lectures of the research resource trainer.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Last August 13 &ndash; 15, 2018, the finalization of research outputs was instigated. The finished research articles were presented and simultaneously corrected by Dr. Padua. Each group of the researchers had accomplished one publishable research article and the other two articles are still on going.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Dr. Edmundo C. Lopez', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-16 15:56:34', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-427b-4a7e-8266-8fe7c95a4d47', 'SDSSU Researchers Attend 12th Philippine National Health Research System Conference', 'sdssu-researchers-attend-12th-philippine-national-health-research-system-conference', '<p>Themed on &ldquo;Research and Innovation for Equity and Health&rdquo;, seven SDSSU faculty and staff researchers attended &nbsp;the 12th Philippine National Health and Research System (PNHRS) Week at the CAP John Hay Trade and Cultural Center in Baguio City on August 6-9, 2018.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Themed on &ldquo;Research and Innovation for Equity and Health&rdquo;, seven SDSSU faculty and staff researchers attended the 12<sup>th</sup> Philippine National Health and Research System (PNHRS) Week at the CAP John Hay Trade and Cultural Center in Baguio City on August 6-9, 2018. The group headed by the Research and Development Unit Director, Dr. Jocelyn B. Panduyos was also joined by Dr. Lady Sol A. Suazo, Dr. Mardie E. Bucjan, Engr. Luzminda S. Bacquial, Ms. Giselle B. Ramos of SDSSU Main, Ms. Liaflora C. Orcullo of SDSSU Lianga Campus and Ms. Violita Dabalos of SDSSU San Miguel.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Dr. Ernesto O. Domingo, a national scientist and the keynote speaker of the event emphasized that &ldquo;the real challenge in research is not excellence but relevance, that research should yield the most for communities; and that real equity is addressing the inequity: lifespan is not enjoyed by all particularly those in the lower strata of the society&rdquo;.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">On the second day, the SDSSU participants attended the parallel session on Traditional Knowledge (TK) research. They joined the Assessment of the Traditional Knowledge Documentation Program based on the WIPO Recommendations with Dr. Isidro C. Sia, the TK Program Leader/consultant. The session aimed to revisit the completed and ongoing TK documentation projects and proposal to determine compliance as SDSSU with its four proposal in the pipeline is currently finalizing requirements for the eventual release of funds to commence implementation.</span></span></span></p>', '12th Philippine National Health Research System Conference.jpg', 'Liaflora C. Orcullo', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-16 16:11:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-454a-4fc1-b33b-8c99f06ea25b', 'RESEARCHERS’ QUEST IN ICMAR', 'researchers-quest-in-icmar', '<p>Last July 24 &ndash; 26, 2018, SDSSU, which is one of the members of the Visayas &ndash; Mindanao Consortium for Journal Publication (VMCJP), was co &ndash; hosting the 1st International Conference on Methodological Advances in Research (ICMAR) held in the University of San Jose Recoletus (USJR), Cebu City.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Last July 24 &ndash; 26, 2018, SDSSU, which is one of the members of the Visayas &ndash; Mindanao Consortium for Journal Publication (VMCJP), was co &ndash; hosting the 1<sup>st</sup> International Conference on Methodological Advances in Research (ICMAR) held in the University of San Jose Recoletus (USJR), Cebu City. Some SDSSU participants served as judges, moderators, and secretariat during the parallel sessions. Besides, the conference was participated by all the members of the VMCJP and non &ndash; members of the association from Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Sixteen (16) researchers from our university were sent to present their research outputs in different categories. Among the research presenters, two of which got the BEST PRESENTER&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">AWARDS in their respective category &ndash; they were Odinah Cuartero &ndash; Enteria and Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Dr. Edmundo C. Lopez', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-16 16:46:28', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-48a2-4d8c-80d1-c55e89fef93b', 'EXTENSION TEAMS VISITS MAITOM', 'extension-teams-visits-maitom', '<p>A courtesy meeting was held with the Brgy. Captain Honorable Hon. Samuel P. Cedron &nbsp;with aim to introduce the SDSSU extension programs.&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:black\">A courtesy meeting was held with the Brgy. Captain Honorable Hon. Samuel P. Cedron&nbsp; with aim to introduce the SDSSU extension programs. The objective of the visit was to engage extension project to the barangay. The team was led by Maria Cristina S. Dela Cerna, OIC Diretor for Extension Services and Linkages, Ms. Roselyn Malong, BSBA Extension Coordinator and Mr. Castor Balacuit, project leader.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:black\">In his response, the brgy.captain expressed his happiness for the visit. He promised his commitment and discuss further opportunities for future collaboration. He then invited the team to attend the barangay session on November 9, 2018.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:black\">At the end of the visit, the team conducted the Training Needs Assessment.</span></span></p>', 'EXTENSION TEAMS VISITS MAITOM.png', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-11-26 07:47:24', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-4be3-4823-8adf-59d6e16814e1', 'Root-crops Production Seminar at Mabuhay', 'root-crops-production-seminar-at-mabuhay', '<p>The BS Hospitality Management of the College of Business and Management spearheaded a seminar on Root-crops Production. The seminar provided a venue for farmers to production issues, to discuss and &nbsp;to learn new technologies.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">The BS Hospitality Management of the College of Business and Management spearheaded a seminar on Root-crops Production.&nbsp; The seminar provided a venue for farmers to production issues, to discuss and to learn new technologies. The activity leader, Ramonito Tan explained the importance of root crops. He emphasized that these products are considered a global source of carbohydrates and provide some minerals and essential vitamins. Root crops are essential sources of food and feed among the residents in Mabuhay, Tandag City Surigao del Sur and agricultural land is devoted to root crops production. Hence, the extension team initiated a seminar to address food and nutrition security and to produce more crops.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><img alt=\"Root-crops Production Seminar at Mabuhay\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Root-crops%20Production%20Seminar%20at%20Mabuhay2.png\" /></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">The available crops such as cassava, sweet potato and Gabi have been made into chips and they named it CHIKA CHIPS. The word chika literally means gossip. The idea came from a beneficiary in her impression that while chatting with friends they make use of their time cooking and producing more chips to increase their income. The beneficiaries dreamed to have the best root crops chips in Surigao del Sur thus participants were encouraged to come up with their own creative dishes.</span></span></span></p>', 'Root-crops Production Seminar at Mabuhay.png', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-11-26 08:00:53', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-4f6f-499a-aaba-0c8a612da593', 'Haribon Foundation Visits Extension Office', 'haribon-foundation-visits-extension-office', '<p>BOW team of the Haribon Foundation visited the Office of the Extension Services and Linkages &nbsp;on September 24, 2018 to finalize the project on Biodiversity on Wheels.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Gill Sans MT&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">BOW team of the Haribon Foundation visited the Office of the Extension Services and Linkages on September 24, 2018 to finalize the project on Biodiversity on Wheels. The Haribon has been the partner of Surigao del Sur State University in the implementation of the extension services for so long. The team explained that the BOW is a moving classroom that uses age-appropriate and interactive ways of teaching the people. It has a built-in multimedia and library rolled into one van that visits schools and communities to teach environmental topics such as Philippine biodiversity and solid waste management. Through BOW biodiversity, conservation is now more accessible to children, but more young people have yet to be reached to ensure a brighter future for ourselves and our environment.</span></span></span></span></p>', 'Haribon Foundation Visits Extension Office.png', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-10-22 08:11:17', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-523b-4367-adad-bb123cbd746c', 'FITS Center launches at Carmen Surigao del Sur', 'fits-center-launches-at-carmen-surigao-del-sur', '<p>The Local Government of Carmen, Surigao del Sur launched its own FITS center on October 12, 2018 spearheaded by the Agricultural Training Institute-Regional Training Center CARAGA.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The Local Government of Carmen, Surigao del Sur launched its own FITS center on October 12, 2018&nbsp;&nbsp; spearheaded by the Agricultural Training Institute -Regional Training Center CARAGA. The said event was attended by the town&rsquo;s Municipal Vice Mayor, Hon.Teofila G. Cabatuan, the provincial agriculturist, Mr. Mark Quico the university president, Dr. Baceledes R. Estal and partner agency representatives. Since Carmen is the adopted municipality of the extension services of Surigao del Sur State University, the university president officially launched the center. After the ribbon cutting ceremony, the university president delivered his message. The content of his message gave emphasis on education and the extension programs the university has. He also encouraged the farmers to bring their children to SDSSU. On the other hand, the Vice Mayor expressed her hopes and gratitude for the success of the event and for the presence of the invited dignitaries. She was also thankful for having their FITS center wherein constituents can avail its services. Likewise, the provincial agriculturist urged the farmers present to use the FITS Center and disseminate the words about it. He added that the backbone of our Nation are the farmers. Accordingly, the OIC-Center Director, ATI Regional Office discussed that the FITS Center is part of the extension modality known as the Techno Gabay Program initiated by the Philippine Council for Agriculture, Aquatic and Natural Resources Research and Development (PCAARRD). In 2012 the TGP was transferred to the Department of Agriculture and is now being implemented by the Agricultural Training Institute. The TGP aims to enhance the extension services of the municipal and provincial agriculture offices in the country with emphasis on the generation, adoption, and promotion of science-based technologies at the farmers &lsquo;level.</span></span></span></p>', 'FITS Center launches at Carmen Surigao del Sur.png', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-10-09 08:19:08', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-54f8-497f-8a75-bd673735fc05', 'Technical Training on Arduino Programming', 'technical-training-on-arduino-programming', '<p>The College of Engineering, Computer Studies and Technology (CECST) &nbsp;spearheaded the &nbsp;Technical &nbsp;Training on Arduino Programming &nbsp;dated September 4-5, 2018 with &nbsp;Mr. Jhon S. Atienza &nbsp;, Automation and Training Director &nbsp;from &nbsp;RSA Automation and &nbsp;Robotics Services &nbsp;whose expertise &nbsp;includes: Android Development , Mobile Computing , Cyber Security , PLC Programming using Siemens LOGO &nbsp;Siemens S7200, Arduino Programming and some of the widely used &nbsp;technology such as: &nbsp;RFID , Sensor , Pneumatics , Semiconductor, Electronic , Automation and Mechatronics Technology.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Gill Sans MT&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">The College of Engineering, Computer Studies and Technology (CECST)&nbsp; spearheaded the&nbsp; Technical&nbsp; Training on Arduino Programming&nbsp; dated September 4-5, 2018 with&nbsp; Mr. Jhon S. Atienza&nbsp; , Automation and Training Director&nbsp; from&nbsp; RSA Automation and&nbsp; Robotics Services&nbsp; whose expertise&nbsp; includes: Android Development , Mobile Computing , Cyber Security , PLC Programming using Siemens LOGO&nbsp; Siemens S7200, Arduino Programming and some of the widely used&nbsp; technology such as:&nbsp; RFID , Sensor , Pneumatics , Semiconductor, Electronic , Automation and Mechatronics Technology.</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Gill Sans MT&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">On September 4, 2018 Registration of Participants starts from 7:30 am to 8:00 am. The Opening Program follows after the registration with Ms. Henz Antoinette Q. Yusico, one of the CECST English Instructors as the emcee. During the short opening program Engr. Jessie A. Demonta&ntilde;o, CECST Assistant Dean and BSCS Faculty Member gave his welcome message. Ms. Born Christian A. Isip, Proponent of the Activity and BSCS Program Chair explains the rationale of the Training. The Extension Coordinator, Engr. Divine Grace N. Loren then introduces the participants followed by the Presentation of the Resource Speaker introduced by the emcee.</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Gill Sans MT&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Right after the fifteen (15)-minute opening program the expert started his lecture on microcontrollers and robotics in order for the participants to have a grasp of Arduino as the widely used microcontroller in programming an automated and embedded systems. When the lecture was done, the resource speaker distributes one microcontroller device for each participant instructing them to connect to the desktop or laptop computer via usb extension port prior to the hands-on activities to be performed by the participants based on the instruction given by the expert. Except for the three (3) BSCS faculty members of the College, majority of the participants do not have basic experience in the use of Arduino Microcontroller. It was difficult for participants to start the initial task/activity despite the step by step instruction given. The participant from St. Theresa College received a cash incentive of two hundred pesos (Php 200.00) from the speaker being the first to present and generate the correct programming output.&nbsp;&nbsp; After the completion of the first task, it was evident that the participants are very much willing to learn and they consider the activities as new ICT educational challenges of which their energy was sustained based on the outputs they have successfully generated throughout the sessions. The training is anchored on the University&rsquo;s Vision in Developing Renewable Energy by designing new and efficient technology using Arduino Microcontroller. The training ended with new knowledge and skills gained by the participants who were logically challenged and at the same time enjoyed with their various outputs. The activity proponent, Born Christian A. Isip distributes the Training Evaluation Sheets after the two-day technical training for the participants to rate, write and suggest on the training being conducted.</span></span></span></span></p>', 'DSC_1505.jpg', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 08:51:35', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-5813-41d6-bae5-7cd834ca5daa', 'Training on Basic Money Management', 'training-on-basic-money-management', '<p>Training on Basic Money Management Skills Part 1 started with the registration of the Participants at 8:00 in the morning.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Training on Basic Money Management Skills Part 1 started with the registration of the Participants at 8:00 in the morning. The training proper started with a topic on budgeting, budgeting breakers, irregular income and household expenses discussed by Ms. Johnith N. Montero, CBM Faculty. The concepts of income expenses and spending were discussed by Dr. Ermilux Matildo. The participants were very interested to know how to manage debt since this is one of the identified contributing factors to poor money management. Money management games for adults initiated by Ms. Suzette L. Josol.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Gill Sans MT&quot;,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">After the training-workshop, one of the participants delivered her impression about the activity.</span></span></span></span></p>', 'Training on Basic Money Management.png', 'Melissa B. Tantoy', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-09-24 08:59:33', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-5b58-425d-b093-b51b4481c3de', 'Extensionists defend the SSF proposal', 'extensionists-defend-the-ssf-proposal', '<p>Last July 28, 2018, the Head of Extension Services, Dr. Maria Cristina S. Dela Cerna together with Ms. Judith J. Sanchez, HM Extension Coordinator and Mr. Ramonito Tan, the proponent successfully presented and defended the SSF proposal in DTI Region in Butuan City.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Last July 28, 2018, the Head of Extension Services, Dr. Maria Cristina S. Dela Cerna together with Ms. Judith J. Sanchez, HM Extension Coordinator and Mr. Ramonito Tan, the proponent successfully presented and defended the SSF proposal in DTI Region in Butuan City.&nbsp; There were series of questions thrown regarding the proposal and the business plan. The DTI team explained the process, the objectives and the purpose of the project once it is approved. It was suggested during the deliberation that the proposal needs to be revised especially in the identification of the facilities. It was further recommended that small equipment need not to be included. Consequently, it was declared proposal has been approved in principle provided that all the suggestions and recommendations be incorporated and final copy shall be submitted on or before the deadline.</span></span></span></p>', 'Extensionists defend the SSF proposal.png', 'Extension Services and Linkages', NULL, 'news', 1, '2018-08-06 09:05:57', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-5dea-4099-aaff-cb883e4cf07e', 'ISO 9001:2015 External Certification Audit', 'iso-90012015-external-certification-audit', '<p>The Surigao Del Sur State University PASSED the recently concluded ISO 9001:2015 External Certification Audit &nbsp;by NQA Global Assurance spearheaded by its led auditor Mr. Rannie Bernardino on January 9-10, 2019.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Surigao Del Sur State University PASSED the recently concluded ISO 9001:2015 External Certification Audit by NQA Global Assurance spearheaded by its led auditor Mr. Rannie Bernardino on January 9-10, 2019. The two-day audit covered the following offices: R and D, Extension Services, Student Affairs, Welfare and Services, Graduate School, Colleges, Human Resource, Quality Assurance, Physical Plant, including Cantilan, Lianga, and Tagbina Campuses. During the exit conference at SDSSU Tagbina the key Officials re-affirmed the commitment of the University in the pursuit of quality management system.&nbsp; The led auditor was also joined by Dr. Ryan Liba, CHE, DBA.</span></span></p>', '49848338_2383422598353640_8248151767578050560_o.jpg', 'Abundio C. Miralles', NULL, 'news', 1, '2019-01-28 10:32:49', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-6147-4e8c-920e-3a098e81bf35', 'SDSSU Library as the First Follet Destiny Library Manager', 'sdssu-library-as-the-first-follet-destiny-library-manager', '<p style=\"margin-right:0pt; text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Electronic Information Solutions Inc. (EISI) celebrates their 25th Founding Anniversary last&nbsp; November 21, 2018 at 4th floor Pavilion Hall, Manhattan Parkview, Araneta Center, Cubao, Quezon City . As part of their celebration, EISI recognized some of their library partners and librarians in the Philippines and received </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\"><em><strong>Plaque of Recognition.</strong></em></span></span></span></span></span></p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Electronic Information Solutions Inc. (EISI) celebrates their 25th Founding Anniversary last&nbsp; November 21, 2018 at 4th floor Pavilion Hall, Manhattan Parkview, Araneta Center, Cubao, Quezon City . As part of their celebration, EISI recognized some of their library partners and librarians in the Philippines and received <em><strong>Plaque of Recognition.</strong></em></span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Surigao Del Sur State University (SDSSU) Library was recognized as the &ldquo;EISI&rsquo;s First Follett Destiny Library Manager Installation in Academic Library (State University)&rdquo;. Ms. Maria Lea Griettel Espa&ntilde;a-Cortez as the representative of the institution received the Plaque of Recognition with the President of EISI Ms. Minna Fe T. Avila, ChE., MBA and the Mindanao Wide EISI Manager.</span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:center\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/46503385_2326321380728734_3606468134187302912_n.jpg\" style=\"height:393px; width:294px\" /></p>', '46518980_2326321237395415_1824346633819652096_n.jpg', 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-25 15:44:19', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-6452-42e2-8cb1-1c1cb7eeff2d', 'NLP-PLD Affiliated Barangay Reading Center', 'nlp-pld-affiliated-barangay-reading-center', '<p>The Surigao Del Sur State University Administration Library Management administration &amp; staff and students would like to congratulate the Victoria Barangay Reading Center Management headed by its Barangay Captain, Hon. Alison Hangad, Tago, Surigao del Sur for completing the 2018 monthly reports to the National Library of the Philippines, Public Libraries Division (NLP-PLD). The said Barangay Reading Center, as an adopted library of Surigao Del Sur State University will be given a Certificate of Completion on March 21, 2019, during the 2019 National Conference of Librarians in Palawan.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Surigao Del Sur State University Administration Library Management administration &amp; staff and students would like to congratulate the Victoria Barangay Reading Center Management headed by its Barangay Captain, Hon. Alison Hangad, Tago, Surigao del Sur for completing the 2018 monthly reports to the National Library of the Philippines, Public Libraries Division (NLP-PLD). The said Barangay Reading Center, as an adopted library of Surigao Del Sur State University will be given a Certificate of Completion on March 21, 2019, during the 2019 National Conference of Librarians in Palawan.</span></p>', NULL, 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 09:59:29', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-67e2-404c-b139-c1de54162fc8', 'CHEDRO Quality Assessment Team Survey Visit for Bachelor of Science in Information Technology', 'chedro-quality-assessment-team-survey-visit-for-bachelor-of-science-in-information-technology', '<p>Upholding the vision to be a &quot;Leading Glocal University&quot;, SDSSU Cagwait Campus submitted BSIT to CHEDRO RQAT team for survey visit which commenced last Nov. 20, 2018.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Upholding the vision to be a &quot;Leading Glocal University&quot;, SDSSU Cagwait Campus submitted BSIT to CHEDRO RQAT team for survey visit which commenced last Nov. 20, 2018. </span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">SDSSU Cagwait Campus welcomed 2 monitoring and evaluation team led by sir Amy C. Saavedra, MSCA together with Ma&#39;am Irene May C. Escauso, MIT. </span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The program was evaluated based on the following areas: 1. Administration; 2. Faculty; 3. Curriculum; 4. Instructional Standards; 5. Library; 6. Physical Facilities; 7. Others.</span></p>', NULL, 'Relina O. Jabal', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 10:09:08', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-6c23-4ee2-bdb5-45785fb43ce6', 'The Move toward Institutional Sustainability Assessment (ISA)', 'the-move-toward-institutional-sustainability-assessment-isa', '<p>In spite having achieved the most numbered of accredited programs by Accrediting Agency of Chartered Colleges and Universities in the Philippines (AACCUP) among SUCs in Caraga, Surigao del Sur State University is showing no signs of resting on its nest.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In spite having achieved the most numbered of accredited programs by Accrediting Agency of Chartered Colleges and Universities in the Philippines (AACCUP) among SUCs in Caraga, Surigao del Sur State University is showing no signs of resting on its nest.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In this continuing pursuit for academic excellence, the university is now moving to submit itself to the Commission on Higher Education&rsquo;s (CHED) Institutional Sustainability Assessment (ISA) accreditation on September 2018.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A training and seminar workshops was called for by the Commission on Higher Education- Regional Office (CHED-RO) for the four State Universities and Colleges in Caraga Region which was held at the Kansilad Beach Resort, Lianga, Surigao del Sur last May 2-4, 2018.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The seminar workshops were participated in by four SUCs of Caraga Region namely: CSU, SSCT, ASCAT and SDSSU.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Speakers were from the four SUCs to wit : Dr. Mary Sylette Gunigundo, the CEPS, QA Division, OIQAG discusses on the topic overview of the ISA Framework. Dr. Rita Sescar, SVEPS, QA Division, OIQAG talks on the ISA Process: Pre-Visit to Post Visit Roles of CHEDRO &amp; OIQAG, Preparation for the Visit Dr. Francis This Cimene delved on the topic The ISA SED, while Dr. Emmanuel James Pattaguan vividly discusses on the topic Writing a Self-Evaluation Document supplemented with a workshops.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In ISA, the institution will be assessed based on the Five Key Result Areas: KRA 1: Governance and management; 2: Quality of teaching and learning; KRA 3: Quality of professional exposure, research and creative works; KRA 4: Support to students; KRA 5: Relations with the community.</span></p>', 'IMG_1006.jpg', 'Ronie A. Sajelan, MSLS', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 10:19:32', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-6f9b-4716-abb1-664a67f1956e', 'SDSSU Tandag Technical Librarian Attends the National Congress', 'sdssu-tandag-technical-librarian-attends-the-national-congress', '<p>The Philippine Librarians Association Incorporated (PLAI) in partnership with the National Commission for Culture and the Arts (NCCA), through the National Committee on Libraries and Information Services (NCLIS) J. Amado Araneta Foundation, and the Quezon City Local Government conducted a National Congress on November 20-23, 2018 at Novotel Manila, Araneta Center, Cubao, Quezon City with the theme &ldquo;Connected&nbsp; Actions, Collective Vision: Libraries Transforming Society&rdquo;.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Philippine Librarians Association Incorporated (PLAI) in partnership with the National Commission for Culture and the Arts (NCCA), through the National Committee on Libraries and Information Services (NCLIS) J. Amado Araneta Foundation, and the Quezon City Local Government conducted a National Congress on November 20-23, 2018 at Novotel Manila, Araneta Center, Cubao, Quezon City with the theme &ldquo;Connected&nbsp; Actions, Collective Vision: Libraries Transforming Society&rdquo;. Ms. Maria Lea Griettel Espa&ntilde;a&ndash; Cortez attended the Congress.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Congress 2018 aimed to understand the role of libraries and Information centers in building literate, informed, and participative societies, thereby contributing to societal, cultural, and economic growth of a nation; recognize that connected actions and collective vision of the library community will help libraries address the challenges of the future; to engage libraries, archives, and other cultural heritage partners and institutions in safeguarding cultural heritage in all its diverse forms; and to advocate the roles of librarians and library associations as key players for societal improvements and change through capacity building and professional agenda.</span></p>', 'Picture34.png', 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 10:30:15', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-73ae-4232-9ff1-54bf3ff75a9e', '84th National Book Week Celebration of SDSSU Library Management System', '84th-national-book-week-celebration-of-sdssu-library-management-system', '<p>The SDSSU Library Management System-Tandag Campus celebrates its 84th National Book Week with its theme: &ldquo;Connected Action, Collective Vision: Libraries Transforming Society&rdquo; Dec. 3-7, 2018. Afternoon of Dec. 3, 2018 the said event was formally opened by conducting the first two activities.</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The SDSSU Library Management System-Tandag Campus celebrates its 84th National Book Week with its theme: &ldquo;Connected Action, Collective Vision: Libraries Transforming Society&rdquo; Dec. 3-7, 2018. Afternoon of Dec. 3, 2018 the said event was formally opened by conducting the first two activities. Namely: The Poster Making and the Essay Writing Contest. Poster Making was participated by CTE and CECST students while the Essay Writing contest was participated by the CBM and CTE students. Day 2 activities were the Spelling Bee &amp; the Find Me contest that last for 3 days. Day 3 activities were the Quiz Bowl and the Library Henyo I could tell that this day was the most enjoyable part of the celebration. Day 4 was for the culminating activity.</span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Library management has also library awardees such as Most Valuable Faculty Users, Top Most Faculty Library Users, Most Valuable Student Library Users and Top Most Student Library Users. Same goes to the other Campuses celebrating the same activity. The Library awardees and winners have received a Certificate of Appreciation and Recognition, trophy and cash during the Culmination Activity.</span></p>', 'IMG_4941.JPG', 'Realyn B. Medrano', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 11:11:19', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-77e5-49a8-925c-836c0d260620', 'CHED – Caraga RQAT Conducts Program Monitoring and Evaluation', 'ched-caraga-rqat-conducts-program-monitoring-and-evaluation', '<p>The SDSSU Lianga Campus Library is one area for RQAT (Regional Quality Assurance Team). The seven program offerings of SDSSU-Lianga Campus submits to Program Monitoring and Evaluation on August 16, 2018 for the issuance of COPC (Certificate of Program Compliance).</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The SDSSU Lianga Campus Library is one area for RQAT (Regional Quality Assurance Team). The seven program offerings of SDSSU-Lianga Campus submits to Program Monitoring and Evaluation on August 16, 2018 for the issuance of COPC (Certificate of Program Compliance). Present during this evaluation are the CHED- Caraga Program Supervisors headed by Dr. Evangeline E. Daga-ang (Educational Supervisor II) and Mrs. Amy C. Saavedra (Education Supervisor II) and Mrs. Coeme Rose B., Deluta (Education Supervisor II). Programs involved are Bachelor of Science in Fisheries (BSFi), Bachelor in Elementary Education (BEED), Bachelor of Secondary Education (BSED), Bachelor of Science in Business Administration major in Financial Management (BSBA-FM), Bachelor of Science in Business Administration major in Business Economics (BSBA-BE), Bachelor of Science in Hotel and Restaurant Management (BSHRM), and Bachelor of Science in Computer Science (BSCS). After inspecting the documents presented and ocular inspection of physical facilities, comments and recommendations to be accomplished with one month are pronounced.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Dr. Cynthia P. Sajot, Campus Director, SDSSU Lianga Campus, gives her commitment to positively response to the given recommendations. Dr. Sajot emphasizes that this aim on issuance of COPC will lead to giving quality education and services to the community.</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Josephine S. Melencion, R.L.', 10, 'news', 1, '2019-07-26 11:20:31', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('987727bc-7bc1-4067-9b80-80baa97887c1', 'SDSSU is a new member of FIMFS', 'sdssu-is-a-new-member-of-fimfs', '<p>FIMFS is an organization that had metamorphosed into a 25-member institution from the original five chartered members in 1968. The Surigao del Sur State University (SDSSU) is the new Institutional member this year in the consortium.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">FIMFS is an organization that had metamorphosed into a 25-member institution from the original five chartered members in 1968. The Surigao del Sur State University (SDSSU) is the new Institutional member this year in the consortium. Dr. Bernardita G. Quevedo, Asst. Campus Director and Mr. Fabio C. Ruaza, Research Head of Lianga Campus, received the plaque of membership at the Southern Leyte State University, Sogod Leyte. Also, the main requirement of the consortium is to present papers (new ideas and concepts in the field of marine sciences) every year, thus, Mr. Ruaza presented his paper entitled &ldquo;Shell Microstructures of the Spondylid Species (Bivalvia: Spondylidae): Do They Have Systematic Implications?&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Composed of public and private institutions of higher learning in the Philippines that are involved in marine and freshwater sciences, the federation is committed in bringing closer partnership among institutional and individual members. The collegial sharing of research outputs, facilities, resources and expertise is central in its quest for a true partnership.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The FIMFS annual scientific convention is one of its major activities hosted in turns by institution members. The convention serves as a venue for exchange and updating of research outputs, as well as a platform for mentoring young budding scientists.</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Fabio C. Ruaza', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-02-11 19:17:29', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-7ff0-43fb-8ac9-30f75e4ea103', 'R&amp;D Tandag holds Prior Art Searching', 'rampd-tandag-holds-prior-art-searching', '<p>As a preliminary phase to apply for a patent grant, the Research and Development office particularly the Innovation and Technology Support Office (ITSO) of the University hosted a Two-Day Workshop on Prior Art Searching last October 17-18, 2019 at HRM, Building, SDSSU, Tandag City.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">As a preliminary phase to apply for a patent grant, the Research and Development office particularly the Innovation and Technology Support Office (ITSO) of the University hosted a Two-Day Workshop on Prior Art Searching last October 17-18, 2019 at HRM, Building, SDSSU, Tandag City.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The main objective of this activity is to help the faculty to determine the originality of their invention and help them produce a better-quality patent draft. The activity was participated by the faculty researchers of the different colleges identified by the program research coordinators for they have the potential technology to be patented.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">It started with a short program and workshop proper follows. Colleagues who have attended the previous trainings were invited as resource speakers for this activity. On the last day, presentation and critiquing of outputs were done. Certificate of completion were given to the participants and outputs were collected by the R and D.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"R&amp;D Tandag holds Prior Art Searching\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/73161619_388790685343007_3377709302599909376_n.jpg\" /></span></span></p>', '72489422_524204031473982_6969882243732865024_n.jpg', 'Jennilyn Doloriel', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-02-11 19:40:20', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-83cd-43ed-92bf-5e047182f6ca', 'SDSSU, Department of Agriculture, the Farmers, and the Crops in a Field Day', 'sdssu-department-of-agriculture-the-farmers-and-the-crops-in-a-field-day', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">On October 11, 2019, 57 participants attended the Field Day conducted at SDSSU-San Miguel Campus with collaboration with the Department of Agriculture Regional and Provincial Office. Farmers from San Miguel and Mr. Elmer E. Enicola the Program leader of the ongoing Soybeans project of DOST-PCAARRD also attended the said event. As part of the activity, the participants had a tour where the crops were planted mainly consist of Soybeans, Corn, Sorghum, Peanuts which is part of the Soybeans Project to maintain and improve soil fertility by planting multiple crops. The farm was managed by Mr. Achilles L. Belarmino who is also the project study leader of Component 2 of Soybeans Project, with the helped of the Farmer Scientist of the project.&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">On October 11, 2019, 57 participants attended the Field Day conducted at SDSSU-San Miguel Campus with collaboration with the Department of Agriculture Regional and Provincial Office. Farmers from San Miguel and Mr. Elmer E. Enicola the Program leader of the ongoing Soybeans project of DOST-PCAARRD also attended the said event. As part of the activity, the participants had a tour where the crops were planted mainly consist of Soybeans, Corn, Sorghum, Peanuts which is part of the Soybeans Project to maintain and improve soil fertility by planting multiple crops. The farm was managed by Mr. Achilles L. Belarmino who is also the project study leader of Component 2 of Soybeans Project, with the helped of the Farmer Scientist of the project.&nbsp;</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Kathleen D. Pame', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-02-11 19:45:27', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-87b8-45b5-a0c0-582ae48d8daa', 'Inception Meeting of the Soybeans project with the DOST-PCAARRD', 'inception-meeting-of-the-soybeans-project-with-the-dost-pcaarrd', '<p>Representatives from DOST-PCAARRD headed by Mr. Rolando S. Corpuz arrived at the New Boardroom of SDSSU-Main Campus for the Inception meeting. Representatives from LGU Agriculture offices from Tandag City and municipalities of Tago and San Miguel also were present on the inception meeting.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong>&ldquo;Let&rsquo;s have our confidence in Soybeans&rdquo; DOST-PCAARRD representative said in an encouraging voice. An inception meeting was conducted on October 18, 2019 at the New Boardroom to lay the boards of the Soybeans Project as it is the pioneering collaboration with the Agency and SDSSU.&rdquo;</strong></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Representatives from DOST-PCAARRD headed by Mr. Rolando S. Corpuz arrived at the New Boardroom of SDSSU-Main Campus for the Inception meeting. Representatives from LGU Agriculture offices from Tandag City and municipalities of Tago and San Miguel also were present on the inception meeting. Tandag City, Tago, and San Miguel were the project sites of the research project. AS the OIC of the President of the University, Mr. Nemesio Loayon opened the meeting with a warm welcome, followed by introduction of the participants and their positions.&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mr. Elmer E. Enicola the Program leader of &ldquo;Improvement of Soybeans (Glycine max [L.]. Merr.) for better Nutrition, Higher Income, and Enhanced Soil Health&rdquo; under the DOST-PCAARRD presented the overview of the project. He encouraged the people present to have confidence in Soybeans. He also discussed the current status of Filipinos relating to Soybeans, problems such as the low consumption of Soybeans and the preference of Filipinos for imported Soybeans. He also expressed his desire to make the Surigao del Sur&rsquo;s Soybean to improve into a value chain from just being a supply chain. He mentioned that the main problem is that the farmers themselves does not consume their produce and sold all of it in the buyers not even leaving seeds for planting. &nbsp;Though similar in many aspects, he differentiated the role of Department of Agriculture and the DOST-PCAARRD in the project. Lastly, he mentioned his desire that many more people to plant this crop and hoped for a higher income through this.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Then the project leader of SDSSU, Ma&rsquo;am Jocelyn B. Panduyos presented the project 5: Improvement of Soybean in Surigao del Sur Through Enhanced Value Chains,&nbsp;Sustainable Seed Sector, and Better Varieties Under Different Cropping System&rdquo;. &nbsp;The project has 2 components: Ma&rsquo;am Jocelyn led the component 1 while Mr. Achilles Belarmino focuses on component 2. She presented the beneficiaries and expected output of the study. Mr. Enicola was active in supporting every step of the plan.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">PCAARRD Grants-in-Aid Guidelines was then presented. Mr. Rolando S. Corpuz, the Senior SRS of CRD-PCAARRD presented the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) Report Requirements while Mr. Ireneo B. Palma, SRS I of CRD-PCAARRD presented the &ldquo;Fund Release and Financial Reporting&rdquo;. The complications about the state of the project in Surigao del Sur was tackled. The fund for the project was 5 months delay that caused the slowing down of the progress of the project especially the component 1 in the area. The PCAARRD representative applauded the SDSSU team for the progress even with the lack of funds. Mr. Corpuz mentioned that the any teams could request for extension however, additional budget could not be given. Ma&rsquo;am Leorelie Kim Dahan then had a discussion with the PCAARRD representatives. This is the first externally funded research project in SDSSU funded by DOST; some matters specially to relating budget was discussed. The group exchanged ideas about the expected output of the project. In the afternoon, the attendees had a tour of the Soybean field in SDSSU-San Miguel were the component 2 of the project was cantered.&nbsp;</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Kathleen D. Pame', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-02-11 19:55:54', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-8bc6-45b1-bfba-482036200aa2', 'Research and Development -The Innovation Technology Support Office (ITSO)', 'research-and-development-the-innovation-technology-support-office-itso', '<p>Innovation Technology Support Office (ITSO) initiated the conduct of a 5-day Intellectual Property Workshop last September 20-24, 2019 at the second floor HRM Bldg. Function Hall.&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Innovation Technology Support Office (ITSO) initiated the conduct of a 5-day Intellectual Property Workshop last September 20-24, 2019 at the second floor HRM Bldg. Function Hall.&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">It was participated by 30 faculty members across campuses. There were three (3) lecturers coming from the Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) who enlightened the participants on the different topics such as; The imperatives of the Innovation Hubs in the Industrial Revolution 4.0, &nbsp; ITSO : from inception to a network of Innovation , Trademarks, Patents , Utility Models and Industrial Designs, Patent Search, Technology Transfer in the Philippines &nbsp;and Technology Commercialization in the Philippines. While the workshop includes Saturdays and Sundays in order to maximize the time of the participants and the lecturers too; indeed It was very fruitful 5-day workshop yet it was a tedious especially that it was highlighted with the presentation of the patent search documents gathered from the different data base systems using the keywords and other techniques in patent search.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Another activity conducted by the ITSO was the Revision of the Intellectual Property Manual held at Bugsay Beach Resort on October 23 to 25. The output of the IP manual revision was reviewed by the Assistant Chief of the Technology Transfer Innovation Bureau of the IPOPHL. This will be presented to the 4rth quarter Academic Council meeting.&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The Third activity conducted by the office of the ITSO was the Patent Drafting and Filing held last Nov 4 to 8, 2019 at the Grand Monique Lodge in Tandag City. With the substantial inputs of the lecturers from the Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines, the participants successfully filed for Patents Online on their Potential Technology. &nbsp;There were 20 applications for Patents and 1 (one) industrial design and there are still coming applications to be reviewed and hoping for additional filing to the Bureau of Patents.&nbsp;</span></span></p>', 'picture one.jpg', 'Luzminda Baquial', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-02-11 20:04:05', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-8fe8-4159-beaf-131e17a1d0b7', 'Pandemic Response Update as of April 06-24, 2020', 'pandemic-response-update-as-of-april-06-24-2020', '<p>COVID-19 has an indefinite timeline, but SDSSU continues to commit itself to join the Nation in its mitigating efforts to address the social and economic impact brought by such pandemic.</p>', '', '95142452_671723986725316_7780335653295751168_n.png', 'Executive Affairs', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-05-03 00:12:57', '2023-02-14 03:49:11', '2023-02-14 03:49:11'),
('987727bc-9466-48fa-a0de-a1127c51e6f0', 'Weekly Status Report for Pandemic Response', 'weekly-status-report-for-pandemic-response', '<p>Weekly status report for pandemic response as of April 20-24, 2020</p>', '<p><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=1QYtcDl4vH-3ZAGKSgrdXAjvkvPhjEd4K\" /></p>', 'Weekly Status Report (As of Apr 20-24)_FrontPage.png', 'Executive Affairs', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-05-03 00:29:33', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-987c-4ca4-9488-fbcc0d0c4318', 'Pandemic Response Update as of April 27-30, 2020', 'pandemic-response-update-as-of-april-27-30-2020', '<p>Pandemic Response Update April 27-30, 2020.</p>', '<p><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=1QYYFfriam-qU8p0g3p9n1d70F5ziGWgL\" /></p>', 'Weekly Status Update (As of Apr 27-30) (1).png', 'Executive Affairs', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-05-03 01:03:08', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-9bbb-4b91-8f5a-9a2125adbf5b', 'List Of Newly Hired And Promoted For Non-Teaching Positions', 'list-of-newly-hired-and-promoted-for-non-teaching-positions', '<p>List Of Newly Hired And Promoted For Non-Teaching Positions</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ds15InW1EqpGNdj8d92ZbMwK4sZZBOCv/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', '122630079_687191662200692_7101783417317598447_n.jpg', 'HR Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-10-27 13:28:04', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-9d9a-41c6-b6d6-a6f3d2812886', 'Commission on Higher Education Issued to College of Arts and Sciences Certificate of Program Compliance', 'commission-on-higher-education-issued-to-college-of-arts-and-sciences-certificate-of-program-compliance', '<p>Congratulation to the College of Arts and Sciences for the Certificate of Program Compliance issued by the Commision on Higher Education for the following Programs.</p>', '<p>Congratulation to the College of Arts and Sciences for the Certificate of Program Compliance issued by the Commision on Higher Education for the following Programs.</p>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Arts in Economics</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Arts in English Language</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Arts in Political Science</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div>\n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Public Administration</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div>\n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Batsilyer ng Sining sa Filipino</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div>\n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Science in Biology</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div>\n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Bachelor of Science in Environmental Science</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tandag Campus</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Effective AY 2020-2021</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          \n          <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </div>\n          </div>\n          </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"800px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17A-XcRwGioFFyPuwntKi6e-8dNY56DTk/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', NULL, 'College of Arts and Sciences', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-11-03 14:20:38', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-9fae-4069-8669-1b1facc3527c', 'Posting for the Ratification of the Collective Negotiation Agreement (CNA) for 2021-2023', 'posting-for-the-ratification-of-the-collective-negotiation-agreement-cna-for-2021-2023', '<p>Posting for the Ratification of the Collective Negotiation Agreement (CNA) for 2021-2023</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"800px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NDsI_gUOT2oYBvployZ1aigqAutDc-4m/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', NULL, 'SDSSU Faculty Union', NULL, 'news', 1, '2020-12-09 15:46:55', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-a210-4f85-9f1d-19ca9a802204', 'SDSSU Extends Assistance During the Devastation of Auring', 'sdssu-extends-assistance-during-the-devastation-of-auring', '<p>Tandag City and its neighboring municipalities met a devastating plight when Tropical Depression Auring veered in these areas. Bringing with it strong winds and heavy rains, many areas were submerged into turbid water and quickly left many families displaced in the morning of February 21, 2022.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Tandag City and its neighboring municipalities met a devastating plight when Tropical Depression Auring veered in these areas. Bringing with it strong winds and heavy rains, many areas were submerged into turbid water and quickly left many families displaced in the morning of February 21, 2022. Dr. Baceledes R. Estal responded immediately to the call of the LGUs for a prompt assistance as he instructed all the Campus Directors to identify designated areas in the Campuses for the evacuated families as their refuge amidst the torments brought by Auring. A salient part of his marching order to the Vice Presidents, Campus Directors, Extension Director, DRR Focal Person, together with all the Key Officials is to extend food aids and other forms of support to the evacuees as part of the emergency response of SDSSU.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Through the concerted efforts of the Key Officials, masks, food assistance, and an overnight shelter were extended to the affected families meeting their most urgent needs. Further, distribution of food packs was also extended to the identified Barangays after Auring left the grounds of Surigao del Sur. &nbsp;Indeed, SDSSU has stood up to its core values&hellip;. SDSSU CARES.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <div class=\"row\">\n          <div class=\"col-md-6 col-xs-6\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/152414566_2866621403581762_6711090639123252036_n.jpg\" /></div>\n          \n          <div class=\"col-md-6 col-xs-6\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/151118558_1163933110722347_764742102959634261_n.jpg\" /></div>\n          </div>', '151263297_3790265924394236_8939076059570283111_n.jpg', 'Executive Affairs', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-02-24 08:52:08', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-a9ae-48f7-be66-7057e612336e', 'SDSSU College of Law Finishes First Full Year Online', 'sdssu-college-of-law-finishes-first-full-year-online', '<p>SDSSU College of Law Finishes First Full Year Online</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"900px\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hx6B3Z2XV4x_cqKScDUZayKOEwGW5oW1/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', 'Screenshot_2.png', 'College of Law', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-08-20 12:34:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-ac75-4af5-832b-222694235c97', 'President\'s Message for Accreditation', 'presidents-message-for-accreditation', '<p>President&#39;s Message for Accreditation</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;At the onset, I would like to express my gratefulness to the men and women of Surigao del Sur State University; starting with the Vice President for Administration and Finance, Dr. Florfie O. Urbiztondo, and the Vice President for Academic Affairs, Dr. Ramel D. Tomaquin, the Campus Director of Tandag Campus, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the Deans, other key Officials, faculty, and staff for your concerted efforts even during the midst of the pandemic in preparation of this quality assurance evaluation. It only goes to show that despite the extraordinary times, we at the Surigao del Sur State University which will be known as North Eastern Mindanao State University, are true to our commitment to provide our major stakeholders, the students, education at its best. We can only do such by proactively maintaining and submitting our programs to program evaluation to ensure that we meet the standards for quality education.&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; To the AACCUP team for this survey visit led by its Coordinator, Dr. Riceli Mendoza of USM and the rest of the team to name, we have with us, Dr. Gladys G. Rosales , Dr. Dariel A. Palmiano, both from CBSUA, Dr. Nino B. Corpuz (TSU), Dr. Evelyn S. Angwian (BengSU), Dr. Freddie P. Masuli (CagSU), Dr. Julius T. CApili (CagSU),, Dr. Elsie P. Sandueta (JRMSU), Dr. Estela A. Sescon (JRMSU), Dr. Lita B. Sopsop (WPU), please accept our gratitude and appreciation for your time and for journeying with us in our quest for excellence. Please extend also the same gratitude to AACCUP through its Executive Director, Dr. Milabel Ho because despite the challenges of the Pandemic, these quality assurance efforts is still ardently pursued.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Accreditation indeed has brought this community together through cooperation, determination and, hard work because of our desire to advance growth and progress through academic excellence. We are firmly anchored in our Vision, Mission and Core Values to offer outstanding academic programs and worthwhile academic experience for our students. Our faculty members are all dedicated to walk with our students in the various phases of their college life and assisting them in order for our students to attain the highest level of achievement within and outside the walls of SDSSU. Thus, we really take this survey visit seriously and by heart because we believe that this can serve as a scaffold as we move forward towards making this University as a premier leading University in this side of the country and continue to produce the best minds who will soon shape the future of the countryside and the nation as a whole. </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I encourage everyone to keep your momentum and be optimistic as we hurdle the challenges of accreditation because through our strong collaboration and dedication, this shall become our legacy, forming part of the many milestones of SDSSU towards paving a path for our youth and empowering them in their journey to self-actualization. Again, I welcome our proactive and devoted Accreditors, rest assured that our counter parts are more than willing and enthusiastic in working with you as we traverse this weeklong survey visit. To the working committees, focal persons, and everyone behind this toil, you have the administration&rsquo;s full support and so in advance, thank you and congratulations to all of us for our best efforts! May the good Lord bless the intentions of this endeavor. <strong>&nbsp;I love you all!</strong></span></span></span></p>', 'President-message_AACCUP.jpg', 'DR. BACELEDES R. ESTAL', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-08-24 02:36:03', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-b263-4c8c-93f8-109afae05037', 'AACCUP Online Accreditation Survey Visit 2021', 'aaccup-online-accreditation-survey-visit-2021', '<p>AACCUP Online Accreditation Survey Visit 2021</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Surigao del Sur State University formally opened the AACUUP Accreditation Visit 2021 on August 23, 2021. The University determines itself in providing quality education in adherence to the standards set by its partner agency. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The AACCUP Accreditation has always been taking its part as one of the pillars of the University. Intending to amplify the academic services provided by the institution, experts and scholars have gathered to assess and evaluate the strengths and areas of improvement of the identified programs.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/AACCUP_Heads.jpg\" /></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;AACCUP Accreditors led by Dr. Riceli C. Mendoza gratefully received SDSSU&rsquo;s warmest welcome for the University president Dr. Baceledes R. Estal, and Campus Director Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon fronted the successful opening program.&nbsp; The said accreditation visit is scheduled for August 23 and is stretched until the 27th assessing seven programs of SDSSU-Tandag campus. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The Director of Quality Assurance, Dr. Rebecca Sanchez, and the &nbsp;Quality Assurance Head-Tandag Campus, Dr. Razil M. Gumanoy, were in high hopes that the Local Task Force Counterparts&rsquo; efforts will be put into fruition with the best efforts of the entire SDSSU community for the benefit of its students and stakeholders. </span></span></p>', 'Big.JPG', 'Mr. Steven Carl M. Silagan', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-08-25 01:46:56', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-b4b5-4711-9b93-8908916acb0a', 'Celebrating the 121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary', 'celebrating-the-121st-philippine-civil-service-anniversary', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Celebrating the 121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary. SDSSU/NEMSU conducts simultaneous Flag Raising Ceremony and Renewal of Oath participated by 7 satellite campuses.</span></span></p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Celebrating the 121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary. SDSSU/NEMSU conducts simultaneous Flag Raising Ceremony and Renewal of Oath participated by 7 satellite campuses.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Mabuhay ang mga Lingkod Bayani!</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/hashtag/pcsa2021?__eep__=6&amp;__cft__[0]=AZVkW3MMTvacxrmRZo_lySddyxYmBxyk7KEK6WNfb_0Rjik4NZFD09_MfBTQdXuvMByMGwmfaCoGP94DK9c75adDsRomeM74q89F_jp1IwqwA4hhNOEX6qCTl3evj7RT7JUNspQLMgnZQYmYhpNiUEwe&amp;__tn__=*NK-R\" tabindex=\"0\">#PCSA2021</a></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/psca2021.jpg\" /></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Message for 121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary</span></strong></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Dr. Baceledes R.Estal</span></strong></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;At the onset, I would like to greet each public servant of Surigao del Sur State University a HAPPY 121st Philippine Civil Service AnniversaryThis year&rsquo;s theme speaks of &ldquo;Transforming Public Service in the next Decade Honing Agile and Future-Ready Servants Heroes.&rdquo;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;As the great Mahatma Ghandi said that the best way to lose ourselves is to find ourselves in the service of others. This year&rsquo;s celebration is special because each of you, the administrators, faculty, and staff has gone the extra mile due to the pandemic that has challenged our operations due to the limitations of face to face transactions. Hence, our theme speaks of your efforts to be swift, active, and innovative despite the trials that threaten to derail us. Indeed, being a public servant gives us the platform to serve our stakeholders, and we have that oath that no matter what comes our way, we have to serve the community with dignity, integrity, enthusiasm, passion, and sustained vision.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I thank you all because even with the current situation that puts us into so much limitations, as public servants, you took the task at hand with extraordinary sacrifices and ardent devotion so that our students will still have the quality education they deserve even if modalities of teaching and other services have abruptly changed.&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Nobody knows how long this phase of virus coexistence will persist. The world after lockdown, on the other hand, is a very different place. Our stakeholders are counting on us to lead them through the months, if not years, of uncertainty ahead. In this unpredictable times, we&#39;ve had to increase our flexibility and adaptability in order to provide great outcomes for both external and internal stakeholders. In this unprecedented time, I applaud your efforts and encourage you to stay loyal to your mission as public servants. Though times have become exhausting and quite demanding, always consider to bring innovation into your workplace &ndash; no matter what your work is whether an administrator, professor, instructor, or a support staff. Stay focus on your tasks know what they are and get them done with a spirit of excellence and zeal.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Many changes in the academic community were accelerated by the pandemic. While it has a negative influence, our adaptability and future-ready talents are indicators of beneficial results. You can build on this momentum. Meeting the needs of our clienteles means harnessing the power of transformative responses to make a lasting difference in the community. Most of all, as public servants, we have to proactively be supportive of each other, because in our togetherness, there are so many things we can attain and overcome, but in our division, there will be little that we can accomplish.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Today as we renew our oath as public servants, let us be inspired by the words of the famous British prime minister, Sir&nbsp;Winston&nbsp;Churchill, we make a living by what we get, but we make a life by what we give. With this, I say, with whatever opportunity we have as public servants, let us work with a happy heart, do the job well, commit and devote ourselves to service despite deploring adversities.&nbsp; This will be our permanent tribute to SDSSU/NEMSU and all its stakeholders. Mabuhay tayong mga Lingkod Bayan! Mabuhay ang SDSSU!</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>', 'PCSA 2021 web slider copy.JPG', 'SDSSU', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-09-06 08:57:57', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-b792-4ce7-9daa-ea5ee8ed71c9', 'The President\'s Report', 'the-presidents-report', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">The President&#39;s Report</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><strong>2nd Quarter Regular Board Meeting FY 2021</strong></span></span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">To the august members of the Board of Regents and to our Chair, the Honorable Commissioner Perfecto Alibin, Representative and Chairman for the House Committee on Higher Technical Education, Deputy Speaker, Congressman, Prospero A. Pichay, Jr. Representative, Chairman on Senate Committee on Senate Committee on Education, Arts and Culture, Atty. Luke Sartorio, NEDA Regional Director Priscilla R. Sonido, DOST OIC Regional Director, Engr. Andrea J. Cabonita, President of the Federation of Faculty Club Association, Dr. Floresito D. Calub, President of the Alumni Associations, Dr. Ponciano G. Alngog, Private Sector Representative, Sir Alan A. Pelenio and President, Federation of the Supreme Student Government, Mr. Edgar Anthony Siman, The Board Secretary, Ma&rsquo;am Catherine F. Salomon, key Officials and resource persons joining us in this 2<sup>nd</sup> Quarter FY 2021 Regular Board Meeting please accept my felicitations and respect. At the onset, allow me to express to everyone that indeed, it has been a pleasure to be working closely with you in the realization of the Vision and Mission of Surigao del Sur State University, and as we traverse the forthcoming years under a new identity, we still, uphold the same CORE values serving multitude of our stakeholders.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p>&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CQbAX-mLiI0\" style=\"width:100%; height:350px;\"></iframe></p>', 'The President.jpg', 'Dr. Baceledes R. Estal', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-09-14 06:53:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-ba9e-4044-bd9b-02d3830dd1ae', 'AACCUP', 'aaccup', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><strong>AACCUP</strong></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Online Accreditation Survey Visit 2021</span></span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Surigao del Sur State University (SDSSU)-Lianga Campus joined the opening of the AACUP Online Accreditation Survey Visit &ndash; Level II for the Bachelor of Science in Computer Science (BSCS) Program yesterday, September 13, 2021. The activity aims to make possible for an evaluated program to know its strength and weaknesses, and in what aspects it needs to develop and to submit to quality standards and remit efforts to maintain them at high level in the delivery of continuous education and service amid the threat of the pandemic. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">To show his overflowing support, the opening program was actively participated by Dr. Baceledes R. Estal, further giving an inspiring message to the local counterparts recognizing their efforts to this institution&rsquo;s feat. The program was formally opened by Lianga&rsquo;s campus director, Dr. Cynthia P. Sajot who also showed his commitment to the said activity as one of the requirements in achieving excellence as an institution. The accreditors, headed by Dr. Ronnie N. Parica, together with Dr. Hershey Alburo even commended the institution as a whole for still submitting for an accreditation amid the many constraints. Other participants were the local counterparts headed by the Head of the Office of Quality Assurance, Dr. Faith P. Villanueva and Asst. Campus Director, Dr. Bernardita G. Quevedo, who also made the honor to formally close the first part of the five-day activity. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">For now, it is the fervent prayer of the BSCS faculty and staff to hear that great news at the end of the week that will be celebrated by the whole university. It is also the institutions anticipations for the accreditors to be happily-working with SDSSU-Lianga while supplementing the campus to be fully equipped with the standards set for a Level II-Accredited Program. Moreover, the institution is beyond grateful for the opportunity to submit despite the circumstances and hindrances brought by the present situation. Soar high, SDSSU-Lianga! </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Pictorials.JPG\" /></span></span></p>', 'Lianga_Banner copy.jpg', 'Dr. Cynthia P. Sajot', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-09-14 08:47:19', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-bdbc-463d-a001-4b4fff2dec81', '121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary Kick off', '121st-philippine-civil-service-anniversary-kick-off', '<p>121st Philippine Civil Service Anniversary Kick off</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"900px\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lL_4anA_IYJ-z0ReetJPxyDntSfcqYLB/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', 'Canrtilan banner.JPG', 'Dr. Juancho A. Intano', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-10-28 04:17:47', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('987727bc-c925-40cf-9cac-ace461049cc2', 'College of Law Celebrates First Anniversary on Law Week', 'college-of-law-celebrates-first-anniversary-on-law-week', '', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Surigao del Sur State University&rsquo;s (SDSSU) College of Law recently celebrated its one-year anniversary of its inception during the Philippine National Law Week last September 20-24, 2021. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The College of Law conducted a week-long series of activities to honor its founding, which included online legal consultations, a virtual acquaintance and fellowship party, a motorcade in Tandag City, and a video conference on a field guide to law school with YouTube animated law personality &ldquo;Lex In Motion&rdquo; as the keynote speaker.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The events saw the induction of the College&rsquo;s first law student practitioners during the week as it prepared for the unveiling of its Legal Aid Clinic pursuant to the Legal Education Board (LEB) Resolution No. 2015-08 which authorizes its establishment. Ten (10) students from the Pioneering batch took their oath before Executive Judge, Hon. Edwin M. Malazarte, of the Regional Trial Court Branch 27, Tandag City, Surigao del Sur, as the first law student practitioners of the SDSSU&rsquo;s College of Law. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/public_files/images/Banner2.JPG\" class=\"img img-responsive\" /></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The celebration coincided with the annual commemoration of the Philippine National Law Week and National Law Day. Presidential Proclamation No. 640, series of 1995, states that the third week of September every year is declared as the Philippine National Law Week. Furthermore, Presidential Proclamation No. 1477, series of 1975, declared September 19 of every year as Law Day.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The LEB stressed that this year&rsquo;s celebration of law day is a reminder of the enduring importance of the rule of law in promoting justice and progress for national recovery. LEB further stated that this year&rsquo;s celebration of law week would &ldquo;serve to remind the legal education community and the broader Philippine nation of the centrality of the rule of law during these changing times.&rdquo;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; In the same week, the College introduced its newest batch, the Cratus. The Cratus is the third batch of law students the College has admitted in only its first year operations following the Pioneers (1<sup>st</sup> batch) and Perseveros (2<sup>nd</sup> batch). </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp; College of Law Dean Atty. Daniel Diaz last August said that SDSSU were commended by other law schools for having an abundance of enrollees despite the pandemic.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &ldquo;It&rsquo;s very fulfilling because despite the struggles we finished a full academic year and that we got to create three sections. I&rsquo;ve heard comments from other law schools that we have an abundance of enrollees. Overall it was not a bad start for a law school,&rdquo; the Dean said.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; He also specified that the possibility of a blended form of in-person and online classes might be imaginable for the next semester as the cases and transmission of COVID-19 are slowly decreasing and the rate of vaccinations have increased.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The SDSSU College of Law is still looking for new enrollees for the next semester A.Y. 2022-2023 beginning in January next year. </span></span></p>', 'Banner.jpg', 'ATTY. DANIEL DIAZ', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-11-03 08:36:25', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-cbd2-4cd1-9af4-68c7bc1790da', 'The Farm Builders', 'the-farm-builders', '<p><strong>NEMSU - SAN MIGUEL CAMPUS</strong></p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"900px\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Joe5GeYmmVVo0m9xBFPlTm67Vh365Uk_/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', 'SM banner.jpg', 'Dr. Clemencia Sumagaysay', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-11-12 01:28:18', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-ce42-4c58-9289-d52e57ed7cec', 'SDSSU-Tagbina hosts NCAFF 2021', 'sdssu-tagbina-hosts-ncaff-2021', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><strong><em><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Confab showcases 91 studies around the Philippines</span></span></em></strong></span></span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">November 4, 2021 marked another triumphant feat for Surigao Del Sur State University-Tagbina Campus (SDSSU-TC) as it hosted the two-day National Conference on Agriculture, Forestry, &amp; Fisheries (NCAFF) 2021. Spearheaded by the SDSSU-Tagbina Campus&rsquo; Research Office, the NCAFF covered a span of two days&mdash;commencing on November 4, 2021 and concluding on the following day, November 5, 2021.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Over 100 participants attended the national conference via Zoom platform. The two-day affair opened with a video presentation that showcased the renowned tourist spots surrounding Surigao Del Sur. A message from the University President, Dr. Baceledes R. Estal, followed.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&ldquo;As a result of SDSSU&rsquo;s initiatives, the Institution has continuously expanded its capabilities over the years. This in turn has fostered a strong research climate aimed at producing high-valued innovative research to improve the University operation, create solutions to the challenges that beset the community and respond to emerging opportunities for continued improvement,&rdquo; Dr. Estal said.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">He also hoped that the conference will jumpstart more research-pertinent endeavors in the future as part of the university&rsquo;s four-fold functions.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&ldquo;Our participation and genuine engagement for the realization of this mission is a mark of our enduring commitment to quality education, to true academic stewardship and as our permanent tribute for nation building as North Eastern Mindanao State University,&rdquo; he added.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Subsequently, the plenary session took off. The Plenary Speaker, Dr. Leslie T. Ubaub, delineated the current learning conditions in the University of the South Pacific in Apia, Samoa, where she&rsquo;s currently affiliated with, as well as their interventions to address the constraints brought about by COVID-19. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">The breakout sessions followed the plenary session in Day 1. It consisted of four parallel sessions: <strong>Agriculture Track 1, Agriculture Track 2, Forestry Track, &amp; the Fisheries Track</strong>. At the onset, the moderators from every parallel session introduced the two main awards that the research presenters may receive: <strong><em>Best Paper Award </em></strong><em>and<strong> Best Oral Presentation Award. </strong></em></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Regarding the number of gathered research presentations, altogether, the conference raked in a total of 91 research studies from all three academic areas: Agriculture Tracks 1&amp;2 elicited 52 researches; the Forestry Track received 17 studies; and the Fisheries track obtained a total number of 22 research papers. A number of evaluators also critiqued the acquired research studies and presentations: four evaluators for the Agricultural Tracks; three evaluators for the Forestry track; and another three evaluators for the Fisheries Track.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">For Day 1, the research critics evaluated 30 research studies from the Agricultural Tracks; 17 research studies from the Forestry Track; and 12 studies from the Fisheries Track. The aforementioned activities comprised all the activities in Day 1.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">The second day of the national conference opened with a replay of the above-mentioned showcase of Surigao Del Sur&rsquo;s famous tourist spots. What came next was the Plenary Session of Dr. Filipina B. Sotto, a professor of the Department of Biology of Cebu Normal University. Dr. Sotto&rsquo;s discussion focused on the impacts of Aquaculture. Specifically, Fisheries, on the facet of Food Security in the country.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Another series of research papers followed the Plenary Session. For Day 2, the evaluators from all three areas evaluated a total number of 22 research studies from the two Agricultural tracks, five research studies from the Forestry track, and 10 papers from the Fisheries track. The proclamation of winners concluded the two-day national conference.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">For the &ldquo;Best Paper Award&rdquo;, the following presenters ranked first in each area: <strong>Agricultural Track</strong>&mdash;the collaborative work of Mr. John G. Ponteras from the Southern Philippines Agri-Business and Marine &amp; Aquatic School of Technology, and Mr. Ulyssses P. Besas from the University of Southeastern Philippines; <strong>Fisheries Track</strong>&mdash;Mr. Leofred C. Velasco from Nueva Vizcaya State University; and <strong>Forestry Track</strong>&mdash;the collaborative work of Ms. Nenita M. Tolentino from Ramon National High School, Marlon U. Saludarez from Western Philippines University, and Mr. Jason Arnold L. Maslang from Saint Mary&rsquo;s University.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">NCAFF 2021 served as a festival of academic exchange, and as a stepping stone for Surigao Del Sur State University-Tagbina Campus&rsquo; undertakings to better serve its clientele, uphold one of its four-fold functions, which is Research, and keep itself abreast with international standards.</span></span></p>', 'NCAFF.jpg', '', NULL, 'news', 1, '2021-11-17 05:09:25', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-d220-4b2e-a14d-69ec8ab3b903', 'SDSSU CANTILAN LIBRARY SERVICES IN NEW NORMAL', 'sdssu-cantilan-library-services-in-new-normal', '<p>COVID-19 has presented an enormous challenge to libraries and librarians. The stress on policies and work habits began during the initial spread of the virus, when most libraries remained open, some with restrictions. These libraries had to figure out<br />\n          how to enforce social-distancing policies in a space that is open to everyone and used to trying to get people through the doors, not keep them at a distance.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">COVID-19 has presented an enormous challenge to libraries and librarians. The stress on policies and work habits began during the initial spread of the virus, when most libraries remained open, some with restrictions. These libraries had to figure out how to enforce social-distancing policies in a space that is open to everyone and used to trying to get people through the doors, not keep them at a distance. Then, as many libraries closed, the challenge grew: how to maintain as many programs and services as possible while in quarantine, and that were for the fortunate staff who work in libraries that did close. Many stayed open much longer than advisable or have re-opened for curbside checkout too soon, putting both their patrons and their staff at risk.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Hence, the Surigao del Sur State University Cantilan Campus Library promotes remote services that will help students and faculty of institution in their needed information.&nbsp;There are 3 online library services offered;</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <ol>\n              <li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Library Reference Assistance (Atheneum), the updated fb account manages by the library staff in answer queries. Students and faculty may we also reach us through </span></span><a href=\"mailto:cantilanlibrary@sdssu.edu.ph\" style=\"color:blue; text-decoration:underline\"><span style=\"background-color:white\">cantilanlibrary@sdssu.edu.ph</span></a><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">.</span></span></span></span></li>\n              <li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Request for Online Document Delivery Service- this is provided for SDSSU Cantilan Library Users only, this process&nbsp; articles and books chapters request from journals, books, e-resources and other library materials available, under this service are photocopying&nbsp; services for walk in clients and scanning&nbsp; of materials&nbsp; to be sent through fb messenger or email address.</span></span></span></span></li>\n              <li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Online E-Book Request, there are two ways to access e books, seek assistance from the Reference Librarian or you may send request to </span></span><a href=\"mailto:cantilanlibrary@sdssu.edu.ph\" style=\"color:blue; text-decoration:underline\"><span style=\"background-color:white\">cantilanlibrary@sdssu.edu.ph</span></a><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">. </span></span></span></span></li>\n              <li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Access to Electronic Resources/ Databases- you can visit our library website </span></span><a href=\"https://www.sdssu.edu.ph\" style=\"color:blue; text-decoration:underline\"><span style=\"background-color:white\">https://www.sdssu.edu.ph</span></a><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">, or our IP address 222.127.147.194:8081 to browse and access the free and available databases.</span></span></span></span></li>\n              <li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">SDSSU&nbsp; Digital Library</span></span></span></span></li>\n          </ol>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">And now our new library services the Digital Library powered by ODILO! This format opens for you the &ldquo;Netflix&rdquo;, of multi-format content and unlimited learning resources. We encourage everyone to make the most of your learning experience with ODILO Digital Library access.</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Enjoy online access wherever you are and anytime you want. Be Safe and God Bless Everyone.</span></span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Maryflor B. Estal', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 09:48:31', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-d7bc-4789-afa4-0bce66fe6ed0', 'SDSSU Libraries Adopts a Work-From-Home Arrangement', 'sdssu-libraries-adopts-a-work-from-home-arrangement', '<p>When the coronavirus (COVID-19) was officially categorized by the World Health Organization (WHO) as a pandemic, many countries including the Philippines has declared a travel ban to stop the spread of the virus.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">When the coronavirus (COVID-19) was officially categorized by the World Health Organization (WHO) as a pandemic, many countries including the Philippines has declared a travel ban to stop the spread of the virus. Public transportation is no longer allowed to limit the movement of the people. Mass gatherings are also prohibited.&nbsp; All schools in all level are ordered to suspend classes and so with other school activities. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">To ensure that school operations continue during ECQ, the Department of Labor and Employement (DOLE) issues an Advisory No. 9 series of 2020, (COVID-19 Flexi Work Advisory) encouraging to adopt a Work-From-Home scheme.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">In compliance with the said advisory, the university president Dr. Baceledes R. Estal on March 27, 2020 issued a memorandum order no. 9, creating a skeletal workforce in all SDSSU Campuses. The university president identified the different office personnel who will still be reporting to school and those who will be in a Work-From-Home arrangement.&nbsp; The idea is to try to prevent the virus from spreading in the workplace and to keep the SDSSU personnel safe.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Following the memorandum order issued by the university president, the SDSSU Library system adopts a Work-From-Home scheme consistent with COVID-19 Flexi Work Advisory issued by the Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE) and to allow the library personnel to continue working/operating while the ECQ is being implemented. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Virtual Conferencing</span></strong></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">While face-to-face meeting among librarians is impossible due to strict travel restrictions and the current work-from-home arrangement, librarians hold their meeting through online platform.</span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Aside from direct phone calling and chatting, virtual conferencing was also used as an alternative mode of conducting a meeting among librarians of the SDSSU system. The librarians downloaded and installed a cloud-based service application, the ZOOM CLOUD MEETING application in-order to listen and participate in the meeting. It is a video conferencing tool that enabled the librarians to communicate even if they are kilometres away from each other. With the present scenario brought about by this global pandemic, everyone must be savvy of all those technology applications so that they can still function and become productive despite working remotely from their respective homes moving the work to the worker instead of the worker to the work. And thanks to this application as it help us a lot in carrying out our respective duties and responsibilities in our respective libraries.</span></span></p>', NULL, 'Ronie A. Sajelan, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 09:53:40', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-dbfc-4b2d-bf15-49f2a2e95a00', 'Mr. Ronie A. Sajelan, Extend his Services to SDSSU Bislig Campus', 'mr-ronie-a-sajelan-extend-his-services-to-sdssu-bislig-campus', '<p>Library is considered &quot;the heart&quot;&nbsp;of the university. It has a prominent role to play in supporting higher education to fulfil the objectives of its parent institution. The role of the library is much more important since library is considered a prime requirement in higher education to facilitate the teaching-learning and research activities of the students, faculty and other stakeholders of the university.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Library is considered &quot;the heart&quot;&nbsp;of the university. It has a prominent role to play in supporting higher education to fulfil the objectives of its parent institution. The role of the library is much more important since library is considered a prime requirement in higher education to facilitate the teaching-learning and research activities of the students, faculty and other stakeholders of the university.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">&nbsp;The function of library is to provide textbooks, references, periodicals, and other library materials on various subjects to students, teachers and researchers. Students in higher education are to be provided with the facilities necessary for mastering the subject matter, techniques, skills, habits of thought, and methods of work in their chosen field. Classroom instructions alone will not provide all the opportunities needed for attaining all these complex educational objectives. It is here that library come to help the students. </span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">However, the library cannot fully provide its services without a librarian. The presence of the librarian in the library can maximize its functions in providing necessary information to its user because a professional librarian has knowledge of a wide variety of scholarly and public information sources. The college librarian help students, faculty and staff in finding and recommending source materials as well as determining what type of materials they need. His <span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">duties include classifying, cataloguing and organizing library materials so that patrons can easily find and locate the information when needed. </span></span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">Recognizing this vital role of the librarian, Dr. Whelson Pasos, Campus Director of SDSSU Bislig campus requested Mr. Ronie A. Sajelan, the head librarian of SDSSU Tagbina Campus to extend his service to SDSSU Bislig as a shared librarian until they are able to hire one to manage their library. The said request was approved by Dr. Ariston O. Ronquillo, the Campus Director of Tagbina Campus,&nbsp; Mr. Ruel T, Lim, the HR head, Dr. Ramel Tomaquin, the Vice President for Academic Affairs,&nbsp; and Dr. Baceledes R. Estal, the University president.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/public_files/images/Extend%20his%20Services%20to%20SDSSU%20Bislig%20Campus.jpg\" /></span></span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'Ronie A. Sajelan, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 10:10:19', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-e0b6-486e-81d3-380a32f7024a', 'Subscription of the Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom', 'subscription-of-the-digital-library-with-contents-of-e-books-and-virtual-classroom', '<p>SDSSU Library Management System availed the subscription of the Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom, where users can access information both online and offline at anytime and anywhere from any devices - such as a personal computer, laptop, mobile, and tablet to ensure that users get information as where and when they need it with just a few taps on their device.</p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">SDSSU Library Management System availed the subscription of the <strong>Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom</strong>, where users can access information both online and offline at anytime and anywhere from any devices - such as a personal computer, laptop, mobile, and tablet to ensure that users get information as where and when they need it with just a few taps on their device.&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">This is a subscription of the whole SDSSU Library Management System of one (1) site per campus (each online resources).<strong> </strong>Each campus can enjoy a personalized web and mobile experience, with its own carousels and content. It is a user-friendly platform because it is fully inclusive, in all devices and has a text to speech and Open-Dyslexic for students with special needs.</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom</span></strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"> is a NETFLIX-STYLED SOLUTION for INTELLIGENT DIGITAL LIBRARIES, it is a highly engaging, mobile friendly and personalized experience similar to Netflix. It has a Single Access to All Your Learning Content because it has a high-quality content of e-books containing 20,000 plus titles. SDSSU Library Management System can also upload its own existing library materials</span></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/digital%20library.png\" /></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:center\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/virtual%20classroom.png\" /></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Virtual Classroom</span></span></span></p>', NULL, 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 10:17:20', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-e4d6-430c-a12c-362b1b432137', '86th NATIONAL BOOK WEEK CELEBRATION', '86th-national-book-week-celebration', '<p>By virtue of Presidential Proclamation No. 109 series of 1936, the period from November 24-30 is proclaimed as the National Book Week (NBW) celebration. This big event focuses on arousing the national interest in reading good books and various types reading materials to enhance knowledge and skills for social and cultural advancement among Filipino people.</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1prW0Hi_2H3Dk2eWdAd44mPepedced9au/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', '86th NATIONAL BOOK WEEK CELEBRATION.jpg', 'Melanie L. Marquez, RL', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 10:35:34', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-e774-4140-a855-7d33cb46110f', 'SYSTEM-WIDE LIBRARIANS’ AND STAFF MEETING', 'system-wide-librarians-and-staff-meeting', '<p>Despite the pandemic, A F2F system-wide librarians&rsquo; and staff meeting of the seven campuses was held with the approval of the University President on March 22-23, 2021, at the main campus 3rd floor academic building with no less than the Director of Libraries, Mrs. Aida C. Osorio as the presiding officer.</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10If09VhvwuRXUGjriVHoAlSRFVytunjz/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', 'SYSTEM-WIDE-LIBRARIANS-AND-STAFF-MEETING.jpg', 'University Library', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 10:43:51', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-ec42-49fc-94a1-d46844c8efab', 'Trainings on Digital Library with contents of E-books and Virtual Classroom', 'trainings-on-digital-library-with-contents-of-e-books-and-virtual-classroom', '<p>To surely ensure the accessibility of the platform SDSSU Library Management System conducted series of trainings via zoom and google meet for Librarians, IT specialists, Faculty Members, Staff and Students for the 7 campuses of Surigao Del Sur State University</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1V-CUfCBszvGiIHJJioQgR3bzAHJ2lbN3/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', NULL, 'University Library', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-15 10:48:33', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-f11d-4e7a-abdb-f95ebb135279', 'Congratulations to North Eastern Mindanao State University for gaining an approval of the Revised Strategic Performance Management System (SPMS) 2022 by the Civil Service Commission, CARAGA Region.', 'congratulations-to-north-eastern-mindanao-state-university-for-gaining-an-approval-of-the-revised-strategic-performance-management-system-spms-2022-by-the-civil-service-commission-caraga-region', '<p>Congratulations to North Eastern Mindanao State University for gaining an approval of the Revised Strategic Performance Management System (SPMS) 2022 by the Civil Service Comission, CARAGA Region.</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wLPifakgMakO5PuEgxjL52t-4FpWpC7j/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', NULL, 'NEMSU Human Resource Management Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-07-01 00:14:41', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-f506-43d9-8a14-980baa66769d', 'PRIME HRM Maturity Level II in Performance Management.', 'prime-hrm-maturity-level-ii-in-performance-management', '<p>Congratulations</p>', '<p>North Eastern Mindanao State University for having met the standards for PRIME HRM Maturity Level II in Performance Management.</p>\n          \n          <p>Thank you to all Faculty, Staff and Top Management for the Constant Support to HR endeavors.</p>\n          \n          <p>Special Acknowledgement to Dr. Eddie Estal.</p>\n          \n          <p><strong>MABUHAY NEMSU FAMILY!</strong></p>', '306654953_127236023403201_6052379013776000007_n.jpg', 'NEMSU Human Resource Management Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-10-04 14:19:05', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-f981-4cbf-99b5-66c108426de3', 'Congratulations! Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon as the New President of  North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU)', 'congratulations-dr-nemesio-g-loayon-as-the-new-president-of-north-eastern-mindanao-state-university-nemsu', '<p>Congratulations to the Newly-Elected President of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100076188341094&amp;__cft__[0]=AZVQfvBv9wBJ222DogUZmNgTAqFns0a10S4d6Lii5BqIk2TuwrfQfrS6rQcs0_q4Cp5tzcOWV8EuXoCsmducswEDfL0-cav4qkX6UEbCQY3afBsVdMvpJhiqZsx5KtbTsGLl1IIvOgataI-PALvQofRBY4EOWPvxVMLf81yp3k85lMOw_PxvOvK5I6cHSJ23Z_D8eU93dnJ8rg8S4HJ6_oBk&amp;__tn__=-]K*F\" tabindex=\"0\">North Eastern Mindanao State University</a>&nbsp;Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon duly approved by the Governing Board of Regents (BOR).<br />\n          <br />\n          Congratulations, Dr. Loayon!<br />\n          <br />\n          Greetings from Hon. Senator Francis &#39;Chiz&#39; Escudero (Chairman, Senate Committee on Higher Technical Vocational Education), Hon. Senator&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BongGoPage?__cft__[0]=AZVQfvBv9wBJ222DogUZmNgTAqFns0a10S4d6Lii5BqIk2TuwrfQfrS6rQcs0_q4Cp5tzcOWV8EuXoCsmducswEDfL0-cav4qkX6UEbCQY3afBsVdMvpJhiqZsx5KtbTsGLl1IIvOgataI-PALvQofRBY4EOWPvxVMLf81yp3k85lMOw_PxvOvK5I6cHSJ23Z_D8eU93dnJ8rg8S4HJ6_oBk&amp;__tn__=-]K*F\" tabindex=\"0\">Bong Go</a>&nbsp;(Chairman, Senate Committee on Sports), Hon.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/markgobaguio?__cft__[0]=AZVQfvBv9wBJ222DogUZmNgTAqFns0a10S4d6Lii5BqIk2TuwrfQfrS6rQcs0_q4Cp5tzcOWV8EuXoCsmducswEDfL0-cav4qkX6UEbCQY3afBsVdMvpJhiqZsx5KtbTsGLl1IIvOgataI-PALvQofRBY4EOWPvxVMLf81yp3k85lMOw_PxvOvK5I6cHSJ23Z_D8eU93dnJ8rg8S4HJ6_oBk&amp;__tn__=-]K*F\" tabindex=\"0\">Congressman Mark Go</a>&nbsp;(Chairman, House Committee on Higher and Technical Education),&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/PhCHED.gov?__cft__[0]=AZVQfvBv9wBJ222DogUZmNgTAqFns0a10S4d6Lii5BqIk2TuwrfQfrS6rQcs0_q4Cp5tzcOWV8EuXoCsmducswEDfL0-cav4qkX6UEbCQY3afBsVdMvpJhiqZsx5KtbTsGLl1IIvOgataI-PALvQofRBY4EOWPvxVMLf81yp3k85lMOw_PxvOvK5I6cHSJ23Z_D8eU93dnJ8rg8S4HJ6_oBk&amp;__tn__=-]K*F\" tabindex=\"0\">Commission on Higher Education(CHED)</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/commlibre?__cft__[0]=AZVQfvBv9wBJ222DogUZmNgTAqFns0a10S4d6Lii5BqIk2TuwrfQfrS6rQcs0_q4Cp5tzcOWV8EuXoCsmducswEDfL0-cav4qkX6UEbCQY3afBsVdMvpJhiqZsx5KtbTsGLl1IIvOgataI-PALvQofRBY4EOWPvxVMLf81yp3k85lMOw_PxvOvK5I6cHSJ23Z_D8eU93dnJ8rg8S4HJ6_oBk&amp;__tn__=-]K*F\" tabindex=\"0\">Comm. Jo Mark M. Libre</a>&nbsp;and Hon. Atty. Ronnie Azura (Representative from the Office of Senator Francis Escudero).<br />\n          <br />\n          All Glory to the Almighty Father through the Son and King</p>', '', 'NEW-PRES.jpg', 'Office of the Board and University Secretary', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-12-06 15:42:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bc-fd84-490e-830e-e4d5ee7a0d69', 'NEMSU is recognized by the CHED Regional Office', 'nemsu-is-recognized-by-the-ched-regional-office', '<p><strong>NEMSU </strong>is recognized by the <strong>CHED Regional Office</strong> in the following fields/areas: For complying Guidelines on the Implementation of Return to Collegiate Atheletics Competition during Pandemic (Cantilan, Main, Cagwait), for the One Million Tree Planting Advocacy Program (Main, Bislig, Cagwait), for Prompt Submission of CHED Scholarship Program Documents (Lianga, Bislig) as Delivering HEI for Full and Part-time Scholarships (Main) and recognized partner in HEMIS Annual Data Collection (Cantilan). Awarding at Malvar Hall, Balanghai Hotel Butuan City.</p>', '<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KekfJ579g1-LsVXTZyd5v9c0W9WM5IrU//preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>', 'ched-20140624.jpg', 'NEMSU', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-12-19 12:45:06', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-00eb-4458-90b7-c42e7c6bf3e4', 'Goal for GOLDS, NEMSU maintains lead as this Year\'s Best Performing SUC in SPORTS during the recently concluded Mindanao Association of State Tertiary Schools Friendship Games in Mati. Congratulations to All of us! (photo credit to The Mindanao Tech)', 'goal-for-golds-nemsu-maintains-lead-as-this-years-best-performing-suc-in-sports-during-the-recently-concluded-mindanao-association-of-state-tertiary-schools-friendship-games-in-mati-congratulations-to-all-of-us-photo-credit-to-the-mindanao-tech', '', '', '316556245_229981312686180_3181743583918676386_n.jpg', 'Photo credit to The Mindanao Tech', NULL, 'news', 1, '2022-11-25 18:20:34', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-04bf-439f-beba-8accf5c428b8', 'Atty Ronnie Azura visits NEMSU for a consultative meeting', 'atty-ronnie-azura-visits-nemsu-for-a-consultative-meeting', '<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">LOOK: The Oversight Resource Person of Senator Francis &ldquo;Chiz&rsquo; Escudero for NEMSU, Atty. Ronnie Azura visits the University for a consultative meeting last February 2, 2023.</span></span></p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">LOOK: The Oversight Resource Person of Senator Francis &ldquo;Chiz&rsquo; Escudero for NEMSU, Atty. Ronnie Azura visits the University for a consultative meeting last February 2, 2023. EMS President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon and key officials welcomed in the arrival of Atty. Azura. The President highlighted in strengthening the relationship between NEMSU and external partners for support and resource generation. Atty. Azura envisions of bringing the University in greater heights with good governance and empowering mindset through the support from the Office of Senator Francis Escudero. His university tour under his supervision oversees the realistic situation on the ground of the different HEIs. The meeting opens comprehensive discussions on the existing concerns in instructions, research, extension and production services.&nbsp;</span></span></p>', 'atty.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-02-05 05:49:01', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-0834-49dc-b14b-493f1848b6da', 'LOOK: Hon. Jo Mark Libre and Atty. Ronnie Azura extend insightful messages in the opening of NEMSU Strategic Planning 2023', 'look-hon-jo-mark-libre-and-atty-ronnie-azura-extend-insightful-messages-in-the-opening-of-nemsu-strategic-planning-2023', '<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">LOOK: The good Commissioner of CHED, Hon. Jo Mark Libre virtually graced the opening program for NEMSU Strategic Planning 2023.&nbsp;</span></span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">LOOK: The good Commissioner of CHED, Hon. Jo Mark Libre virtually graced the opening program for NEMSU Strategic Planning 2023.&nbsp;Hon. Libre reminded everyone to always be at the top of innovation and maintain the momentum to hasten the higher education reforms. The presence of the Commissioner fuels the event as it manifested through inspired engagement of the participants. Atty. Ronnie Azura, The Oversight Resource Person of Senator Francis &ldquo;Chiz&rsquo; Escudero for NEMSU also extended his insightful message through his virtual presence in the event. In his message, he strengthened the essence of NEMSU towards quality and excellent higher education are indications in the strategic planning. The University secures that the elements in the strategic planning addresses the call and needs of its clients and stakeholders. </span></span></p>', 'libre.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-02-05 06:05:22', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-0b7d-4ce6-96ca-4f80df202686', 'CHED Memorandum Order No. 12 Series of 2018\r\n2016 SUC Levelling Results, SUC Levelling Benefits, and SUC Levelling Appeal Procedures', 'ched-memo', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ched-memo-6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />', 'ched-memo-0.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-05-30 11:59:11', '2023-05-30 11:59:11', '2023-05-30 11:59:11'),
('987727bd-13ff-4af5-b3e9-153e7561a5ba', 'Enrollment Period for Graduate Studies Student', 'enrollment-period-for-graduate-studies-student', NULL, '<p>The enrollment period of Graduate Studies Student will be extended until June 24, 2017.</p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-06-15 11:54:04', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-158f-4c00-89b2-23352519f873', 'Graduate Studies Announcement', 'graduate-studies-announcement', NULL, '<p>Classes in the Graduate Studies will start on June 24, 2017.</p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-06-21 09:10:15', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-16f6-4a2b-b449-f3749fa2373a', 'Graduate School students enrolled in Dissertation', 'graduate-school-students-enrolled-in-dissertation', NULL, '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Graduate School students enrolled in Dissertation, Thesis and Research classes are required to attend to the Seminar workshop on Qualitative Research Methodology on July 15, 2017 at the SDSSU Main Campus Audio Visual Center. Registration fee is P500 to cover kit, snacks and accommodation of speaker</span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Other interested students will be excused from their respective classes should they wish to attend.</span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dean,</span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Graduate School</span></p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-07-14 16:25:41', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('987727bd-1870-4a77-8c3c-93418bba6565', 'All First Year Students (1st Sem.)', 'all-first-year-students-1st-sem', NULL, '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><big><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:#002060\">What: Intake Interview</span></strong></span></span></big></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><big><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:#002060\">Where: Guidance Center</span></strong></span></span></big></p>\n          \n          <table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover table-striped\">\n              <thead>\n                  <tr>\n                      <th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-align:center\">Date</th>\n                      <th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-align:center\">College</th>\n                      <th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-align:center\">Guidance&nbsp; Counselor</th>\n                  </tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"3\">\n                      <p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">August 21-31,2017</span></strong></p>\n          \n                      <p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(09:00 A.M. - 4:00 P.M)</span></strong></p>\n                      </td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">CAS</td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">ARMIERA B. RAMIREZ</td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">CBM</td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">NELIA THERESA E. BURGOS</td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">CTE &amp; CECST</td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\">JOAN M. ZARTIGA</td>\n                  </tr>\n              </tbody>\n          </table>\n          \n          <p><br />\n          <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong><span style=\"color:#002060\">Note:</span></strong><strong> </strong><strong><span style=\"color:red\">Come in group, maximum of 5 members. </span></strong></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong><span style=\"color:red\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; This is a clearance item </span></strong><strong><span style=\"color:red\">(1<sup>st</sup> Sem.).</span></strong></span></span></p>\n          \n          <p>&nbsp;</p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-08-18 13:39:26', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-19f3-4e76-8d0b-8c5873eefb0d', 'All Graduating Students ', 'all-graduating-students', NULL, '<p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><big>All Graduating Students are required to take the Personality Test on August 21-31, 2017&nbsp;@ the Guidance Center.</big></span></span></p>\n          \n          <table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover table-striped\">\n              <thead>\n                  <tr>\n                      <th colspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\" style=\"text-align:center\">TEST SCHEDULE</th>\n                  </tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1<sup>st</sup> Batch</span></span></td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">9:00 &ndash; 10:00 A.M.</span></span></td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2<sup>nd</sup> Batch</span></span></td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">10:30 - 11:30 A.M.</span></span></td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3<sup>rd</sup> Batch</span></span></td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1:30 - 2:30P.M.</span></span></td>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4<sup>th</sup> Batch</span></span></td>\n                      <td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3:00 &ndash; 4:00P.M.</span></span></td>\n                  </tr>\n              </tbody>\n          </table>\n          \n          <p>&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Note: Come in group, maximum of 10 members.&nbsp;<br />\n          &nbsp; &nbsp;This is a clearance item.</span></span></strong></span></p>\n          \n          <p>&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p>&nbsp;</p>\n          \n          <p><br />\n          &nbsp;</p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-08-18 13:54:19', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-1e24-49a8-85ee-bec2aa060c52', 'Graduating Students As Of October 2017', 'graduating-students-as-of-october-2017', NULL, '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">TO ALL </span></span><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><strong>GRADUATING STUDENTS AS OF OCTOBER 2017,&nbsp;</strong></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">PLEASE SUBMIT YOUR</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"> <strong><span style=\"font-size:18px\">APPLICATION FOR GRADUATION&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:16px\">AT THE REGISTRAR&#39;S OFFICE <strong>ON OR BEFORE SEPTEMBER 29, 2017.</strong>&nbsp;FORMS WILL BE AVAILABLE AT YOUR RESPECTIVE COLLEGES. PLEASE BE GUIDED.&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">THANK YOU.</span></span></p>\n          \n          <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><em><strong><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">THE REGISTRAR</span></span></strong></em></p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-09-20 14:20:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-1fd2-4623-8956-e17e11d89fe1', 'Last day of enrollment for the Graduate Studies', 'last-day-of-enrollment-for-the-graduate-studies', NULL, '<p>Last day of enrollment for the Graduate Studies of Surigao Del Sur State University-Main Campus will be on <strong><span style=\"color:#ff0000\">November 25, 2017</span></strong></p>\n          ', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2017-11-23 09:39:56', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-2134-4e33-ab16-e85f0ff33df5', 'Enrollment is extended until August 13, 2021', 'enrollment-is-extended-until-august-13-2021', NULL, '<p><br />\n          <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Undergraduate.png\" /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2021-09-07 01:58:26', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-2290-4ee2-8ea8-665a8908c8f0', 'SDSSU Graduate School classes will start on August 28, 2021', 'sdssu-graduate-school-classes-will-start-on-august-28-2021', NULL, '<p><br />\n          <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Announcement.JPG\" /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2021-09-07 02:01:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-27dd-4184-ab8b-edf280f6efba', 'NOTICE OF SEARCH AND CALL FOR APPLICATIONS', 'notice-of-search-and-call-for-applications', NULL, '<p><strong>NOTICE OF SEARCH AND CALL FOR APPLICATIONS</strong></p>\n          \n          <p>The Board of Regents of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU)<br />\n          formally and publicly announces that the Search for Presidency of the University is now open. Interested applicants and/ or nominees are invited to send their formal applications to the Search Committee for Presidency.<br />\n          <br />\n          MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:<br />\n          1. Not less than thirty-five (35) years old and not a day older than the sixty-<br />\n          first (61st) birthday at the time of the expiration of the term of the incumbent<br />\n          President;<br />\n          2. A Filipino citizen;<br />\n          3. Holder of an earned doctorate degree from a CHED-recognized HEI or foreign<br />\n          institution accredited by its respective higher education ministry/commission<br />\n          or appropriate regulatory body which is defined as Level 8 in the QPF, under<br />\n          RA No. 10968;<br />\n          4. With a proven track record as SUC/LUC administrator (e.g., president,<br />\n          vice-president, dean, campus administrator, director) or high-level management executive/administrator, whether in the public or private sector, for at least five years; Nomenclature of the position, especially in the private sector may be clarified by the GB as long position is high-level management, and,<br />\n          5. Must not have been convicted for a crime involving moral turpitude, or an<br />\n          offense punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding six (6) years, or<br />\n          suspended administratively for twelve (12) months, or dismissed from the<br />\n          service.<br />\n          DOCUMENTARY REQUIREMENTS:<br />\n          1. Formal Application Letter addressed to:<br />\n          Hon JO MARK M. LIBRE, DPA<br />\n          Commissioner, CHED<br />\n          CP Garcia Ave, Diliman Quezon City<br />\n          2. Detailed curriculum vitae, attested and signed by the applicant.<br />\n          3. Transcript of records, training certifications, professional accreditations, diplomas, and employment/service records;<br />\n          4. Published research work, if any;<br />\n          5. A signed and notarized statement containing the Proposed Vision, Mission, and Development Goals for NEMSU by the applicant;<br />\n          6. Certificates/clearances from the following government agencies, obtained no more than three (3) months from the filing date of the application, indicating that the applicant has not been found guilty in any administrative or criminal case:<br />\n          &bull; National Bureau of Investigation (NBI)<br />\n          &bull; Sandiganbayan<br />\n          &bull; Civil Service Commission (CSC)<br />\n          &bull; Office of the City Prosecutor<br />\n          &bull; Office of the Ombudsman (for government employees)<br />\n          &bull; Institution/Company where the applicant is presently employed<br />\n          In case of delay in the issuance of the agency/office concerned due to pandemic or fortuitous events, proof of payment of application fee may be<br />\n          used in the application subject to submission of the Certificates/Clearances at the time of the pre-evaluation process by the SCP. The deadline is set for September 23, 2022.<br />\n          7. Birth certificate authenticated by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA);<br />\n          8. Medical certificate of physical fitness issued by a physician from a government health institution, not in any way connected with the applicant or the SUC applied for;<br />\n          9. Drug testing certificate pursuant to the CSC Memorandum Circular No. 13,<br />\n          s. 2017;<br />\n          10. Neuro-psychiatric examination results were obtained from a government health institution. In case there is none, the neuro-psychiatric examination result shall be obtained from a DOH-accredited institution not connected with the applicant;<br />\n          11. Duly accomplished, computerized, and notarized Personal Data Sheet (CSC Form 212); and, other documents that may be required by the SUC GB.<br />\n          An applicant who does not meet any of the above minimum qualifications and fails to submit any of the documentary requirements shall automatically be disqualified from the search process.<br />\n          Important: Interested Applicants must send the above-stated documents in one (1) original and six certified true copies on or before August 31, 2022 to any of the following:<br />\n          NEMSU- SCP SECRETARIAT<br />\n          MS. CATHERINE F. SALOMON STEPHANY L. CONDEZ, LLB(J.D.)<br />\n          Board Secretary V Chief of Staff , Office of Commissioner Libre<br />\n          NEMSU Commission on Higher Education<br />\n          Tandag City, Surigao del Sur Quezon City<br />\n          MT - Aug. 6, 13 &amp; 20, 2022</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 0, '2022-08-06 11:09:22', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-296a-4355-a5cf-98d0f708a76b', 'Please be informed that today (January 25, 2023) will be the official start of classes for the 2nd Semester, A.Y 2022-2023', 'please-be-informed-that-today-january-25-2023-will-be-the-official-start-of-classes-for-the-2nd-semester-ay-2022-2023', NULL, '<p><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/COL-Announcement.jpg\" /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2023-01-25 21:41:02', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-2ac3-4632-a77b-65c159153bd3', 'Please be Guided for the schedules of Adding and Dropping of Subjects for 2nd Semester (AY 2022-2023)', 'please-be-guided-for-the-schedules-of-adding-and-dropping-of-subjects-for-2nd-semester-ay-2022-2023', NULL, '<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/public_files/images/A01-Registrar.jpg\" class=\"img img-responsive\"  /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2023-01-24 21:51:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-2be4-45fc-9aab-fa5f39af8007', 'LOOK: The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) will open its classes for Second Semester (AY 2022-2023) on January 30, 2023.', 'look-the-north-eastern-mindanao-state-university-nemsu-will-open-its-classes-for-second-semester-ay-2022-2023-on-january-30-2023', NULL, '<p><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/PIP01-NEMSU.jpg\" /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2023-01-25 21:53:45', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('987727bd-2d19-4770-9f4f-584bac2ff4ec', 'LOOK: NEMSU Simultaneous Class Opening Program for the Second Semester of Academic Year 2022-2023 on January 30, 2023. See Yah!', 'look-nemsu-simultaneous-class-opening-program-for-the-second-semester-of-academic-year-2022-2023-on-january-30-2023-see-yah', NULL, '<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/public_files/images/PIP01-opening.jpg\" class=\"img img-responsive\" /></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'announcement', 1, '2023-01-27 12:12:28', '2023-02-14 03:49:12', '2023-02-14 03:49:12'),
('98a13af4-c520-4fce-a0fd-e8539a02a97d', '2023 NATIONAL WOMEN’S MONTH CELEBRATION LAUNCHING PROGRAM', '2023-national-womens-month-celebration-launching-program', '<p>The NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon gracefully extended his message during the launching of National Women&#39;s Month today, March 1, 2023 at NEMSU audio-visual center.</p>', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col-md-3 col-sm-3 col-xs-3\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/1(2).png\" /></div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"col-md-3 col-sm-3 col-xs-3\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/3%20(1).png\" /></div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"col-md-3 col-sm-3 col-xs-3\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/6%20(1).png\" /></div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"col-md-3 col-sm-3 col-xs-3\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/5.png\" /></div>\r\n            </div>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon gracefully extended his message during the launching of National Women&#39;s Month today, March 1, 2023 at NEMSU audio-visual center.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Gracing the event to inspire the participants in his message: &ldquo;Today, we celebrate the countless women who have fought tirelessly and courageously for equality, justice, and opportunity particularly here in our beloved institution- NEMSU. &nbsp;We also reaffirm our commitment to advancing the rights and opportunities for women especially in all the positions which our University has been hiring. &nbsp;In our pursuit for PRIME-HRM initiatives, we do not forget to integrate the ideals and principles of women empowerment and equal opportunity among others.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The full participation of women is a foundational tenet of a progressive and dynamic University. &nbsp;Women continue to lead as advocates for reproductive rights, champions of gender equality, and LGBTQI+ equality. &nbsp;Throughout history, women have opened the doors of opportunity for subsequent generations of dreamers and doers.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">NEMSU is lucky enough to have women who form part of the top management of the University. Our 3 vice presidents are all women. That&rsquo;s why, even CHED Regional Director George Colorado, dubbed them as Loayon&rsquo;s Little Angels. Deeper than that, it symbolizes women empowerment and equal opportunity among others.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">As community leaders in the academe, women help lead our University to a gender-responsive government agency. As innovators, entrepreneurs, and essential workers of NEMSU, they represent the very best of the University.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Let us continue to have a University established upon a profound but simple idea that all people are created equal.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">My administration and leadership is committed to upholding that idea and to making its promise real for everyone here in NEMSU. &nbsp;Our GAD Focal Person is always ready to assist us to advance gender equity.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The Office of the NEMSU President promotes the rights and opportunities of women across campuses, which outlines my Administration&rsquo;s commitment to equal access to for women, including our students.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">My Administration will continue to defend women&rsquo;s rights to ensure that all NEMSU employees, regardless of their gender, race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or income, have the ability to make the choices that are right for themselves and their families.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n            <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">This month, as we continue our work to advance gender equity and equality, let us celebrate the contributions of women. Good afternoon and Mabuhay!&rdquo;</span><br />\r\n            &nbsp;</p>', '2023-national-womens-month-celebration-launching-program.png', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-03-07 17:37:11', '2023-03-07 17:37:11', '2023-03-07 17:37:11'),
('98bfe361-6e27-11ee-a3fc-a233a240566f', 'Memorandum of Agreement with the City Government of Tandag', 'NEMSU-TANDAG-2023', 'NEMSU officially signs Memorandum of Agreement with the City Government of Tandag on strengthening partnership and sharing of resources, skills and human resource.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nNEMSU officially signs Memorandum of Agreement with the City Government of Tandag on strengthening partnership and sharing of resources, skills and human resource. <br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tdg-moa-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n', 'tdg-moa-00.jpg', 'Office of the Campus Director - Tandag', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-10-18 18:33:11', '2023-10-18 18:33:11', '2023-10-18 18:33:11'),
('99bc618b-3276-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐤𝐬 𝟒𝐭𝐡 𝐢𝐧 𝐓𝐨𝐩 𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐚𝐠𝐚 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐞𝐬 – 𝐖𝐞𝐛𝐨𝐦𝐞𝐭𝐫𝐢𝐜𝐬', '2023-nemsu-ranks', 'Based on web visibility, transparency, and excellence, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (formerly Surigao del Sur State University) placed 4th in the Caraga Region according to the recent report of Webometrics Ranking of World Universities (July 2023 edition).', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Based on web visibility, transparency, and excellence, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (formerly Surigao del Sur State University) placed 4th in the Caraga Region according to the recent report of Webometrics Ranking of World Universities (July 2023 edition).</span></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Evaluated by the Cybermetrics Lab, the global ranking encompasses 31,000 Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) across 200 countries, and operates on the aim of promoting general accessibility to the academic and cultural knowledge generated in diverse HEIs.</span></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Moreover, the institution also managed to break into the 215th ranking in the Top Philippine Universities of the same quantitative research body, further cementing its place in the educational landscape of the country.</span></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">With NEMSU’s vision of being an epicenter of research and development, the said recognition proves that we are on the right track towards the goal of being a leading glocal university.</span></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">You can access the full list here:</span></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<u><a href=\"https://www.webometrics.info/en/asia/philippines\" target=\"_blank\">www.webometrics.info</a></u><br>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\nWritten by: John Damort Guingguing\r\n\r\n', 'covernemsu.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-02 15:09:53', '2023-08-02 15:09:53', '2023-08-02 15:09:53'),
('9a64eb87-3284-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Orientation CUM Consultative Meeting of BAC', 'BAC-Consultative-meeting-2023', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU conducted an Orientation cum Consultative Meeting of BAC, BAC Secretariat, TWG and other Procurement Personnel of the University on August 1-2, 2023 ', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/bac-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU conducted an Orientation cum Consultative Meeting of BAC, BAC Secretariat, TWG and other Procurement Personnel of the University on August 1-2, 2023 at Selades Apartelle and Convention Center.. The event made possible to ensure the smooth and efficient procurement and BAC transactions. Dr. Florife O. Urbiztondo, CAO-Admin, shared her knowledge on essential topics relative to the event. NEMSU BAC and Procurement Personnel across the seven (7) campuses participated the event.\r\n<br/>\r\n', 'bac-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-04 13:30:53', '2023-08-04 13:30:53', '2023-08-04 13:30:53'),
('9b14acae-2214-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM CELEBRATES 87TH NATIONAL BOOK WEEK', '87th-National-book-Week', '', '\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Every year the National Book Week Celebration has been observed all over the country with a varied program of activities.<br><br>\r\n\r\nIt is a fact that the National Book Week celebration is organized by the Philippine Library Association, Inc. (formally known as the Philippine Library Association) intended to encourage reading and literacy among Filipinos and to promote Public libraries in the Philippines. It is with an utmost aim to arouse the national interest in reading good books and designed to sell the public library to the community by focusing the attention of the people on its resources and nature of the services even in this new normal condition. Also, encourage greater participation in the varied activities which include the essay writing contest, poster making contest, and other forms of challenges by the public various libraries, and educational institutions to make the celebration laudable all over the country.<br><br>\r\n\r\nIn line with the historical background of the event and the present time during new normal NEMSU formerly Surigao Del Sur State University spearheaded by the Library Management System conducted similar activities on the 87th National Book Week Celebration on the theme “Outcomes. Outreach. Outstanding: Libraries Beyond Boundaries”. A weeklong virtual celebration was formally started with the opening program on the first day Nov. 24, 2021, at exactly 02:00 in the afternoon. The said celebration has seven (7) activities which participated by the students of the different Colleges namely: Virtual Essay Writing Contest, Virtual Poster Making Contest, Virtual Calligraphy Slogan Contest, Online Library Trivia, and Social Media Contest such as Book Selfie, Book Face and Tiktok: Pass a Book Challenge virtually. All of the winners received cash prizes and certificates during the Culminating Activity on the 5th day with our resource speaker Dr. Anita C. Sornito, BLIS program coordinator of the University of Southern Mindanao, Kabacan, Philippines. <br><br>\r\n\r\nThe Library Management has also library awardees such as Most Valuable Faculty Users, Top Most Faculty Library Users, and Top Most Digital Library Student Users both Graduate and Under Graduate Students. Highlighted in the awarding ceremony are the Faculty awardees for being the first Digital Library Advocators and Surigao Del Sur State University as the First ODILO Digital Library Subscriber in Caraga Region..<br><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bokwek12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<b>FACULTY AWARDS</b></div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><p>ODILO AWARDEES (Digital Library)</p>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libaward08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', 'bokwek01.jpg', 'Ms. Realyn B. Medrano', 10, 'news', 1, '2021-12-01 08:09:53', '2021-12-01 08:09:53', '2021-12-01 08:09:53'),
('9c3e913b-6e29-11ee-a3fc-a233a240566f', 'AACCUP Hybrid Accreditation Survey Visit for Levels 3 and 4 Phase I', 'AACCUP-October-2023', 'AACCUP Hybrid Accreditation Survey Visit for Levels 3 and 4 Phase I of the Graduate School and the College of Teacher Education Programs on October 16-20,2023.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe Ongoing AACCUP Hybrid Accreditation Survey Visit for Levels 3 and 4 Phase I of the Graduate School and the College of Teacher Education Programs on October 16-20,2023.<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aaccup-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n', 'aaccup-00.jpg', 'Office of the Campus Director - Tandag', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-10-16 11:30:11', '2023-10-16 11:30:11', '2023-10-16 11:30:11'),
('9e0bc2db-6de9-11f0-ae5d-a233a240566f', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Information Unit hosts the NEMSULTI:', 'Information-Unit-hosts-the-NEMSULTI', '5th Executive Press Conference at NEMSU Tagbina Campus on June 2, as an avenue for open discussion and collaborative promotion across seven campuses.', '</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Information Unit hosts the NEMSULTI: 5th Executive Press Conference at NEMSU Tagbina Campus on June 2, as an avenue for open discussion and collaborative promotion across seven campuses. Participants from other campuses join via Zoom, ensuring inclusive participation through the online platform. The event also aims to deliver comprehensive updates on university initiatives, address key concerns, and foster a unified approach to the continuous development of the institution.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe press conference highlights significant accomplishments and ongoing initiatives within the academic year 2024-2025, reinforcing NEMSU\'s commitment to academic excellence and community empowerment.', 'Information Unit hosts the NEMSULTI.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-06-04 16:31:19', NULL, NULL),
('9ed2925f-91e4-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', 'THEY HAVE CONQUERED THE BAR EXAMS! ', 'THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS', 'At exactly 6:17 PM, the #AMYzingFive of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) College of Law triumphantly stepped out of the gates of Ateneo de Davao University – Senior High School (ADDU-SHS), marking the end of their 3-day battle in the 2025 Bar Examinations. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS 6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nAt exactly 6:17 PM, the #AMYzingFive of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) College of Law triumphantly stepped out of the gates of Ateneo de Davao University – Senior High School (ADDU-SHS), marking the end of their 3-day battle in the 2025 Bar Examinations. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nWhat began in the early mornings, with courage as their armor and faith as their shield, has now reached its victorious close. After endless nights of preparation, years of sacrifice, and the unwavering support of their community, they have finally conquered one of the greatest challenges of their lives. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nToday, they walk out not just as examinees, but as inspirations that embodying perseverance, resilience, and the unbreakable spirit of future lawyers. As they exit the testing center, they carry with them not only the pride of their families and friends but also the hopes of the entire NEMSU College of Law family and the people of Caraga. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nMabuhay ang ating #AMYzingFive of NEMSU College of Law! The exams may be over, but the journey to justice and service has only just begun. \r\n#amyzingfive\r\n#AMYzingBar2025\r\n#nemsucollegeoflaw', 'THEY-HAVE-CONQUERED-THE-BAR-EXAMS.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-09-15 11:27:22', NULL, NULL),
('a004f174-f86b-11ed-affb-a600064b4626', 'NEMSU attends the virtual Technical Budget Hearing for FY 2024 Budget Proposals with Department of Budget Management (DBM)', 'DBM-Virtual-meeting', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/DBM-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>The North Eastern Mindanao State University attends the virtual Technical Budget Hearing for FY 2024 Budget Proposals with Department of Budget Management (DBM). In attendance are NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon and key officials, DBM Regional Director Maria Fe D. Jagna, DBM-RO Personnel, Mr. Elvin Chato, and Ms. Rhona Mae U. Gabia. The partnership between NEMSU and DBM Region XIII entail formal consultation, queries, and technical assistance provided by the department’s Budget and Management Specialists assigned to the University. </p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>The preparation of the University’s budget is a critical process that involves evaluating the proposed PPAs. With the presence of the DBM specialists, the activity ensures that the university’s proposed PPAs will be prioritized based on their importance, alignment with the university’s goals and objectives, as to completeness to render the proposals implementation ready.</p>', 'DBM-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-05-05 11:11:02', '2023-05-05 11:11:02', '2023-05-05 11:11:02'),
('a01ebd46-86f3-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴 𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀 𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱 𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴 𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲, 𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗿𝗮𝗶𝘀𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗰𝗲𝗿𝗲𝗺𝗼𝗻𝘆', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲', 'To begin the first day of the ASEAN Month Celebration, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) – Tandag Campus marked an ASEAN-themed Flag Parade and Flag-Raising ceremony today, August 18, at the CAS Grounds, highlighting regional unity as students, faculty, and staff came together, donning national costumes from various ASEAN countries. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nTo begin the first day of the ASEAN Month Celebration, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) – Tandag Campus marked an ASEAN-themed Flag Parade and Flag-Raising ceremony today, August 18, at the CAS Grounds, highlighting regional unity as students, faculty, and staff came together, donning national costumes from various ASEAN countries. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nEach college and department represented assigned ASEAN countries through their attire, with the College of Arts and Sciences embodying Vietnam, the College of Business and Administration representing Brunei, and the College of Engineering and Technology channeling Indonesia. The College of Information Technology Education represented Malaysia, while the Colleges of Teacher Education, Law, and Medicine personified Laos, Cambodia, and Thailand, respectively.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn his message during the flag-raising ceremony, Dr. Floresito D. Calub, OIC Campus Director, emphasized that the ASEAN celebration promotes unity beyond national borders.\r\nHe highlighted that cultural diversity, regional cooperation, and mutual respect are the driving forces that propel the community of nations forward.\r\nBy embracing these values in line with SDG 4: Quality Education, the university reinforces its commitment to shaping globally aware students who will contribute to building a more united ASEAN community.\r\n<br/><br/>', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀-𝗔𝗦𝗘𝗔𝗡-𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗱-𝗳𝗹𝗮𝗴-𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗱𝗲-1.jpg', 'Rachelle Mae Enoc', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-08-18 05:20:39', NULL, NULL),
('a35ba26a-02a7-11ef-904a-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔\'𝐬 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐋𝐚𝐰 𝐇𝐨𝐬𝐭𝐬 𝐋𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐮𝐫𝐞 𝐒𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐞𝐬 𝐨𝐧 𝐑𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐚𝐥 𝐋𝐚𝐰', 'Remedial-Law-2024', 'The College of Law of North Eastern Mindanao State University  (NEMSU) conducted its highly anticipated lecture series focusing on Remedial Law. The lecture took place on April 24, 2024, at Room 2 of the College of Law Building. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/remedial-law/remedial-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/remedial-law/remedial-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/remedial-law/remedial-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe College of Law of North Eastern Mindanao State University  (NEMSU) conducted its highly anticipated lecture series focusing on Remedial Law. The lecture took place on April 24, 2024, at Room 2 of the College of Law Building. \r\n<br><br>\r\nGuiding the insightful discourse was Atty. Mario L. Luna, a distinguished lawyer and author of \"Disquisition and Jurisprudence on Remedial Law.\" With his expertise and extensive experience, Atty. Luna adeptly discussed the complexities of this legal topic, offering invaluable insights to the participants.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe lecture series, designed to provide a comprehensive understanding and practical insights on Remedial Law, is divided into two parts. The second part and continuation of the lecture series are scheduled on April 26, 2024, Saturday.\r\n<br/>', 'remedial-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-04-24 12:57:48', '2024-04-24 12:57:48', '2024-04-24 12:57:48'),
('a3c4093a-ca10-11ee-aa14-a233a240566f', 'The Executive Committee of North Eastern Mindanao State University has convened for an Executive Meeting and Direction Setting session at the University Board Room on this auspicious day of February 13, 2024.', 'Executive-Meeting-2024', 'The Executive Committee of North Eastern Mindanao State University has convened for an Executive Meeting and Direction Setting session at the University Board Room on this auspicious day of February 13, 2024.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/acos-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/acos-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/acos-003.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe Executive Committee of North Eastern Mindanao State University has convened for an Executive Meeting and Direction Setting session at the University Board Room on this auspicious day of February 13, 2024.\r\n<br/>', 'acos-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-02-13 09:40:11', '2024-02-13 09:40:11', '2024-02-13 09:40:11');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('a44405fc-0b3f-11ee-affb-a600064b4626', 'Message of President Loayon on the Ocassion of the 2nd Quarter joint-academic and administrative councils meeting', 'acoadcosm2023', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/adcosm-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Beautiful morning to all of us!\r\nIt is indeed a very good opportunity to be with you today as we come together to once again validate our commitment to public service. Let us all be inspired by the wisdom that says, “The only way to work great is to love what you do.” If you have not found it yet, do not settle but keep looking.\r\nExhibiting our great work also needs God’s guidance. Hence, as Matthew teaches us, let us acknowledge God before men so that we will also be acknowledged by the Father who is in heaven.\r\nLet me congratulate our ROTC Unit led by Ms. Sol Virtudazo, our NSTP Director, for the successful conduct of the Regional Annual Administrative Tactical Inspection held last week.\r\nLikewise, let us congratulate the College of Teacher Education for the successful conduct of the Teachers’ Congress held in Cantilan also last week, led by the Dean Prof. Annie Y. Samarca, and of course the notable performance of Lianga Campus for producing a topnotcher in the recent LET results!\r\nToday, let us again engage in fruitful dialogues which are imperative for the success of our joint-academic and administrative council meeting. With the freshness of the green environment of the San Miguel Campus under the leadership of Prof. Clemencia Sumagaysay, may it flourish our creative minds to create and develop things that are worthwhile for the NEMSU Community. The different programs, projects, and other undertakings will strengthen the foundation of NEMSU as the laying portals of the brilliant hatch.\r\nFor the love of learning, coupled with our deep commitment to public service, let the NEMSU education bring a positive impact to all our valued stakeholders. MABUHAY!</span></p>', 'adcosm-01.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-06-09 11:40:11', '2023-06-09 11:40:11', '2023-06-09 11:40:11'),
('a517edf5-e4f4-11ef-8bc4-a233a240566f', '𝐁𝐮𝐢𝐥𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐁𝐫𝐢𝐝𝐠𝐞𝐬: 𝐀 𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞 𝐚𝐭 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔', '𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞', 'Strengthening partnerships and fostering collaboration, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) successfully conducted  the Stakeholder’s Meeting for the College of Medicine on January 28, 2025, at the NEMSU Old Boardroom.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nStrengthening partnerships and fostering collaboration, the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) successfully conducted  the Stakeholder’s Meeting for the College of Medicine on January 28, 2025, at the NEMSU Old Boardroom.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAmong the participants were University Key Officials, Dr. Oscar M. De Jesus Jr., Provincial Health Officer representing the Office of the Provincial Governor and Provincial Health Office; Atty. Dona Marie Flores Trinidad, representative of the 1st District Congressman of Surigao del Sur; Dr. Frederick C. Amhihan, Education Program Supervisor of CHED Caraga; and Indigenous Peoples representatives, city health officers, barangay representatives, and Dr. Janice V. Pagaran-Alcordo, Medical Center Chief II of ASTMMC, alongside key personnel from ASTMMC.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nOpening the program, Dr. Evelyn T. Bagood, Campus Director, highlighted the importance of unified efforts in shaping a medical education program responsive to community needs. Participants were acknowledged by Dr. Keith Andrew A. Sanchez, faculty of the College of Medicine. Dr. Alilaine B. Cuanan-Cubero presented key updates, achievements, and plans for the College of Medicine. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe discussion followed, with inputs from different participating stakeholders. Dr.  Amhihan commended NEMSU for its visionary leadership in establishing a College of Medicine and emphasized the Commission’s full support. The conversation highlighted the need for collaborative efforts to ensure that NEMSU\'s medical education program remains relevant and impactful.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn closing, Dr. Jennifer M. Montero, OIC to the VP-Academic Affairs, expressed gratitude to the participants and reiterated the university\'s commitment to fostering strong partnerships for the College of Medicine\'s success.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe meeting marked a significant step toward building stronger alliances that will help shape a dynamic and inclusive medical education program, benefiting both the university and the community it serves.\r\n', '𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫’𝐬-𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐟𝐨𝐫-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-01-28 09:28:22', '2025-01-28 09:28:22', '2025-01-28 09:28:22'),
('a5d8b5f4-52f1-11ef-8071-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐌𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐬 𝐇𝐢𝐬𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐲 𝐢𝐧 𝐓𝐫𝐢𝐩𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐞 𝐌𝐎𝐀 𝐒𝐢𝐠𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡 𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐈𝐈𝐓 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐆𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐭 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲', 'MOA-Signing-with-MSUIIT-and-Ghent-University', 'Cagwait, Surigao del Sur - August 5, 2024, North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) through Lianga Campus has reached a significant milestone in its internationalization journey with the signing of a tripartite Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) with Mindanao State University Iligan Institute of Technology (MSU-IIT) and Ghent University.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nCagwait, Surigao del Sur - August 5, 2024, North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) through Lianga Campus has reached a significant milestone in its internationalization journey with the signing of a tripartite Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) with Mindanao State University Iligan Institute of Technology (MSU-IIT) and Ghent University.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn his speech, NEMSU President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon expressed his enthusiasm about this historic partnership, highlighting the shared vision of ALPAS—academic leverage for progressive and aboveboard service. This collaboration aims to foster innovative research and contribute meaningfully to sustainable development.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Loayon emphasized that the MOA represents hope and progress, symbolizing the collective efforts of three distinguished universities coming together to push the boundaries of knowledge and make a difference in their communities. He noted that the synergy between NEMSU, MSU-IIT, and Ghent University promises to bring groundbreaking research, meaningful exchanges, and a deeper understanding of global challenges and opportunities.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\"Our partnership with MSU-IIT and Ghent University is built on mutual respect, shared goals, and a commitment to excellence,\" Dr. Loayon said. \"By pooling our resources, expertise, and passion, we are poised to make significant contributions to these fields and address some of the most pressing issues of our time.\"\r\nThe President extended his deepest gratitude to Prof. Bart Braeckman, from Ghent University, for his support and enthusiasm for this partnership, and he looks forward to many fruitful collaborations ahead.\r\n<br><br>\r\nToday\'s MOA signing is a celebration of partnership, innovation, and the limitless potential that comes from working together. This marks a new chapter of discovery, growth, and positive impact for NEMSU, MSU-IIT, and Ghent University.\r\n\r\n<br><br>\r\nMabuhay ug padayon sa pag-ALPAS NEMSU!\r\n<br/>', 'moa-signing-msuiit.jpg', 'NEMSU Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-08-05 14:11:56', '2024-08-05 14:11:56', '2024-08-05 14:11:56'),
('a669462a-2b17-11ef-8173-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐋𝐞𝐚𝐝𝐬 𝐈𝐧-𝐃𝐞𝐩𝐭𝐡 𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐫𝐢𝐜𝐮𝐥𝐮𝐦 𝐄𝐧𝐡𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐌𝐚𝐩𝐩𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐅𝐨𝐫 𝐆𝐫𝐚𝐝𝐮𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐠𝐫𝐚𝐦𝐬', 'gs-curriculum-review-2024', 'The NEMSU Graduate School faculty joined forces for the 2-day Curriculum Review, Revision and Mapping of the program offerings on June 13-14, 2024 at Gold Bar Grill & Restaurant in Tandag City. Participants included Graduate School faculty, key university officials, and the University President. ', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe NEMSU Graduate School faculty joined forces for the 2-day Curriculum Review, Revision and Mapping of the program offerings on June 13-14, 2024 at Gold Bar Grill & Restaurant in Tandag City. Participants included Graduate School faculty, key university officials, and the University President. \r\n<br><br>\r\nThe first day featured resource speakers Dr. Aldrin A. Darilag, Commissioner and Chairperson of the Board of Regents, and Dr. Alma Sy-Patron, OIC Regional Director of Caraga Commission on Higher Education. Their insightful discussions focused on aligning the Philippine Qualifications Framework (PQF) with graduate school frameworks and aligning institutional program course outcomes with curriculum mapping, respectively.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn the afternoon, experts from various disciplines assessed the current curriculum, ensuring its alignment with the evolving demands of higher education. Their evaluations aimed to ensure that NEMSU’s programs remain relevant and responsive to both local and global educational needs.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe second day commenced with Dr. Sy-Patron\'s insightful session on enhancing Graduate School syllabi. She stressed adherence to the CMO 15 series of 2019, which outlines the policies, standards, and guidelines for graduate school programs. Following her presentation, faculty members from various disciplines engaged in a syllabi workshop, collaborating to refine and improve their course outlines.\r\nThis initiative of the Graduate School addressed the ever-evolving, demanding continuous review and revision of curricula to meet the dynamic needs of both students and the global workforce.\r\n</p>\r\n', 'gs-curr-2024.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-06-15 12:02:56', '2024-06-15 12:02:56', '2024-06-15 12:02:56'),
('a7879a1f-91e0-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', 'House Panel to Tackle Bill on Establishing College of Medicine in NEMSU', 'House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill', 'The House of Representatives’ Committee on Higher and Technical Education (CHTE) is currently holding its Organizational and First Regular Committee Meeting at the Speaker Belmonte Hall, South Wing Annex, Batasang Pambansa Complex.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill 1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill 2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill 3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill 4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nQuezon City — September 1, 2025\r\nThe House of Representatives’ Committee on Higher and Technical Education (CHTE) is currently holding its Organizational and First Regular Committee Meeting at the Speaker Belmonte Hall, South Wing Annex, Batasang Pambansa Complex.\r\n<br/>\r\nAmong the measures in today’s agenda is House Bill No. 2888, which seeks the establishment of a College of Medicine at the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU). The bill is principally authored by Surigao del Sur First District Representative Romeo S. Momo Sr.\r\n<br/>\r\nNEMSU officials VPAA Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo and Executive Assistant Mick Mars Silvano, led by University President Dr. Nemesio Loayon, are in attendance to express their support and readiness to provide inputs on the proposed measure. The university has conveyed its deep gratitude to the CHTE, chaired by Hon. Jude Acidre, for including HB 2888 in the committee discussions, recognizing it as a significant step toward advancing accessible medical education in Caraga and beyond.\r\n<br/>\r\nIf passed into law, the measure will pave the way for the training of future doctors in Mindanao, helping to address the shortage of medical professionals in underserved areas and strengthening the delivery of health services in the region.\r\n<br/>', 'House-Panel-to-Tackle-Bill.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-09-01 10:58:42', NULL, NULL),
('a80950e9-3cd7-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'In preparation for the upcoming academic year, the NEMSU- College of Law', 'Law-2023', 'In preparation for the upcoming academic year, the NEMSU- College of Law together with NEMSU Key Officials held its first Faculty Meeting', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/law-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/law-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/law-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn preparation for the upcoming academic year, the NEMSU- College of Law together with NEMSU Key Officials held its first Faculty Meeting and Lunch Fellowship earlier today, August 17, 2023 at Moot Court, College of Law, NEMSU, Tandag City. <br><br> \r\nDiscussed in the meeting, among others, were:<br>\r\n1. Faculty Orientation and Introduction of New Faculty Members;<br>\r\n2. Bar Review Strategy for the upcoming 2024 Bar Examination; and<br>\r\n3. Renewal and Signing of Contract.\r\n<br/>\r\n', 'law-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-17 18:30:53', '2023-08-17 18:30:53', '2023-08-17 18:30:53'),
('a8593d0b-2084-4561-af19-0f89778ee263', 'Message of Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon to the Harmonization of Academic Unit Manuals', 'message-of-pres-nemesio-g-loayon-to-the-harmonization-of-academic-unit-manuals', '<p>Greetings.<br />\r\nIsaac Newton once said, &ldquo;If I have seen farther than others, it is because I was standing on the shoulder of giants.&rdquo;</p>', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/1%20(3).png\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2%20(3).png\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/3%20(2).png\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Greetings.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Isaac Newton once said, &ldquo;If I have seen farther than others, it is because I was standing on the shoulder of giants.&rdquo;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Today, we come to harmonize our Academic Unit Manuals. This means that as a University with 7 campuses, and considered the largest in Caraga, we work on areas which are complementary in order to have plans working together for the achievement of an overall strategic objective.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">This harmonization will surely help all academic units of the University share the same vision, work together, and optimize the use of resources.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Today, you, participants, are the giants whom the University stands on. For NEMSU to see farther, you form part of its vision that is geared to international standards.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">My administration&rsquo;s 8-point Agenda include knowledge-sharing and skills-driven internationalization program, where we are bound to produce globally competitive graduates with a specific action for an international curriculum and quality assurance for globally competitive education, as well as identifying international mobility of student and faculty mobility and knowledge-based economy. To make this happen, we need to establish strong linkages and networking industries locally and internationally.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Speaking of strong linkages, yesterday, we have presented our 2024 Proposed Budget during the RDC-SDC 1st Quarter Meeting held at the NEDA Caraga Conference Hall. With yesterday&rsquo;s presentation, we were able to invite the interest of Gawad Kalinga to be a partner in the journey to a future full of hope.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">With this activity today, let us not only harmonize our academic unit manuals, but may we also live in harmony with one another.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The President is one with you in sustaining our culture of excellence through our constant compliance to international standards.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">Hence, allow me to thank the initiatives of the Office of the Vice President for Academic Affairs Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo with the Director for Curriculum Development Dr. Erwin B. Berry, and all of you for pouring out valuable efforts for NEMSU to be great always.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">A pleasant morning ladies and gentlemen.</span><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '5 (2).png', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-03-08 10:46:58', '2023-03-10 03:03:22', '2023-03-10 03:03:22'),
('a8adec56-3cc0-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Lianga Campus - Class Opening for A.Y. 2023-2024', 'Class-Lianga-2023', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University-Lianga Campus opened its doors for the academic year 2023-2024 with the new edition of \"Jumpstart\" to welcome the new and old students and new faculty and staff, initiated by the Office of Student Welfare and Development (OSWD)', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Lianga-open-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗟𝗖 𝘄𝗲𝗹𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗲𝘀 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗻𝗲𝘄 𝗮𝗰𝗮𝗱𝗲𝗺𝗶𝗰 𝘆𝗲𝗮𝗿, 𝗼𝗹𝗱 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗻𝗲𝘄 𝘀𝘁𝘂𝗱𝘀 𝗷𝗼𝗶𝗻 𝗝𝘂𝗺𝗽𝘀𝘁𝗮𝗿𝘁 <br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University-Lianga Campus opened its doors for the academic year 2023-2024 with the new edition of \"Jumpstart\" to welcome the new and old students and new faculty and staff, initiated by the Office of Student Welfare and Development (OSWD) and University Student Government (USG), at the NEMSU-Lianga Quadrangle on August 16, 2023.<br><br>\r\nIn line with this event, a short program was administered in order to give students further instructions and information with regard to the release of certificates of records (COR) and the schedule of classes.<br><br>\r\nThe activity also highlighted the introduction of the faculty, administrative staff, and USG officers to give new students a chance to meet their instructors and leaders of the institution.<br><br>\r\nThe campus director, Dr. Cynthia P. Sajot, extended her welcome message to both new and old students. In her statement, she emphasized that she was delighted to know that the population of the university was increasing.<br><br>\r\nAlso in attendance is the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences (CAS), Dr. Romeo Patan, who carried out a message to the students of NEMSU.<br><br>\r\nMoreover, the students are advised to get their CORs in the designated areas of the different colleges.<br><br>\r\nAfter the program, the unity dance followed, and the students visited various organization booths, including the sports club and the student publication.\r\nReport by Noe M. Quezada<br><br>\r\nPhotos by Lizafern Mae Castillo, Lee Van Cleff M. Labsan & Manuel Allada <br><br>\r\n#TheSeaStrivers <br>\r\n#SailingAndStrivingForTheTruth <br>\r\n#NEMSULiangaCampus\r\n<br/>\r\n', 'Lianga-open-00.jpg', 'The Sea Strivers Publication', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-16 19:45:52', '2023-08-16 19:45:52', '2023-08-16 19:45:52'),
('a9967969-2202-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU LIANGA BOOK DISPLAY 2022', 'NEMSU-LIANGA-BOOK', '<p>The book selection and acquisition process are the responsibility and collaboration efforts of the Librarian, Faculty members, students, and other stakeholders to support the information needed for instruction.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>The book selection and acquisition process are the responsibility and collaboration efforts of the Librarian, Faculty members, students, and other stakeholders to support the information needed for instruction. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nSince we still have restrictions on every transaction, book companies are trying to connect with us Librarians for easy and convenient transactions. With the support and approval of the Campus Director, Dr. Cynthia P. Sajot, the Assistant Campus Director, Dr. Bernardita G. Quevedo and Administrative Officer IV, Mr. Aniceto C. Sanchez, Jr., there were three (3) book providers who were willing to display their materials for an easy book selection namely: CD Books International, Inc., Serv Enterprises and New Century Books, unfortunately, only the CD Books had a chance to display their materials because of unplanned circumstances on March 21, 2022.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/bdisplay02.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'bdisplay01.jpg', 'Jehoney V. Alboroto, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-21 08:09:53', '2022-03-21 08:09:53', '2022-03-21 08:09:53'),
('aaaff5ac-127d-11ef-b18a-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐇𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐞𝐫 𝐄𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝐒𝐮𝐦𝐦𝐢𝐭 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟒!', 'ched-summit-2024', 'The National Higher Education Day Summit 2024 is currently in session at the PICC Reception Hall in Pasay City. Commenced at 9:00 AM today, this summit commemorates the 30th anniversary of the Commission on Higher Education (CHED), as established by Republic Act No. 7722, the \"Higher Education Act of 1994.\"', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe National Higher Education Day Summit 2024 is currently in session at the PICC Reception Hall in Pasay City. Commenced at 9:00 AM today, this summit commemorates the 30th anniversary of the Commission on Higher Education (CHED), as established by Republic Act No. 7722, the \"Higher Education Act of 1994.\"<br><br>\r\nNEMSU Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon, alongside CHED Commissioners and fellow SUC Presidents, reflects with pride and honor on their roles within the country\'s higher education landscape.\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n#nheds2024 #CHEDAnniversary\r\n<br/>', 'ched-summit-2024.jpg', 'NEMSU Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon ', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-05-15 13:00:20', '2024-05-15 13:00:20', '2024-05-15 13:00:20'),
('aaef6897-f41a-11ef-b8b6-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬 𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐢𝐧 𝐃𝐢𝐫𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧-𝐒𝐞𝐭𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐒𝐞𝐬𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐏𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐧𝐭', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧', 'North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) concluded a successful Direction-Setting Session on February 25, 2025, at its Cantilan Campus, spearheaded by University President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon. This event was attended by selected faculty and staff who were set to receive their office orders for their designated and re-designated positions.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nNorth Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) concluded a successful Direction-Setting Session on February 25, 2025, at its Cantilan Campus, spearheaded by University President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon. This event was attended by selected faculty and staff who were set to receive their office orders for their designated and re-designated positions.\r\n\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nDr. Mick Mars P. Silvano formally opened the session by presenting the rationale of the event, emphasizing the importance of direction setting in ensuring alignment with the institution’s Vision, Mission, Core Values, and INNOVATE Agenda. He elaborated on the key objectives of the session, highlighting its role in fostering collaboration and operational efficiency. He also underscored Leadership and Governance in the University as outlined in CMO 7, s. 2022, focusing on Academic Leadership, Institutional Leadership, and Leadership in Resource Mobilization.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nDuring the session, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon delivered a compelling message centered on NEMSU’s Mission, Vision, Core Values, and the 8-Point Strategic Directional Agenda. He emphasized the university’s role as a Research University, requiring faculty to uphold the Four-Fold Functions of instruction, research, extension, and production. He encouraged all teaching staff to integrate research into their teaching methodologies and to embrace an aggressive approach to innovation.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe session also featured a presentation by Engr. Kenny Montenegro, Planning Officer III, who outlined the Office Performance Commitment Review (OPCR) Targets and SUC Levelling Targets for Instruction, Research, Extension, Production, and Governance. His presentation provided crucial insights into the university’s roadmap for achieving excellence in these areas.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nDr. Juancho A. Intano, Campus Director of NEMSU Cantilan, expressed his unwavering commitment to the university’s vision. He extended his profound gratitude to Dr. Loayon for his continued support and technical assistance, as well as to all faculty and staff who participated in the session.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe Direction-Setting Session served as a significant platform for reinforcing NEMSU’s institutional goals, ensuring that leadership and faculty remain aligned with the university’s strategic vision. With a renewed sense of purpose, the attendees left the session equipped with the necessary guidance to fulfill their roles in advancing NEMSU’s mission of academic and research excellence. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe event concluded with the distribution of designation orders to the attendees, solidifying their new roles and responsibilities within the university.\r\n', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬-𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐭𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥-𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧.jpg\r\n', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-26 08:15:36', '2025-02-26 16:15:35', NULL),
('ac973f8b-86e5-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', 'North Eastern Mindanao State University proudly participated in the 1st International Cultural Exchange (ICE) Program', 'NEMSU-1st-International-Cultural Exchange-(ICE)-Program', 'North Eastern Mindanao State University proudly participated in the 1st International Cultural Exchange (ICE) Program virtually conducted by Polyteknik Piksi Ganesha, Indonesia on July 24, 2025 via Zoom. The event was spearheaded by the Office of International Affairs in coordination with the Office of Culture, Arts, and Sports of NEMSU. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/nemsu-ice-2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/nemsu-ice-3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/nemsu-ice-4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/nemsu-ice-5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nNorth Eastern Mindanao State University proudly participated in the 1st International Cultural Exchange (ICE) Program virtually conducted by Polyteknik Piksi Ganesha, Indonesia on July 24, 2025 via Zoom. The event was spearheaded by the Office of International Affairs in coordination with the Office of Culture, Arts, and Sports of NEMSU. \r\n<br/>\r\nThe faculty and students of the Department of Languages of the College of Arts and Sciences, PATHFIT, the College of Teacher Education, and the ELT program of the Graduate School successfully represented NEMSU in the international virtual platform.\r\n<br/>\r\nThe 1st ICE Program with its theme Culture Connect!, participated by different international universities of the ASEAN region including NEMSU, was driven to enhance knowledge and open cultural cooperation networks between participating international partners through the showcase of different cultural performances. \r\n<br/>\r\nThe cultural performances highlighted the different music and dances that mirrored the culture and traditions of the participating institutions. The active and meaningful involvement of the faculty and students coupled with the proactive support of the University administration, the North Eastern Mindanao State University was able to recreate the cultural performances of the Itik-itik (Duck) and the Karatong dances, which garnered distinctions:\r\n<br/>\r\n𝟭𝘀𝘁 𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗖𝗼𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗯𝗼𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗧𝗲𝗮𝗺𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝗶𝗻 𝗠𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗰 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 - 𝗞𝗮𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗼𝗻𝗴 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 \r\n𝟮𝗻𝗱 𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗡𝗮𝗿𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 (𝗜𝘁𝗶𝗸-𝗜𝘁𝗶𝗸 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲) \r\n𝟮𝗻𝗱 𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗖𝗼𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗯𝗼𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗧𝗲𝗮𝗺𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝗶𝗻 𝗔𝗿𝘁𝘀 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗠𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 - 𝗞𝗮𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗼𝗻𝗴 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 \r\n𝟯𝗿𝗱 𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗱𝘂𝗰𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 - 𝗜𝘁𝗶𝗸-𝗜𝘁𝗶𝗸 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 \r\n𝟯𝗿𝗱 𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗡𝗮𝗿𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 - 𝗞𝗮𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗼𝗻𝗴 𝗗𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲\r\nThis accomplishment reflects the University’s ongoing commitment to academic and cultural excellence on the global stage, highlighting the talent pipeline if NEMSU’s faculty and students. The recognition received at the ICE Program serves as both a milestone and a motivation to further engage in meaningful international collaborations.\r\n---\r\n𝘌𝘷𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘋𝘪𝘳𝘦𝘤𝘵𝘰𝘳: 𝘋𝘳. 𝘚𝘩𝘺𝘭𝘢 𝘖. 𝘔𝘰𝘳𝘦𝘯𝘰 \r\n𝘚𝘤𝘳𝘪𝘱𝘵 𝘞𝘳𝘪𝘵𝘦𝘳𝘴 & 𝘕𝘢𝘳𝘳𝘢𝘵𝘰𝘳𝘴:\r\n𝘌𝘭𝘺𝘴𝘴𝘢 𝘒𝘢𝘺 𝘝. 𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘵𝘪𝘯𝘦𝘻 , 𝘌𝘳𝘸𝘪𝘯 𝘙. 𝘉𝘶𝘤𝘫𝘢𝘯 \r\n𝘙𝘰𝘴𝘢𝘭𝘺𝘯 𝘊. 𝘋𝘢𝘺𝘢𝘰 , 𝘈𝘭𝘮𝘢 𝘈. 𝘊𝘰𝘳𝘯𝘦𝘭𝘪𝘰 \r\n𝘛𝘳𝘦𝘹𝘪𝘦 𝘖. 𝘈𝘭𝘢𝘸𝘪 , 𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘥𝘪𝘦 𝘌. 𝘉𝘶𝘤𝘫𝘢𝘯 \r\n𝘑𝘦𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘯𝘦 𝘛. 𝘚𝘶𝘳𝘪𝘭𝘭𝘢 , 𝘓𝘰𝘷𝘦𝘭𝘺 𝘑𝘦𝘯 𝘚. 𝘛𝘢𝘭𝘪𝘬𝘪𝘨 \r\n𝘚𝘵𝘦𝘷𝘦𝘯 𝘊𝘢𝘳𝘭 𝘔. 𝘚𝘪𝘭𝘢𝘨𝘢𝘯 \r\n𝘍𝘢𝘤𝘶𝘭𝘵𝘺 𝘋𝘢𝘯𝘤𝘦 𝘗𝘦𝘳𝘧𝘰𝘳𝘮𝘦𝘳𝘴:\r\n𝘑𝘰𝘩𝘯 𝘙𝘦𝘪𝘭 𝘓. 𝘉𝘦𝘯𝘥𝘰𝘺 \r\n𝘋𝘢𝘷𝘦 𝘉𝘰𝘩𝘰𝘭 \r\n𝘊𝘩𝘢𝘳𝘭𝘰𝘶 𝘗. 𝘔𝘢𝘯𝘭𝘢, 𝘕𝘦𝘭𝘪𝘵𝘰 𝘌. 𝘎𝘢𝘭𝘭𝘦𝘨𝘰 \r\n𝘊𝘢𝘳𝘭 𝘗𝘢𝘵𝘳𝘪𝘤𝘬 𝘊. 𝘓𝘢𝘮𝘣𝘢𝘤𝘰 , 𝘎𝘳𝘢𝘤𝘦 𝘈𝘯𝘯 𝘗. 𝘓𝘶𝘮𝘢𝘬𝘪𝘯 \r\n𝘑𝘰𝘷𝘪𝘦 𝘈𝘯𝘯 𝘑𝘶𝘢𝘳𝘦𝘻 , 𝘚𝘩𝘦𝘪𝘭𝘢 𝘔𝘢𝘦 𝘙𝘪𝘷𝘢𝘴 \r\n𝘙𝘰𝘴𝘢𝘯𝘯𝘦 𝘜. 𝘋𝘪𝘢𝘥𝘶𝘭𝘢 , 𝘊𝘩𝘳𝘪𝘴𝘵𝘪𝘯𝘦 𝘗. 𝘔𝘰𝘯𝘵𝘦𝘯𝘦𝘨𝘳𝘰 \r\n𝘋𝘢𝘯𝘪𝘦𝘷𝘦 𝘜. 𝘎𝘢𝘳𝘤𝘪𝘢 , 𝘙𝘺𝘢𝘯 𝘏𝘦𝘯𝘳𝘺 𝘛. 𝘓𝘢𝘨𝘶𝘳𝘢 \r\n𝘒𝘩𝘪𝘮 𝘎𝘦𝘵𝘩𝘦𝘳 𝘛. 𝘉𝘶𝘵𝘳𝘰𝘯 , 𝘊𝘢𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘳 𝘝. 𝘉𝘢𝘭𝘢𝘤𝘶𝘪𝘵, 𝘑𝘳. 𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘪𝘢 𝘓𝘢𝘢𝘳𝘯𝘪 𝘖. 𝘑𝘶𝘦𝘨𝘰, 𝘈𝘯𝘨𝘦𝘭 𝘈𝘯𝘯 𝘈. 𝘓𝘢𝘨𝘶𝘳𝘢 \r\n𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘺 𝘈𝘯𝘯 𝘚. 𝘖𝘭𝘢𝘤𝘰 , 𝘊𝘭𝘢𝘳𝘪𝘴𝘴𝘦 𝘚. 𝘓𝘰𝘢𝘺𝘰𝘯 \r\n𝘑𝘰𝘯𝘢 𝘓. 𝘙𝘢𝘮𝘣𝘰𝘺𝘰𝘯\r\n𝘚𝘵𝘶𝘥𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘗𝘦𝘳𝘧𝘰𝘳𝘮𝘦𝘳𝘴:\r\n𝘎𝘩𝘦𝘯𝘦 𝘙𝘰𝘴𝘦 𝘊. 𝘚𝘰 , 𝘕𝘩𝘰𝘺𝘭𝘦𝘯 𝘖. 𝘊𝘰𝘮𝘪𝘭𝘪𝘯𝘨 𝘑𝘦𝘯𝘯𝘦𝘭𝘺𝘯 𝘘𝘶𝘪𝘻𝘢𝘥𝘢 , 𝘒𝘦𝘻𝘪𝘢𝘩 𝘍𝘢𝘪𝘵𝘩 𝘗. 𝘎𝘢𝘳𝘥𝘪𝘨𝘰 𝘎𝘩𝘦𝘯𝘦 𝘔𝘢𝘦 𝘊. 𝘚𝘰, 𝘑𝘢𝘥𝘦 𝘉. 𝘝𝘪𝘭𝘭𝘢𝘳𝘪𝘯 , 𝘊𝘨𝘪𝘦 𝘈𝘯𝘨𝘦𝘭𝘰 𝘔. 𝘊𝘢𝘴𝘪𝘰, 𝘎𝘳𝘦𝘨 𝘔𝘪𝘤𝘩𝘢𝘦𝘭 𝘚. 𝘉𝘢𝘨𝘶𝘪𝘰,  𝘑𝘳 𝘌. 𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘵𝘪𝘯𝘦𝘻 𝘑𝘰𝘩𝘯, 𝘔𝘢𝘳𝘬 𝘓. 𝘝𝘦𝘳𝘴𝘰𝘻𝘢\r\n𝘝𝘪𝘥𝘦𝘰𝘨𝘳𝘢𝘱𝘩𝘦𝘳𝘴 :\r\n𝘙𝘰𝘨𝘪𝘭 𝘑𝘰𝘯𝘦 𝘐𝘐 𝘌. 𝘊𝘢𝘯𝘦𝘵𝘦, 𝘈𝘳𝘪𝘦𝘭 𝘑𝘶𝘯𝘦 𝘓. 𝘙𝘢𝘤𝘩𝘰, 𝘌𝘳𝘸𝘪𝘯 𝘊𝘢𝘭𝘮𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘯\r\n\r\n', 'nemsu-ice.jpg', 'Dr. Elyssa Kay V. Martinez', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-07-24 11:28:45', NULL, NULL),
('ada3a080-0044-11ef-904a-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐓𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐬 𝐏𝐡𝐚𝐬𝐞 𝟐 𝐓𝐨𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐝𝐬 𝐄𝐬𝐭𝐚𝐛𝐥𝐢𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐠𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐌𝐞𝐝𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐧𝐞', 'College-of-Medicine-Phase2', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) conducted Phase 2: Advancing NEMSU\'s College of Medicine Program through Strategic Collaboration from April 18-20, 2024, at O\'s Landing Beach Resort in San Agustin, Surigao del Sur.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/college-Medicine-P2/comp2-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) conducted Phase 2: Advancing NEMSU\'s College of Medicine Program through Strategic Collaboration from April 18-20, 2024, at O\'s Landing Beach Resort in San Agustin, Surigao del Sur.\r\n<br><br>\r\nAttending the event were Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the University President III, Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, the Vice President for Academic Affairs, Dr. Rolly G. Salvaleon, Vice President for Extension and Research, Dr. Abundio C. Miralles, Vice President for Administration and Finance, members of the revision and enhancement committee, the academic committee, and expert consultants such as Dr. Michael Leocadio and Dr. Ma. Cecilia C. Cruiz. The presence of a distinguished guest, Atty. Malaya M. Capulong, MD, who is both a doctor and a lawyer, added valuable perspectives to the event. Meanwhile, the two other consultants, namely, Dr. Horacio Saguil, Jr., and Dr. Milabel Ho, contributed remotely via Zoom, ensuring a comprehensive exchange of ideas.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe primary objective of this gathering was to finalize the necessary documentation and paperwork required for submission to the Commission on Higher Education (CHED). The event also included an insightful discussion led by Dr. Leocadio on the topic of Mindfulness, aimed at equipping participants with essential mindfulness techniques.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThis significant milestone underscores the tangible progress made towards realizing the vision of establishing the College of Medicine at NEMSU. It reflects the efforts and dedication of all involved parties towards this noble endeavor.\r\n<br/>', 'comp2-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-04-20 12:04:21', '2024-04-20 12:04:21', '2024-04-20 12:04:21'),
('adfc6c32-db7d-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐀𝐬𝐬𝐮𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐚𝐭 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐞𝐟𝐫𝐨𝐧𝐭: 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐏𝐫𝐞𝐩𝐚𝐫𝐞𝐬 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐈𝐒𝐎 𝟗𝟎𝟎𝟏:𝟐𝟎𝟏𝟓 𝟐𝐧𝐝 𝐒𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐢𝐥𝐥𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐕𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐭', 'Manual-Review-2024', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) recently took a significant step forward in its commitment to excellence and quality assurance by convening a Management Review as part of its ISO proceedings on March 5, 2024, at the NEMSU Old Board Room. Presided over by Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President III, the meeting brought together key officials and leaders of the university. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-review-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-review-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-review-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) recently took a significant step forward in its commitment to excellence and quality assurance by convening a Management Review as part of its ISO proceedings on March 5, 2024, at the NEMSU Old Board Room. Presided over by Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President III, the meeting brought together key officials and leaders of the university. \r\n<br><br>\r\nAmong the attendees were Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, Vice President for Academic Affairs, Dr. Rolly G. Salvaleon, Vice President for Research and Extension, campus directors from various NEMSU campuses, directors, college deans, and other unit heads representing the seven (7) NEMSU campuses.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThroughout the meeting, the participants engaged in fruitful discussions, delving into crucial topics important to NEMSU\'s continuous improvement journey. They meticulously reviewed the findings and results stemming from the ISO 9001:2015 Comprehensive Internal Audit, emphasizing the importance of adherence to standards and the availability of requisite documentation as evidence of process adherence.\r\n<br><br> \r\nThe proceedings also underscored the paramount importance of assessing the extent of conformity of each unit, college, and campus to ISO 9001:2015 standards. This thorough examination serves as a basis for identifying areas of improvement and intervention, essential for maintaining the university\'s commitment to enhancing efficiency, elevating standards, and refining the very core of operations.\r\n<br><br>\r\nAs the proceedings drew to a close, it was unanimously ascertained that the seven NEMSU campuses, alongside the university as a whole, will prepare for the upcoming ISO 9001:2015 2nd Surveillance Audit this May.\r\n<br/>', 'manual-review-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-06 10:40:59', '2024-03-06 10:40:59', '2024-03-06 10:40:59'),
('af23b654-37e0-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Strategic planning Management and Executive Committee Meeting. ', 'Managment-Executive', 'Productive discussions and strategic planning at yesterday\'s Management and Executive Committee Meeting.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mancom-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mancom-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mancom-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nProductive discussions and strategic planning at yesterday\'s Management and Executive Committee Meeting. Working together to shape a brighter future.\r\n<br/>\r\n#Teamwork <br>\r\n#StrategicPlanning <br>\r\n#MovingForwardTogerther\r\n', 'mancom-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-08 20:23:50', '2023-08-08 20:23:50', '2023-08-08 20:23:50'),
('b1434cd5-f419-11ef-b8b6-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐎𝐛𝐬𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐬 𝐑𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐭𝐞 𝐋𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝐢𝐧 𝐂𝐨𝐦𝐦𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐨𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐄𝐃𝐒𝐀 𝐏𝐞𝐨𝐩𝐥𝐞 𝐏𝐨𝐰𝐞𝐫 𝐑𝐞𝐯𝐨𝐥𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐎𝐛𝐬𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐬-𝐑𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐭𝐞-𝐋𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠', 'In honor of the EDSA People Power Revolution Anniversary, February 25, 2025, will be observed as a Remote Learning Day across all NEMSU campuses.', '\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn honor of the EDSA People Power Revolution Anniversary, February 25, 2025, will be observed as a Remote Learning Day across all NEMSU campuses.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThis historic day serves as a reminder of the bravery and unity that restored democracy in the Philippines. As we commemorate this occasion, all faculty, staff, and students are encouraged to take part in meaningful activities that uphold the values of freedom, civic responsibility, and national unity.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAs a university committed to democratic values, human rights, and civic engagement, NEMSU stands in solidarity with the ideals of the EDSA People Power Revolution. May this day inspire us to continue fostering a community that values justice, equality, and the power of collective action.\r\n', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐎𝐛𝐬𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐞𝐬-𝐑𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐭𝐞-𝐋𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠.jpg\r\n', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-23 16:11:22', NULL, NULL),
('b1686375-4619-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', '🏆 Recognizing Excellence 🎓 | DOST team\'s visit to North Eastern Mindanao State University', 'DOST-2023', 'where they expressed their heartfelt appreciation for NEMSU\'s pivotal role as a testing center for this Sunday\'s examination. ', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nwhere they expressed their heartfelt appreciation for NEMSU\'s pivotal role as a testing center for this Sunday\'s examination. Collaborations like these drive innovation and ensure a seamless testing experience for all participants. <br>\r\n#DOSTAppreciation <br>\r\n#TestingExcellence\r\n<br>', 'dost-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 17, 'news', 1, '2023-08-25 11:40:11', '2023-08-25 11:40:11', '2023-08-25 11:40:11');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('b4697330-ea64-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐥𝐞𝐚𝐝𝐬 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐚𝐛𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐞 𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐤𝐞𝐡𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐞𝐫 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐬𝐮𝐥𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐭𝐨 𝐀𝐝𝐯𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐜 𝐃𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐥𝐨𝐩𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭', 'NLCSC-Advance-Strategic-Development-2024', 'In a visionary move towards advancing the strategic development, the NEMSU initiated the consultative dialogue with the stakeholders for the strategic development on March 22, 2024 at NEMSU Conference Room. The dialogue, aimed at soliciting different perspectives, provides an avenue in NEMSU’s commitment to academic excellence and innovations.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/ICSCA-Strategic-Development/consultative-dialogue-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a visionary move towards advancing the strategic development, the NEMSU initiated the consultative dialogue with the stakeholders for the strategic development on March 22, 2024 at NEMSU Conference Room. The dialogue, aimed at soliciting different perspectives, provides an avenue in NEMSU’s commitment to academic excellence and innovations.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe consultative dialogue brought together key officials, representatives from faculty, students, staff, industry, and government agencies partners. The diverse composition of participants ensured a comprehensive exchange of ideas and insights vital for shaping the strategic direction of NEMSU.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Abundio C. Miralles, VPAF, highlighted in his opening remarks the importance of stakeholder engagement in driving meaningful change and innovation within the institution. He recognized that the stakeholders are invaluable partners in our journey towards excellence.\r\n<br><br>\r\nMeanwhile, Atty. Michiko Donaire-Maglinte, Legal Officer and OIC of the NEMSU President, extends her gratitude to the presence of the different stakeholders in helping NEMSU materialize its vision in becoming a premier research university.\r\nFurthermore, Dr. Rolly G. Salvaleon, the VPRE, provided framework in the presentation and open forum of the consultative dialogue. He emphasized the vital roles of the stakeholders in achieving the objectives of the activity. \r\n<br><br>\r\nThroughout the dialogue sessions, stakeholders generously provided inputs and suggestions spanning curriculum enrichment, research imperatives, faculty-student support services, and proactive community engagement initiatives. The stakeholders praised NEMSU’s milestone over the years and reaffirmed their commitment to support the university in its quest to excellent.\r\n<br><br>\r\nLooking forward the horizon, Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, the VPAA, remains resolutely committed to leveraging the insights gleaned from the consultative dialogue to inform its strategic roadmap. Dr. Suazo reiterated the institution unwavering dedication to participatory decision-making.\r\n<br><br>\r\nNEMSU\'s consultative discussion is a proactive step in its goal of building an active, innovative, and excellence-oriented culture within the university. With the utilization of the combined expertise and experience of its stakeholders, NEMSU is in a strong position to steer a clear and active path toward achieving its targets and leaving its mark on the area of education management.\r\n<br/>', 'consultative-dialogue-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-23 08:15:39', '2024-03-23 08:15:39', '2024-03-23 08:15:39'),
('b4bafbe7-8a5e-11ee-8f14-a233a240566f', 'The Main Campus Retooling the Participative Bottom-up Budget Planning Strategy, PPMP Writeshop and Post Evaluation participated by the Fund Managers', 'budget-call-2023', 'The Main Campus Retooling the Participative Bottom-up Budget Planning Strategy, PPMP Writeshop and Post Evaluation participated by the Fund Managers, Student Leaders and Stakeholders in a Two Day Activity at Rock Island Resort, Baranggay Cambatong Hinatuan,SDS.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-13.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-14.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-15.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-16.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-17.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/budget-call-18.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>', 'budget-call-00.jpg', 'Office of the Campus Director - Tandag', 0, 'news', 1, '2023-11-23 13:50:11', '2023-11-23 13:50:11', '2023-11-23 13:50:11'),
('b4c19d0e-4616-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU holds ACO-ADCO meeting', 'aco-adco-2023', 'Representatives from different NEMSU campuses gathered at NEMSU-Main\'s Prospero B. Pichay Sr. Gymnasium on August 23 for the joint meeting of the Academic and Administrative Councils (ACO-ADCO) focused on discussing important university matters.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aco-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aco-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/aco-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nRepresentatives from different NEMSU campuses gathered at NEMSU-Main\'s Prospero B. Pichay Sr. Gymnasium on August 23 for the joint meeting of the Academic and Administrative Councils (ACO-ADCO) focused on discussing important university matters.<br><br>\r\nUniversity President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, took the podium to provide key updates regarding university affairs. Central to his address was the impact of trust, confidence, and reputation on NEMSU\'s standing within the community. Notably, this influence led to a substantial rise in enrollment across campuses. Figures climbed from 16,870 in the previous academic year to an impressive 28,930.<br><br>\r\nAddressing the need for evolution, Campus Director Abundio C. Miralles, Ed.D, asserted the necessity of progressiveness in his words of welcome. Miralles emphasized how time and shifting priorities have necessitated adjustments in plans, directions, and mandates. He stressed that the changing needs of both the local community and the nation at large were driving forces behind this demand for reform within the institution.<br><br>\r\n“Subalit sa paglipas ng panahon, marami nang nagbago: ang mga plano, prayoridad, direksyon, at mandato. Ito ay dahilan ng mga nakikita nating pagbabago ng pangangailangan ng ating pamayanan, ng ating bansa at dahilan kung bakit maging ang ating institusyon ay kailangan din ng reporma upang ito ay maging akma sa pangangailangan ng bagong panahon.” Miralles said. <br><br>\r\nAdditionally, Miralles conveyed a strong message to fellow public servants, emphasizing the significance of remaining committed to their goals and underscoring that while administrators may change, their core aspirations should endure.<br><br>\r\nThe joint ACO-ADCO meeting is held quarterly to discuss key issues in the university. <br>\r\n\r\n', 'aco-00.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-24 15:23:07', '2023-08-24 15:23:07', '2023-08-24 15:23:07'),
('b5477339-f413-11ef-b8b6-a233a240566f', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝗘𝘅𝗲𝗰𝘂𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲𝘀 𝗨𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗰𝗼𝗿𝗲 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗙𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗹 𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗶𝗻 𝗨𝘁𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗘𝘅𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀', '𝗙𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗹-𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗶𝗻-𝗨𝘁𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗘𝘅𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀', 'During the fourth  installation of NEMSUlti: Executive Press Conference at NEMSU Cantilan Audio-Visual Center, Dr. Abundio C. Mirralles, Vice President for Administration and Finance (VPAF); Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) and Bids and Awards Committee (BAC) Chairperson for Infrastructure; and Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President, address questions from The Craftsman Publication regarding the implementation of infrastructure and development projects of the university amidst the reported cuts to the 2025 budget allocation for state universities and colleges (SUCs) as reflected in the General Appropriations Act (GAA).', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗙𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗹-𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗶𝗻-𝗨𝘁𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗘𝘅𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/476249555_660636499808772_6994676550594268751_n-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nDuring the fourth  installation of NEMSUlti: Executive Press Conference at NEMSU Cantilan Audio-Visual Center, Dr. Abundio C. Mirralles, Vice President for Administration and Finance (VPAF); Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) and Bids and Awards Committee (BAC) Chairperson for Infrastructure; and Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President, address questions from The Craftsman Publication regarding the implementation of infrastructure and development projects of the university amidst the reported cuts to the 2025 budget allocation for state universities and colleges (SUCs) as reflected in the General Appropriations Act (GAA).\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nDr. Miralles calls on the campuses to help the university in highlighting and identifying issues by empowering the grassroots to engage with the decision-making processes of the campuses. “On the top management, I assure you that is the direction of our university right now it\'s infra, infra, infra,” the VPAF elucidates.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThereafter, Dr. Suazo emphasizes the different strategies for securing funding for the infrastructure projects of the university. “So, there are actually many strategies that we can proceed with. Our infrastructures for the university, we do not only rely on the GAA, we also rely on our savings,” she discusses. Moreover, the VPAA and BAC Chairperson for Infrastructure also commends the campus directors of the different campuses for ‘really strategizing on savings.’ In her statement, she also points out that the infrastructure projects in NEMSU Cantilan Campus come from the accumulated savings as well as the income-generating project (IGP). “Here in Cantilan, many of your buildings and infrastructures are actually coming from your savings appropriation, and apart from that, because you have a very active income-generating project here in Cantilan Campus,” she adds.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAs the open forum continues, Dr. Suazo further explains that other resources for infrastructure funding come from IGP and outsourced funds, particularly through research and development initiatives. She highlights that research projects, as long as they align with infrastructure needs, can also serve as a source of funding.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nDr. Loayon, in his closing remarks, emphasizes the importance of networking and collaboration with Philippine government agencies and non-government organizations (NGOs) to secure additional funding. He expresses confidence in the university’s ability to overcome fiscal challenges, citing the expertise of faculty and the collective effort of the university community. “We welcome opportunities from various government agencies and NGOs to source out funds. Despite the limited fiscal space, we are so confident with the caliber of our key officials, the faculty and your participation in our effort to ensure we can provide the facilities that you need and the quality of education we wanted to deliver to you. Thank you,” PNGL concludes.\r\n', '𝗙𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗹-𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗶𝗻-𝗨𝘁𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗘𝘅𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀.jpg', 'Elton Jose Armendarez', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-07 15:26:08', NULL, NULL),
('b603420d-e4f2-11ef-8bc4-a233a240566f', '𝗙𝗼𝗿𝗴𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗣𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗻𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽𝘀 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗲𝘀𝘀: 𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆 𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹 𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀 𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨', '𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨', 'In a significant event aimed at strengthening collaborations and advancing technical education, the 𝗡𝗼𝗿𝘁𝗵 𝗘𝗮𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗻 𝗠𝗶𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗼 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗲 𝗨𝗻𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘆 (𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨) 𝘄𝗲𝗹𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗲𝗱 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝘃𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁 𝗼𝗳 𝗧𝗲𝗰𝗵𝗻𝗶𝗰𝗮𝗹 𝗘𝗱𝘂𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗦𝗸𝗶𝗹𝗹𝘀 𝗗𝗲𝘃𝗲𝗹𝗼𝗽𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗔𝘂𝘁𝗵𝗼𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆 (𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔) 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆 𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹 𝗙𝗲𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗮𝗿𝗱𝗼 𝗥. 𝗖𝗼𝗹𝗮𝗺𝗯𝗼 𝗼𝗻 𝗝𝗮𝗻𝘂𝗮𝗿𝘆 𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱. The gathering, themed “Forging Partnerships for Progress,” highlighted a shared vision for educational development and innovation.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a significant event aimed at strengthening collaborations and advancing technical education, the 𝗡𝗼𝗿𝘁𝗵 𝗘𝗮𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗻 𝗠𝗶𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗼 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗲 𝗨𝗻𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘆 (𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨) 𝘄𝗲𝗹𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗲𝗱 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝘃𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁 𝗼𝗳 𝗧𝗲𝗰𝗵𝗻𝗶𝗰𝗮𝗹 𝗘𝗱𝘂𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗦𝗸𝗶𝗹𝗹𝘀 𝗗𝗲𝘃𝗲𝗹𝗼𝗽𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗔𝘂𝘁𝗵𝗼𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆 (𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔) 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆 𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹 𝗙𝗲𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗮𝗿𝗱𝗼 𝗥. 𝗖𝗼𝗹𝗮𝗺𝗯𝗼 𝗼𝗻 𝗝𝗮𝗻𝘂𝗮𝗿𝘆 𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱. The gathering, themed “Forging Partnerships for Progress,” highlighted a shared vision for educational development and innovation.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nHeld at the University Boardroom, the program formally started with the introduction of NEMSU officials by Executive Assistant III Dr. Mick Mars P. Silvano, setting the tone for meaningful discussions.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nNEMSU President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon delivered a comprehensive message, highlighting the university’s strategic efforts to support the development of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) programs. He proudly shared the accomplishments of NEMSU San Miguel Campus in this regard, emphasizing its growing reputation as a hub for skills development and livelihood training. Dr. Loayon also reiterated the university’s commitment to aligning its programs with TESDA’s mission to equip learners with industry-relevant competencies and skills.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nVice President for Admin and Finance Dr. Abundio C. Miralles formally introduced Deputy Director General Colombo, who delivered a message centered on collaboration, innovation, and progress. Colombo emphasized TESDA’s commitment to bridging the skills gap and enhancing employability among Filipino learners. He acknowledged NEMSU’s role as a vital partner in driving education reforms in the region.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAn open forum and interaction session followed, providing a platform for stakeholders to share insights, raise concerns, and explore potential projects with TESDA. The fruitful discussion showcased NEMSU’s proactive stance in advocating for educational and technical advancements.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nVice President for Academic Affairs Dr. Lady Sol A. Suazo delivered the closing remarks, highlighting the importance of continuous dialogue and partnership in achieving educational excellence.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe program concluded with a video presentation of the NEMSU Hymn and a photo opportunity with the guests and university officials. \r\nThe visit of Deputy Director General Colambo to NEMSU marks a significant milestone in the university’s ongoing efforts to strengthen partnerships with national agencies, reaffirming its commitment to producing globally competitive and socially responsible graduates.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThis event underscores the shared vision of NEMSU and TESDA in empowering learners and communities, forging a brighter and more progressive future for Mindanao and the entire nation.\r\n', '𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗗𝗲𝗽𝘂𝘁𝘆-𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿-𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹-𝗩𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘀-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-01-30 09:19:31', '2025-01-30 09:19:31', '2025-01-30 09:19:31'),
('b6595b29-02a8-11ef-904a-a233a240566f', '𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐜𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐚𝐢𝐠𝐧 𝐚𝐠𝐚𝐢𝐧𝐬𝐭 𝐆𝐞𝐧𝐝𝐞𝐫-𝐁𝐚𝐬𝐞𝐝 𝐒𝐞𝐱𝐮𝐚𝐥 𝐇𝐚𝐫𝐚𝐬𝐬𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭 (𝐆𝐁𝐒𝐇)', 'Bawal-bastos-2024', 'In an effort to strengthen the campaign against Gender-Based Sexual Harassment (GBSH), the North Eastern Mindanao State University Tandag Campus (NEMSU-Tandag) took proactive measures by hosting the RA 11313 Safe Spaces Act, also known as the Bawal Bastos Law Seminar, on April 24, 2024, at NEMSU-Tandag Gymnasium.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Bawal-bastos/bawal-bastos-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn an effort to strengthen the campaign against Gender-Based Sexual Harassment (GBSH), the North Eastern Mindanao State University Tandag Campus (NEMSU-Tandag) took proactive measures by hosting the RA 11313 Safe Spaces Act, also known as the Bawal Bastos Law Seminar, on April 24, 2024, at NEMSU-Tandag Gymnasium.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe seminar aimed to empower and inform students about their rights under this legislation, equipping them with the tools necessary to recognize, report, and prevent instances of harassment.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn addition to this significant event, representatives from the Regional Recruit and Selection Units (RRSU) of the Philippine National Police (PNP) also participated and organized the Recruitment Information Drive. Through this initiative, PNP RRSU personnel were able to disseminate information about the agency\'s recruitment process to qualified and interested individuals in the campus.', 'bawal-bastos-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-04-24 10:57:48', '2024-04-24 10:57:48', '2024-04-24 10:57:48'),
('b8a7c870-8358-11ee-bea4-a233a240566f', '𝗛𝗔𝗧𝗦 𝗢𝗙𝗙 to the outstanding winners of the Oral Health Research Paper Presentation (Professional) at Health Con \'23.', 'Best-Paper-Health-con', '𝗛𝗔𝗧𝗦 𝗢𝗙𝗙 to the outstanding winners of the Oral Health Research Paper Presentation (Professional) at Health Con \'23.', '\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝗕𝗲𝘀𝘁 𝗣𝗮𝗽𝗲𝗿 𝗣𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿 | North Eastern Mindanao State University – Main Campus\r\n𝗗𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗳𝗶𝗹𝗲 𝗼𝗳 𝗕𝗮𝗰𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗹 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗺𝘂𝗻𝗶𝘁𝗶𝗲𝘀 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝗼𝗰𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗶𝗻 𝗪𝗮𝘁𝗲𝗿 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗠𝗼𝗹𝗹𝘂𝘀𝗸 𝗦𝗽𝗲𝗰𝗶𝗲𝘀 (𝑭𝒂𝒖𝒏𝒖𝒔 𝒂𝒕𝒆𝒓) 𝗶𝗻 𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴 𝗥𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿 𝗘𝗰𝗼𝘀𝘆𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗺\r\nRoxan Eupeña-Caray <br>\r\nGiselle B. Ramos <br>\r\nJocelyn B. Panduyos <br>\r\nLuzminda S. Bacquial <br>\r\nSharon Rose Tabugo\r\n<br>\r\n', 'chrdc-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-11-10 14:50:11', '2023-11-10 14:50:11', '2023-11-10 14:50:11'),
('b91e24f2-b023-11ee-9af6-a233a240566f', 'The Office of fhe Vice President of the Republic of the Philippines recognizes NEMSU for contributing in the realization of the VP\'s vision  to reach, serve, and create lasting impact on the lives of the Filipino people.', 'OVP-2024', 'The Office of fhe Vice President of the Republic of the Philippines recognizes NEMSU for contributing in the realization of the VP\'s vision  to reach, serve, and create lasting impact on the lives of the Filipino people.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ovp-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ovp-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ovp-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n', 'ovp-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-01-09 17:55:11', '2024-01-09 17:55:11', '2024-01-09 17:55:11'),
('bcad2f31-aaa6-43c7-be29-befdc1cadfa2', 'Consultative meeting with the Department of Agriculture (Regional and Provincial Offices)', 'consultative-meeting-with-the-department-of-agriculture-regional-and-provincial-offices', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The NEMSU Research Development, Innovation and Extension Services conducted a consultative meeting with the Department of Agriculture (Regional and Provincial Offices) on February 14, 2023 at NEMSU RD Conference Room.</span></span></p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">The NEMSU Research Development, Innovation and Extension Services conducted a consultative meeting with the Department of Agriculture (Regional and Provincial Offices) on February 14, 2023 at NEMSU RD Conference Room. Mr. Mark Quico, Provincial Agriculturist, and Dr. Gemma A. Asufre, Regional Focal on Feed Formulation and Plant Health Program represented the DA office. The gathering carefully plan out the future directions and actions and harmonize its operations across campuses in the areas of Research and Development, Innovation and Extension units to align with the new direction of the present administration.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Sir%20Jojo-RDEI%20(1).png\" /></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/rd1.png\" /></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/8.png\" /></span></p>', '1(1).png', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-02-15 11:53:20', '2023-02-17 04:46:28', '2023-02-17 04:46:28'),
('bd396f34-df41-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐌𝐚𝐢𝐧 𝐜𝐡𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐬 𝐌𝐞𝐠𝐚 𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐂𝐮𝐩 𝐐𝐮𝐢𝐳 𝐒𝐡𝐨𝐰, 𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬 𝐭𝐢𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐭 𝐭𝐨 𝐍𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥𝐬', 'MEGA-Champ-2024', 'In a thrilling showcase of intellect, NEMSU Team B, composed of Jesriel Carbonilla, Pierce Andy Andoy, and Elino Joson, grabbed the championship trophy in the Mega Regional Cup Quiz Show, hosted by the Philippine Institute of Civil Engineers - Father Saturnino Urios University Student Chapter (PICE-FSUU),', '\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a thrilling showcase of intellect, NEMSU Team B, composed of Jesriel Carbonilla, Pierce Andy Andoy, and Elino Joson, grabbed the championship trophy in the Mega Regional Cup Quiz Show, hosted by the Philippine Institute of Civil Engineers - Father Saturnino Urios University Student Chapter (PICE-FSUU), in partnership with Megareview Center on March 9, 2024.\r\n<br><br>\r\nParticipated by all Civil Engineering institutions across the Caraga region, the competition inside the FSUU CBE Hall serves as a one-way ticket to the national level, which will be held in Cebu.\r\n<br><br>\r\nMeanwhile, NEMSU Team A, composed of Ime Cadavos, Niño Nickel Suazo, and Glory De La Serna, placed 7th out of 11 participating teams.\r\n<br><br>\r\nReport by John Damort Guingguing<br>\r\nPhoto from Niño Nickel Suazo\r\n<br>\r\n', 'CEChamp.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', 32, 'news', 1, '2024-03-09 17:50:55', '2024-03-09 17:50:55', '2024-03-09 17:50:55'),
('bd7c5322-4463-45b4-bc50-6361b5f67d22', 'NEMSU Cantilan Campus hosts the 1st Joint ACO-ADCO Councils Meeting', 'nemsu-cantilan-campus-hosts-the-1st-joint-aco-adco-councils-meeting', '<p>The North Eastern Mindanao State University commenced its 1st Quarter Joint Academic and Administrative Councils Meeting hosted by NEMSU Cantilan Campus on February 6, 2023.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The North Eastern Mindanao State University commenced its 1st Quarter Joint Academic and Administrative Councils Meeting hosted by NEMSU Cantilan Campus on February 6, 2023. Dr. Juancho A. Intano, NEMSU Cantilan Campus Director, opens the event with his strong message of welcoming the participants with enthusiasm and warm hospitality. Dr. Intano also expressed his great honor of hosting the 1st Quarter ACO-ADCO Councils Meeting in 2023. At the event, NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, presided over the council meeting with an assurance that every voice of the council would be heard. The proponents of the different agenda articulated the objectives of their proposal subject to a comprehensive discussion of the council. The meeting was a preparation for the upcoming Special Board Meeting to be participated by NEMSU&rsquo;s Board of Regents.</span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/4.png\" /></span></p>\r\n            \r\n            <p><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/6.png\" /></span></p>', 'NEMSU Cantilan Campus hosts the 1st Joint ACO-ADCO Councils Meeting.png', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-02-07 11:45:41', '2023-02-07 11:45:41', '2023-02-07 11:45:41'),
('be8c97a1-2210-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'Book Selection of Tagbina Faculty at Davao City', 'Book-Selection-davao-city', '', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>Bringing our faculty to various book publishing companies and book distributors in Davao City for greater access and participation in the selection and acquisition of books and other printed library materials. \r\n<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/select02.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/select03.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/select04.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'select01.jpg', 'Ronie A. Sajelan, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-22 10:09:53', '2022-03-22 10:09:53', '2022-03-22 10:09:53'),
('c16aaa2b-47a7-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', 'Hans Spencer Lumampao', 'local-masts-Taekwondo', '<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hans Spencer Lumampao, a 2022 MASTS qualifier, proved once more his supremacy by retaining his title in the men\'s Taekwondo Kyorugi welterweight category, making him</span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">𝗟𝗢𝗖𝗔𝗟 𝗠𝗔𝗦𝗧𝗦 𝗨𝗣𝗗𝗔𝗧𝗘: Hans Spencer Lumampao, a 2022 MASTS qualifier, proved once more his supremacy by retaining his title in the men\'s Taekwondo Kyorugi welterweight category, making him one of the flag bearers of NEMSU in the upcoming Mindanao-wide sporting event in September.\r\n<br>\r\nReport by Lee Van Cleff M. Labsan<br>\r\nPhoto by Manuel B. Allada\r\n<br><br>\r\n#2023LocalMASTS<br>\r\n#TheSeaStrivers<br>\r\n#SailingAndStrivingForTheTruth\r\n\r\n</span></span></p>', 'sea-taek-00.JPG', 'The Sea Strivers Publication', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-08-30 18:10:07', '2023-08-30 18:10:07', '2023-08-30 18:10:07'),
('c18891af-4aef-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', '[SUCsTREND:  Strengthening Universities and Colleges Through Responsive, Engaging, and  Novel Discourses]', 'SUCsTREND-2023', '[SUCsTREND:  Strengthening Universities and Colleges Through Responsive, Engaging, and  Novel Discourses]\r\nTOPIC: ChatGPT and Artificial Intelligence\'s Prospects and Implications in Philippine Higher Education (PHEI)', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nTOPIC: <b>ChatGPT and Artificial Intelligence\'s Prospects and Implications in Philippine Higher Education (PHEI)</b><br><br>\r\nDate: September 26, 2023 (Tuesday)\r\nTime: 10am-12nn<br><br>\r\n[RESOURCE SPEAKER]<br>\r\nATTY. DIONEL O. ALBINA<br>\r\nChancellor, USTsP CDO<br><br>\r\nUniversity of Science and Technology of Southern Philippines (USTsP)\r\nExpected Participants: <br><br>\r\n- All Philippine Higher Education Institutions (PHEIs) (State Universities and Colleges (SUCs), Private HEIs (PHEIs) and Local Universities and Colleges (LUCs)<br><br>\r\n- OCJML SUCs Undercharge <br><br>\r\nALL Presidents, Vice-Presidents, Chancellors, Officials, Faculty, Staff and Students (Graduate and Undergraduate)<br><br>\r\n[Zoom Credentials]<br><br>\r\nMeeting ID: 916 5886 6694<br>\r\nPasscode: 598158<br><br>\r\nOur gratitude to CHED Comm. Jo Mark M. Libre for this learning opportunities in the advancement of Philippine Higher Education Institutions (PHEIs).\r\n<span>\r\n', 'chatgpt-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-09-03 12:15:05', '2023-09-03 12:15:05', '2023-09-03 12:15:05'),
('c18b2eaa-2b16-11ef-8173-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐉𝐨𝐢𝐧𝐬 𝐆𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐚𝐝𝐞 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐎𝐩𝐞𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐂𝐞𝐫𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐧𝐲 𝐨𝐟 𝟔𝟒𝐭𝐡 𝐀𝐫𝐚𝐰 𝐧𝐠 𝐒𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐠𝐚𝐨 𝐝𝐞𝐥 𝐒𝐮𝐫, 𝐂𝐞𝐥𝐞𝐛𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐇𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐂𝐨𝐦𝐦𝐮𝐧𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐒𝐩𝐢𝐫𝐢𝐭', 'Araw-ng-Surigao-Opening', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU)-Main Campus participated in the foot parade and opening ceremony of the 64th Araw ng Surigao del Sur, a grand celebration commemorating the province\'s rich history and cultural heritage.', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU)-Main Campus participated in the foot parade and opening ceremony of the 64th Araw ng Surigao del Sur, a grand celebration commemorating the province\'s rich history and cultural heritage. \r\n<br><br>\r\nNEMSU\'s involvement in the Araw ng Surigao del Sur not only highlights the university\'s commitment to community engagement but also emphasizes its role in preserving and promoting local culture. The opening ceremony, which featured speeches from local officials and cultural performances from NEMSU Singing Ambassadors, served as a platform for NEMSU to demonstrate its solidarity with the wider Surigao del Sur community.\r\n<br><br>\r\nBy participating in such events, NEMSU reinforces its dedication to fostering a sense of pride and belonging among its members, while also contributing to the province\'s ongoing narrative of growth and unity.\r\n</p>\r\n', 'araw-surigao-2024.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-06-15 17:56:27', '2024-06-15 17:56:27', '2024-06-15 17:56:27'),
('c2a11185-91df-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴 𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱 𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹, 𝗼𝗽𝗶𝘀𝘆𝗮𝗹 𝗻𝗮 𝗶𝗻𝗶𝗹𝘂𝗻𝘀𝗮𝗱 𝗮𝗻𝗴 𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺', 'Sa pagbubukas ng bagong taong panuruan, pormal na isinagawa ng North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Tandag Graduate School ang oryentasyon para sa kanilang mga mag-aaral kaninang umaga, Agosto 30, sa University Gymnasium.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺 6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nSa pagbubukas ng bagong taong panuruan, pormal na isinagawa ng North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Tandag Graduate School ang oryentasyon para sa kanilang mga mag-aaral kaninang umaga, Agosto 30, sa University Gymnasium.\r\n<br/>\r\nMatapos magbigay ng pambungad na salita si Dr. Floresito D. Calub, ang OIC Campus Director, binigyang-diin ni Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, SUC President III, sa kanyang mensahe ng inspirasyon ang kahalagahan ng pag-aaral upang hubugin ang husay sa kanilang propesyon.\r\n<br/>\r\n\"We understand the vital role of the graduate school on your professional achievements, but foremost, that is very vital for your work and profession,\" ani Pres. Loayon.\r\nKasunod nito, ipinakilala ni Dr. Jennifer M. Montero, Dean ng Graduate School, ang mga tagapag-ugnay ng programa, mga guro, at kawani ng NEMSU Tandag Grad School. Kalauna\'y naglahad din siya ng mga balita ukol sa mga operasyon nito. \r\n<br/>\r\nBukod doon, nagbahagi ang Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) na si Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo ng mga akademikong impormasyon na may kaugnayan sa mga mag-aaral. Samantala, tinalakay naman ni Vice President for Research and Extension na si Dr. Rolly G. Salvaleon ang mga usapin hinggil sa pananaliksik ng Grad School. Habang nagpaalala ang University Registrar na si Ms. Lynnet A. Sarvida ukol sa mga dokumentong kailangang isumite upang maging maayos ang daloy ng kanilang pag-aaral.\r\n<br/>\r\nKasabay ng nasabing orientation program, nagsagawa rin ng eleksyon para sa mga bagong estudyanteng manunungkulan sa NEMSU Graduate School Student Organization, kung saan pormal na nahalal si G. Mark Jade G. Burlat bilang bagong pangulo.\r\n<br/>\r\nAyon sa datos na ipinakita ni Dr. Montero, umaabot sa 1,486 ang kabuuang bilang ng mga mag-aaral sa Grad School ngayong taong panuruan 2025-2026.\r\nPara sa mga karagdagang  kuhang-larawan, maaring bisitahin ang Google drive na nakalagay sa post\r\n<br/>', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗱-𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹-𝗢𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻-𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺.jpg', 'Rhea Malinao Cedron', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-08-30 10:52:16', NULL, NULL),
('c79c49a4-f412-11ef-b8b6-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐂𝐨𝐦𝐩𝐥𝐞𝐭𝐞𝐬 𝐎𝐟𝐟𝐢𝐜𝐢𝐚𝐥 𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨 𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐨𝐟 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧', '𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧', 'The official studio recording of the NEMSU Hymn has been successfully completed in Davao City. This initiative aims to standardize and preserve the university’s official hymn, reinforcing its significance in fostering institutional identity across all campuses.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe official studio recording of the NEMSU Hymn has been successfully completed in Davao City. This initiative aims to standardize and preserve the university’s official hymn, reinforcing its significance in fostering institutional identity across all campuses.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nStudents from Tandag Campus and Tagbina Campus took part in the recording process, representing the university’s student body in this milestone project. They were joined by key officials and faculty members, including Dr. Evelyn T. Bagood (lyricist), Mr. Carl Martin R. Engcoy (arranger), Mr. Castor V. Balacuit (musician), Dr. Mick Mars P. Silvano, Dr. Shyla O. Moreno, Ms. Kim Mary E. Narcana, Mr. Revelyn G. Enderes, Dr. Romel C. Nemiño, and Mr. Rojil Jone E. Cañete. Their presence and active participation ensured the smooth execution of the recording sessions.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe team worked on refining the hymn’s official rendition, ensuring clarity, precision, and adherence to musical standards. The studio recording will serve as the definitive audio reference for official university functions, ceremonies, and events, strengthening NEMSU’s institutional presence.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nWith the successful completion of this project, NEMSU moves forward in its commitment to upholding its traditions while embracing new ways to enhance its identity as a premier academic institution.\r\n', '𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐨-𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠-𝐨𝐟-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐇𝐲𝐦𝐧.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-07 14:03:26', NULL, NULL),
('c8538195-8ed7-11ef-bdca-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐬 𝐈𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐜𝐞𝐬𝐬𝐞𝐬 𝐓𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐠𝐡 𝐑𝐞𝐟𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐡𝐞𝐫 𝐂𝐨𝐮𝐫𝐬𝐞 𝐨𝐧 𝐀𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐭', 'Strengthens-Internal-Audit-Quality-process', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) held a successful Refresher Course Training on Internal Quality Audit on October 17-18, 2024, at Shacene Pension House, Tandag City. The event, spearheaded by the university\'s Quality Assurance Office, aimed to enhance the internal auditing capabilities of its personnel, ensuring continued compliance with quality standards.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) held a successful Refresher Course Training on Internal Quality Audit on October 17-18, 2024, at Shacene Pension House, Tandag City. The event, spearheaded by the university\'s Quality Assurance Office, aimed to enhance the internal auditing capabilities of its personnel, ensuring continued compliance with quality standards.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe two-day event was graced by Engr. Severino M. Villalon, Jr., an esteemed BCJA Auditor, who served as the resource speaker. Engr. Villalon shared his extensive expertise in internal quality audits, providing practical insights and methodologies essential for auditing various university processes and functions.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn her opening message, Dr. Evelyn T. Bagood, Campus Director of NEMSU Tandag, emphasized the importance of consistent quality assurance practices in ensuring that NEMSU maintains its educational excellence. She encouraged participants to actively engage in the discussions and apply the knowledge gained in their respective units.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Nemesio G. Loayon, NEMSU President, delivered an inspirational message, highlighting the vital role of quality audits in achieving the university\'s long-term goals. He commended the initiative of the Quality Assurance Office and challenged the participants to uphold the standards that would make NEMSU a premier educational institution in the region.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe refresher course highlighted critical auditing principles and reinforced participants\' skills in identifying areas for improvement in internal processes.', 'internal-coa-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-10-18 19:37:55', '2024-10-18 19:37:55', '2024-10-18 19:37:55');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('c8e1d1f5-91e3-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', '𝐆𝐥𝐨𝐛𝐚𝐥 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐧𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬: 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬 𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩 𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡 𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞 𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞 𝐋𝐭𝐝. 𝐭𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐠𝐡 𝐕𝐢𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐚𝐥 𝐌𝐎𝐔 𝐒𝐢𝐠𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐈𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐧𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐖𝐢𝐧𝐞 𝐓𝐚𝐥𝐤', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝', 'North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) strengthened its global linkages through a Virtual Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) Signing Ceremony with Fine Vintage Ltd., followed by an International Wine Talk, held on September 8, 2025, via Zoom Meeting.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝 1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝 2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝 3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝 4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) strengthened its global linkages through a Virtual Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) Signing Ceremony with Fine Vintage Ltd., followed by an International Wine Talk, held on September 8, 2025, via Zoom Meeting.<br>\r\nThe university was represented by Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President, together with the Vice Presidents, Internationalization Directors, heads, and other key officials. Fine Vintage Ltd. was represented by James Cluer, CEO and Master of Wine; Charles Curtis, Master of Wine and consultant based in New York City; Mike Lee, Director of Education Programs from British Columbia; and Ms. Jane Edorio, Sales and Administration Manager based in Tandag City.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nFine Vintage Ltd., founded in 1995 by James Cluer MW, is an institution recognized for its work in wine education. It offers WSET (Wine & Spirit Education Trust) certification courses, wine training, wine tours, and consulting services across the Americas and Asia.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe MOU outlines several areas of collaboration. NEMSU students and faculty will have access to free online WSET wine certification courses, with the possibility of microcredential recognition. The agreement also opens part-time employment opportunities for the top 50–100 students in sales and marketing projects, alongside internships in wine tour businesses that may be used as academic case studies.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn addition, faculty members will receive specialized training in ICT, graphic design, accounting, and marketing projects. Both institutions will also explore joint research on wine production, marketing trends, tourism development, and other related fields.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThis partnership is particularly directed toward the BS in Business Administration (BSBA) and BS in Hospitality Management (BSHM) programs. It is expected to enhance academic instruction, research, and training, while also improving employability through industry-recognized certifications and practical experiences.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThrough this international collaboration, NEMSU continues to pursue opportunities that extend learning beyond the local context, ensuring that its graduates are prepared to engage with professional and academic communities worldwide.\r\n<br/><br/>', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔-𝐒𝐞𝐚𝐥𝐬-𝐏𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩-𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡-𝐅𝐢𝐧𝐞-𝐕𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐠𝐞-𝐋𝐭𝐝.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-09-08 11:21:48', NULL, NULL),
('ca0e2356-86ed-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', '𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗, 𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨, 𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔 𝗜𝗻𝗸 𝗠𝗢𝗔 𝘁𝗼 𝗕𝗼𝗼𝘀𝘁 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗺𝘂𝗻𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗟𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗹𝗶𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗱𝘀 𝗶𝗻 𝗦𝘂𝗿𝗶𝗴𝗮𝗼 𝗱𝗲𝗹 𝗦𝘂𝗿', '𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A', 'In a landmark event to empower vulnerable communities, the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD), in collaboration with the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) and the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA), successfully held the SurSur Livelihood Congress and ceremonial Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) and Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) signing on August 7, 2025, at the University Gymnasium of NEMSU Main Campus.\r\n', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a landmark event to empower vulnerable communities, the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD), in collaboration with the North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) and the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA), successfully held the SurSur Livelihood Congress and ceremonial Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) and Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) signing on August 7, 2025, at the University Gymnasium of NEMSU Main Campus.\r\n<br/>\r\nThemed “SLP SurSur HININANG 2025: A Community Fashion and Livelihood Showcase,” the congress is part of the Sustainable Livelihood Program (SLP) initiatives to strengthen institutional partnerships that uplift the lives of the poor, vulnerable, and marginalized communities across the province.\r\n<br/>\r\nThe highlight of the event was the formalization of two key partnerships:\r\n • One between DSWD-SLP and NEMSU\r\n • Another between DSWD-SLP and TESDA Surigao del Sur\r\nThe MOA signing was graced by Dr. Nemesio Loayon, University President of NEMSU; Director Ramel Nartatez of TESDA; and Dr. Mari-Flor A. Dollaga, Regional Director of DSWD Field Office Caraga. These partnerships are expected to provide greater access to technical education and community-based livelihood opportunities for SLP participants.\r\n<br/>\r\nIn his message of commitment, Dr. Loayon expressed NEMSU’s dedication to contributing to inclusive development through education and livelihood assistance. TESDA and DSWD likewise reaffirmed their commitment to grassroots empowerment and strategic collaboration.\r\nA key feature of the program was the “HININANG” showcase, derived from the Tandaganon word meaning “made of,” which displayed products made by SLP associations from different municipalities of Surigao del Sur. The fashion and livelihood exhibit featured innovative local products, modelled and presented to the public, aimed at promoting market readiness, expanding visibility, and strengthening distribution networks.\r\n<br/>\r\n<br/>\r\nThe event also served as a platform for knowledge sharing, inspiring innovation, and enhancing the sustainability of local enterprises. Stakeholders, beneficiaries, and guests witnessed the creativity and entrepreneurial spirit of SLP participants, further strengthening community pride and market access.\r\nThe SurSur Livelihood Congress not only signaled a renewed commitment among institutions but also opened doors for expanded enterprise development and long-term community resilience in the Caraga region.\r\n\r\n', '𝗗𝗦𝗪𝗗-𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗗𝗔-𝗜𝗻𝗸-𝗠𝗢A-1.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-08-07 04:30:43', NULL, NULL),
('cb21dfa1-3287-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Empowering our university\'s research community through a transformative journey into the realm of Futures Thinking and Foresight!', 'Future-Thinking-2023', 'Empowering our university\'s research community through a transformative journey into the realm of Futures Thinking and Foresight! 🚀🔍 Excited to unlock new possibilities and shape a brighter tomorrow through knowledge and innovation.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/for-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/for-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/for-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/future-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/future-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/future-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nEmpowering our university\'s research community through a transformative journey into the realm of Futures Thinking and Foresight! 🚀🔍 Excited to unlock new possibilities and shape a brighter tomorrow through knowledge and innovation.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n#ResearchCapabilityBuilding <br>\r\n#FuturesThinking <br>\r\n#Foresight\r\n#ReadyForTheFuture', 'for-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-03 18:30:53', '2023-08-03 18:30:53', '2023-08-03 18:30:53'),
('cb5f229a-2206-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'Law Library Orientation: Face-to-Face', 'law-orientation-2022', '<p>In preparation for the 2nd Semester A.Y. 2021-2022 and in coordination with the College of Law, the Law Librarian attended the face-to-face College of Law Faculty Fellowship and Orientation held last January 24, 2022</p>', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>In preparation for the 2nd Semester A.Y. 2021-2022 and in coordination with the College of Law, the Law Librarian attended the face-to-face College of Law Faculty Fellowship and Orientation held last January 24, 2022, from 10:00 am-2:00 pm at the Moot Room of the College of Law Building. The Law Librarian was given the opportunity to talk about the Law Library services and updates offered for the law faculty and staff. The program started with prayer and the singing of the Philippine National Anthem and was followed by a welcome message from our Law Dean Atty. Daniel L. Diaz. The introduction of the faculty and staff members of the College of Law was made.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe presence of our VPAA Dr. Ramel D. Tomaquin and Campus Director Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon were also there for their words of inspiration. There are a total of 26 law faculty and staff who attended the said event. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nOn January 28, 2022, the Law Librarian conducted a face-to-face library orientation to our law students during General Orientation held at the NEMSU gymnasium. Among the presenters were Atty. Daniel L. Diaz who presented the faculty members, Atty. Christian Lee R. Ramires discussed the Student Handbook, Atty. Lucks Mae Digaum-Yblernas shared the “Tips to Survive Law School”. An inspirational message was also given by our VPAA likewise closing remarks were given by our Campus Director.  The program was also highlighted with an open forum where students\' questions and queries were addressed.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/law02.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/law03.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'law01.jpg', 'Jehoney V. Alboroto, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-01-24 10:09:53', '2022-01-24 10:09:53', '2022-01-24 10:09:53'),
('cd50d068-a97a-11ee-9af6-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐒𝐨𝐚𝐫𝐬: 𝐓𝐨𝐩 𝟑 𝐢𝐧 𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐚𝐠𝐚 𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐨𝐧, 𝐒𝐞𝐜𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝟏𝟕𝟒𝐭𝐡 𝐒𝐩𝐨𝐭 𝐢𝐧 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐑𝐚𝐧𝐤\'𝐬 𝐓𝐨𝐩 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐞𝐬 𝐢𝐧 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐏𝐡𝐢𝐥𝐢𝐩𝐩𝐢𝐧𝐞𝐬', 'UniRANK-2024', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) clinches a spot in the UniRank\'s prestigious rankings, not only securing its place among the top universities in the Philippines but also claiming the impressive position of Top 3 in the Caraga Region. ', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) clinches a spot in the UniRank\'s prestigious rankings, not only securing its place among the top universities in the Philippines but also claiming the impressive position of Top 3 in the Caraga Region. \r\nUniRank, established in 2005, is the leading international higher education portal and search engine featuring reviews and rankings of over 13,900 officially recognized Universities and Colleges in 200 countries. \r\n<br><br>\r\nThis achievement is a testament to NEMSU\'s unwavering commitment to providing quality education. The University\'s faculty, equipped with a wealth of expertise, has consistently inspired students to reach new heights of academic achievement. The innovative teaching methodologies have further contributed to NEMSU\'s stellar academic reputation.\r\n<br><br>\r\nAs NEMSU celebrates this momentous achievement, it also looks toward a future filled with continued growth, innovation, and a steadfast commitment to shaping the leaders of tomorrow. The University\'s inclusion in the top universities in the Philippines is a recognition of its dedication to providing quality education and making a positive impact on society.\r\n</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<b>#NEMSUCARES</b>', 'unirank.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-01-02 22:15:11', '2024-01-02 22:15:11', '2024-01-02 22:15:11'),
('cfcacd9f-5777-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', 'Official Tally of Medals', 'Masts-Medals-2023', NULL, '<iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M3Nyuxhnzib4G7pS-obclFPZ22ecaw60/preview\" width=\"100%\"></iframe>', 'medals-00.JPG', 'Public Information Office', 1, 'news', 1, '2023-09-20 05:35:04', '2023-09-20 13:50:11', '2023-09-20 13:50:11'),
('d37bbb51-093f-45f4-9488-c777d1420f11', 'Provincial Director of CSC-SDS Aurora Mantilla Visits NEMSU President to Discuss Upcoming Civil Service Exam', 'provincial-director-of-csc-sds-aurora-mantilla-visits-nemsu-president-to-discuss-upcoming-civil-service-exam', '<p>The Provincial Director of CSC-SDS Field Office, Aurora B. Mantilla paid courtesy visit to NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon discussing the important matters for the upcoming Civil Service Examination &ndash; Pen and Paper Test (CSE-PPT) on March 26, 2023.<br />\r\nThe Civil Service Examination is an important component of the recruitment process for many government jobs. It ensures that government agencies are able to recruit the most qualified and capable applicants for the job, while also securing a fair, merit-based, and consistent selection process.<br />\r\nNEMSU Tandag Campus is one of the identified testing centers in the entire Caraga Region. The meeting between Dr. Loayon and Director Mantilla hope for smooth and successful conduct of the CSE-PPT 2023.</p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The Provincial Director of CSC-SDS Field Office, Aurora B. Mantilla paid courtesy visit to NEMSU President, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon discussing the important matters for the upcoming Civil Service Examination &ndash; Pen and Paper Test (CSE-PPT) on March 26, 2023.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">The Civil Service Examination is an important component of the recruitment process for many government jobs. It ensures that government agencies are able to recruit the most qualified and capable applicants for the job, while also securing a fair, merit-based, and consistent selection process.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\">NEMSU Tandag Campus is one of the identified testing centers in the entire Caraga Region. The meeting between Dr. Loayon and Director Mantilla hope for smooth and successful conduct of the CSE-PPT 2023.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode,Lucida Grande,sans-serif\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/1%20(1).png\" /></span></p>', '2 (1).png', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-03-08 11:11:02', '2023-03-10 03:03:22', '2023-03-10 03:03:22'),
('d3afb34d-0927-11ef-9740-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐇𝐨𝐬𝐭𝐬 𝐏𝐄𝐒𝐎𝐌𝐀𝐏 𝐒𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐠𝐚𝐨 𝐝𝐞𝐥 𝐒𝐮𝐫 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠', 'PESOMAP-2024', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) serves as the venue for the gathering of the Public Employment Service Office Managers Association of the Philippines (PESO MAP) in Surigao del Sur. The meeting brought together key stakeholders and leaders to discuss important issues and initiatives related to employment and public service.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/Pesomap/2024/peso-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Pesomap/peso-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Pesomap/peso-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Pesomap/peso-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Pesomap/peso-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Pesomap/peso-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) serves as the venue for the gathering of the Public Employment Service Office Managers Association of the Philippines (PESO MAP) in Surigao del Sur. The meeting brought together key stakeholders and leaders to discuss important issues and initiatives related to employment and public service.<br><br>\r\nThe ongoing event, held at NEMSU\'s campus in Tandag, is well-attended by PESO managers and officials from various municipalities across Surigao del Sur. The gathering provided a platform for networking, collaboration, and knowledge-sharing among participants.\r\n<br/>', 'peso-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-04-26 11:29:42', '2024-04-26 11:29:42', '2024-04-26 11:29:42'),
('d81d39b4-e4cf-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐑𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐧𝐟𝐢𝐠𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐄𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐧𝐝𝐚𝐫𝐝𝐬: 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔’𝐬 𝐖𝐨𝐫𝐤𝐬𝐡𝐨𝐩 𝐨𝐧 𝐆𝐫𝐚𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐒𝐲𝐬𝐭𝐞𝐦𝐬 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐇𝐚𝐫𝐦𝐨𝐧𝐢𝐳𝐞𝐝 𝐓𝐚𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐒𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐢𝐟𝐢𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬', 'Reconfiguring-Education-2024', 'Shaped by the university’s mission, a two-day workshop on grading systems and the harmonized table of specifications (TOS) convened NEMSU’s academic stewards to recalibrate its standards for evaluating students\' performance and to enhance the faculty’s capability to ensure that its assessments align with the program and institution\'s outcomes.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/wgrading-2024/two-day-grading-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nShaped by the university’s mission, a two-day workshop on grading systems and the harmonized table of specifications (TOS) convened NEMSU’s academic stewards to recalibrate its standards for evaluating students\' performance and to enhance the faculty’s capability to ensure that its assessments align with the program and institution\'s outcomes.\r\n<br><br>\r\nNow in its second phase, Vice President for Academic Affairs Dr. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo led the Office of Curriculum Development in continuing the implementation of the three-phase university curriculum roadmap, which was initiated and prepared last year by former Curriculum Development Director Dr. Erwin B. Berry.\r\n<br><br>\r\n“Our grading system is the backbone of our assessment process,” Dr. Suazo exclaimed, emphasizing the need to recalibrate it to meet emerging standards and existing policies in the current educational landscape, which expect outcomes-based education for learners.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe two-day workshop generated ideas to address current challenges and provided additional learning opportunities for educators. Dr. Berry led the harmonization of the Table of Specifications, ensuring that each faculty member understood the importance of content validity through aligning course-intended learning outcomes with assessments. During this workshop, with Dr. Berry\'s assistance and the active participation of department chairs, curriculum heads, directors, and deans, a new format for the Table of Specifications was established.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe fruitful collaboration among academic officials, vigorously facilitated by Dr. Romeo A. Patan, the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences, resulted in the creation of a unified grading system proposal, considering each program\'s unique requirements and study program outlined in respective CMOs. The outcomes of this session, including the new transmutation table and the NEMSU e-class record, will be unveiled to stakeholders during a public presentation no later than the last week of March.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe gathering also provided an opportunity to reorient department chairpersons regarding the university’s Faculty Development Policy. This policy outlines numerous opportunities and faculty support the university can offer to address faculty capability development, professional growth, and program priority needs.\r\n<br/>', 'two-day-grading-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-15 17:28:39', '2024-03-15 17:28:39', '2024-03-15 17:28:39'),
('d9945c0a-9526-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', 'Celebrating PLAI @ 100 years', 'Celebrating-PLAI', 'Various campuses of NEMSU embarked on a journey to the Culinary Heart of the Philippines', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>From November 21 to 24, 2023, seven librarians representing various campuses of NEMSU (NEMSU-Cagwait, NEMSU Lianga, NEMSU Cantilan, NEMSU-San Miguel, and NEMSU Tandag) embarked on a journey to the Culinary Heart of the Philippines—the Province of Pampanga. Their destination: the 𝗣𝗟𝗔𝗜 𝗡𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝗮𝗹 𝗖𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗻𝗻𝗶𝗮𝗹 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝗴𝗿𝗲𝘀𝘀, themed \"𝗣𝗮𝗴𝗵𝗮𝗻𝗱𝘂𝗿𝗮𝘄 𝗸𝗮𝗴 𝗣𝗮𝗱𝗮𝘆𝗼𝗻: 𝗛𝗘𝗥𝗜𝗧𝗔𝗚𝗘. 𝗛𝗢𝗥𝗜𝗭𝗢𝗡. 𝗛𝗔𝗥𝗠𝗢𝗡𝗬.\" The congress unfolded at the SMX Convention Center Clark Field, Pampanga, 𝗳𝗲𝗮𝘁𝘂𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝟯 𝗞𝗲𝘆𝗻𝗼𝘁𝗲 𝗦𝗽𝗲𝗮𝗸𝗲𝗿𝘀, 𝟵 𝗣𝗹𝗲𝗻𝗮𝗿𝘆 𝗦𝗽𝗲𝗮𝗸𝗲𝗿𝘀, 𝟮𝟮 𝗣𝗮𝗿𝗮𝗹𝗹𝗲𝗹 𝗦𝗲𝘀𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀, 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝟮𝟭 𝗣𝗼𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿 𝗣𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nAmong the distinguished Keynote Speakers was 𝗔𝗺𝗯𝗲𝘁𝗵 𝗢𝗰𝗮𝗺𝗽𝗼, a Professor of History and the Humanities at Ateneo de Manila University. Ocampo, a renowned Public Historian, Independent Curator, scholar, and prolific writer, addressed the congress on the topic \"𝑳𝒊𝒘𝒂𝒏𝒂𝒈 𝒔𝒂 𝑫𝒊𝒍𝒊𝒎: 𝑳𝒊𝒃𝒓𝒂𝒓𝒊𝒆𝒔 𝒊𝒏 𝒕𝒉𝒆 𝑨𝒈𝒆 𝒐𝒇 𝑫𝒊𝒔𝒊𝒏𝒇𝒐𝒓𝒎𝒂𝒕𝒊𝒐𝒏.\" 𝑹𝒆𝒇𝒍𝒆𝒄𝒕𝒊𝒏𝒈 𝒐𝒏 𝑯𝑬𝑹𝑰𝑻𝑨𝑮𝑬, Prof. Ocampo emphasized that being a public historian requires a collective effort, stating that libraries are torn between sharing and selfishness. On the theme of 𝗛𝗢𝗥𝗜𝗭𝗢𝗡, 𝗛𝗼𝗻. 𝗬𝗼𝗹𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮 𝗚𝗿𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮, Chairperson of the Professional Regulatory Board for Librarians, concluded in her keynote address that \"HORIZON represents limitless possibilities, unexplored territories—the uncharted or unknown services still to be discovered in providing assistance to users and the transformative power of our profession.\" Granda encouraged embracing historical, technological, cultural, and educational horizons, paving the way for a challenging, more inclusive, and more enlightened future for LIS in the Philippines. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nA significant highlight of the event was the signing of an agreement between the 𝗣𝗵𝗶𝗹𝗶𝗽𝗽𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗟𝗶𝗯𝗿𝗮𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗻𝘀 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝗼𝗰𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻, 𝗜𝗻𝗰. (𝗣𝗟𝗔𝗜) 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗣𝗵𝗶𝗹𝗶𝗽𝗽𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝗼𝗰𝗶𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗠𝗲𝗱𝗶𝗮 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗜𝗻𝗳𝗼𝗿𝗺𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗟𝗶𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗰𝘆 (𝗣𝗔𝗠𝗜𝗟).\r\nThis agreement marks a crucial step toward fostering a collaborative partnership, reflecting a shared commitment to the promotion and cultivation of media and information literacy in today\'s dynamic and information-rich environment.\r\n<br><br>\r\nTo foster 𝗛𝗔𝗥𝗠𝗢𝗡𝗬 and a sense of unity and shared enthusiasm, the 𝗟𝗶𝗯𝗿𝗮𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗻𝘀 𝗙𝗲𝗹𝗹𝗼𝘄𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽 𝗡𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀 were also part of the program. During this event, librarians and information professionals showcased their vibrant Filipiniana attire, adding a cultural touch to the congress\'s atmosphere. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/plai-1.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/plai-2.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/plai-4.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'Celebrating PLAI.jpg', 'Ms. Dina Mae Ibut, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2023-11-29 14:46:31', '2025-09-19 14:46:31', NULL),
('d995f60b-51d2-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', 'Campus Values Formation Coordinators Gather to Enhance NEMSU\'s Values Formation Program', 'values-Formation-2023', 'In a virtual meeting held today via Google Meet, the Values Formation Coordinators of the various campuses of North Eastern Mindanao State University,', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a virtual meeting held today via Google Meet, the Values Formation Coordinators of the various campuses of North Eastern Mindanao State University, together with Vice President for Academic Affairs Prof. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo and University President Prof. Nemesio G. Loayon, convened to discuss and enhance the Values Formation Program of the University. <br><br>\r\nThe meeting, which took place at 9:30 AM, saw the active participation of the University\'s key decision-makers and those responsible for shaping the character and values of the institution\'s students. The Values Formation Program has long been a cornerstone of NEMSU\'s educational philosophy, aiming to foster not only academic excellence but also the development of well-rounded and morally responsible individuals.<br><br>\r\nVice President for Academic Affairs Prof. Suazo, presented the Values Formation Program of the University and has emphasized the vital role of values in education. She stated, \"In a rapidly changing world, it is essential that we provide our students not only with knowledge but also with a strong moral foundation. We must continuously strive to improve it to meet the evolving needs of our students.\"<br><br>\r\nCoordinators from the different campuses shared their insights and best practices and the gaps and challenges encountered among students, faculty, and stakeholders, creating a collaborative environment for discussing effective strategies to instill values such as integrity, empathy, and social responsibility among students.<br><br>\r\nUniversity President Prof. Loayon commended the dedication of the Values Formation Coordinators and stressed the University\'s commitment to promoting a values-driven educational experience. \"Our goal is not just to produce graduates with academic achievements but also individuals who are compassionate, ethical, and ready to contribute positively to society,\" he stated.<br><br>\r\nSome of the activities conducted on the campuses relative to Values Formation include Mental Health Activities, Monthly Mass, Spiritual Enhancement, and Recollection for Graduating Students. On the other hand, the gaps and challenges encountered revolve around family issues, students coping with the University culture, mental health issues, suicide, and teenage pregnancy.<br><br>\r\nAs the meeting concluded, it was clear that NEMSU is poised to further elevate its Values Formation Program to prepare students not only for academic success but also to be responsible citizens who can make a positive impact on society. The commitment of the Values Formation Coordinators and the support of the University\'s leadership ensures that NEMSU continues to be a place where values and education are intertwined to create well-rounded individuals.\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'values-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-09-12 17:33:11', '2023-09-12 17:33:11', '2023-09-12 17:33:11'),
('dade32e6-e4ef-11ef-8bc4-a233a240566f', '𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝗛𝗼𝗹𝗱𝘀 𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦 𝟭𝟬𝟭 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗶𝗻 𝗣𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗻𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵 𝗛𝗲𝗮𝗹𝘁𝗵 𝗔𝗴𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗶𝗲𝘀', '𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆', 'Tandag City, January 31, 2025 — North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) successfully conducted the “HIV-AIDS 101 and Testing” event at the Ground Floor of the Administration Building, NEMSU Tandag Campus. The initiative was spearheaded by the Office of the University President in collaboration with Adela Serra Ty Memorial Medical Center (ASTMMC) and the City Health Office of Tandag.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nTandag City, January 31, 2025 — North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) successfully conducted the “HIV-AIDS 101 and Testing” event at the Ground Floor of the Administration Building, NEMSU Tandag Campus. The initiative was spearheaded by the Office of the University President in collaboration with Adela Serra Ty Memorial Medical Center (ASTMMC) and the City Health Office of Tandag.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe educational and health awareness activity aimed to promote a deeper understanding of HIV-AIDS and encourage proactive testing among the NEMSU community. The resource speaker for the event was Mr. Paolo Alberto A. Martinez, RPm, from ASTMMC, who provided essential insights on HIV prevention, treatment, and the importance of early testing.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAdding star power and advocacy to the event was Miss Universe Philippines-Siargao, Ms. Millien Joy Montenegro Cabigas. She delivered an inspiring message highlighting her advocacy on HIV awareness, stressing the need for inclusive education and community involvement in addressing health concerns. Her presence added motivation to participants, especially students, to be health-conscious and informed advocates within their own circles.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe program commenced with the opening remarks delivered by Dr. Evelyn T. Bagood, OIC Campus Director of NEMSU Tandag. Dr. Mick Mars P. Silvano, Executive Assistant III, presented the event rationale, emphasizing the significance of raising awareness about HIV-AIDS to foster a healthier, informed campus environment.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn his message, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, SUC President III, highlighted the university’s commitment to supporting health and wellness initiatives that align with its mission of promoting holistic development among students, faculty, and staff.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe event culminated in an engaging forum where participants had the opportunity to ask questions and clarify misconceptions about HIV-AIDS. Free and confidential HIV testing was also offered to attendees, further underscoring the health-centric approach of the activity.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn closing, Dr. Abundio C. Miralles, Vice President for Administration and Finance, expressed gratitude to the event partners and encouraged the community to continue participating in health awareness campaigns.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThis collaborative effort between NEMSU, ASTMMC, and the City Health Office of Tandag highlights the university’s dedication to fostering a culture of health awareness and support, contributing to a safer and more informed campus community.', '𝗛𝗜𝗩-𝗔𝗜𝗗𝗦-𝟭𝟬𝟭-𝗮𝗻𝗱-𝗧𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴-𝗔𝗰𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗶𝘁𝘆.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-04 08:55:43', '2025-02-04 08:55:43', '2025-02-04 08:55:43'),
('db72c383-e004-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐎𝐕𝐏𝐀𝐀 𝐋𝐚𝐮𝐧𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 𝐅𝐚𝐜𝐮𝐥𝐭𝐲 𝐃𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐥𝐨𝐩𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭 𝐏𝐨𝐥𝐢𝐜𝐲', 'OVPAA-Launches-Faculty-Development-Policy-2024', 'The Faculty Development Policy, backed by BOR Resolution No. 163, series of 2023, details the processes and guidelines for faculty regarding capability development, scholarships, and faculty immersion. Department chairpersons from the university system attended the hybrid orientation, as they will be responsible for implementing these policies at the grassroots level. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/FDP-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/FDP-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/FDP-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe Faculty Development Policy, backed by BOR Resolution No. 163, series of 2023, details the processes and guidelines for faculty regarding capability development, scholarships, and faculty immersion. Department chairpersons from the university system attended the hybrid orientation, as they will be responsible for implementing these policies at the grassroots level. During the orientation, the Vice President for Academic Affairs, Dr. Suazo, discussed all the guidelines, timetables, and requirements embedded in the Faculty Development Policy. Dr. Suazo further empowered each department to maximize the FDP by identifying the strengths and weaknesses of the faculty based on program requirements and statutory standards.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Suazo also expressed gratitude during the orientation for the collaborative efforts of the Technical Working Group, which includes the deans, faculty union president, human resource management, the secretariat, and the Board of Regents, in bringing this endeavor to fruition for the enhancement of faculty development.\r\n<br/>', 'FDP-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-11 17:07:35', '2024-03-11 17:07:35', '2024-03-11 17:07:35'),
('dc832240-0a0d-11ef-9740-a233a240566f', '𝟐𝐧𝐝 𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐞𝐫 𝐒𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐢𝐚𝐥 𝐁𝐨𝐚𝐫𝐝 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠', '2nd-Quarter-Special-Board-Meeting-2024', '2nd Quarter Special Board Meeting held earlier this morning via hybrid modality. \r\nThank you Commissioner Aldrin A. Darilag and all members of the board of regents for attending this meeting, paving the way to addressing urgent concerns of North Eastern Mindanao State University.\r\nSpecial thanks goes to Cantilan Campus headed by Dr. Juancho A. Intano for the superb hosting!\r\nPadayon ta!', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n2nd Quarter Special Board Meeting held earlier this morning via hybrid modality. \r\nThank you Commissioner Aldrin A. Darilag and all members of the board of regents for attending this meeting, paving the way to addressing urgent concerns of North Eastern Mindanao State University.\r\nSpecial thanks goes to Cantilan Campus headed by Dr. Juancho A. Intano for the superb hosting!<br>\r\nPadayon ta!\r\n<br/>', 'special-boardmeeting-00.jpg', 'NEMSU Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon ', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-05-02 19:57:12', '2024-05-02 19:57:12', '2024-05-02 19:57:12'),
('dd0c0f7b-1f8d-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU - Cantilan Campus 14th University Commencement Exercises', 'Cantilan-Campus-14-Commencement-Exercises', 'The Graduation Ceremony commenced with a remarkable Academic Procession, featuring distinguished participants, including Academic Marshals, Candidates for Graduation, Administrative Staff, University Faculty Members,', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-cantilan-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mcomm-cantilan-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-cantilan-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-cantilan-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-cantilan-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-cantilan-78.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\"Decades of Sculpting Better Lives: North Eastern Mindanao State University - Cantilan Campus 14th University Commencement Exercises\". <br><br>\r\n\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University - Cantilan Campus held its Graduation Ceremony on June 27, 2023, 1:00 PM at the NEMSU-Cantilan Campus Center for Culture and the Arts. The ceremony served as the culminating event of a two-day celebration, honoring the graduates and their achievements. <br><br>\r\n\r\nThe Graduation Ceremony commenced with a remarkable Academic Procession, featuring distinguished participants, including Academic Marshals, Candidates for Graduation, Administrative Staff, University Faculty Members, Key Officials of the University, Guests, Board of Regents, University Mace, University President, Commencement Speaker, and The Colors. The procession showcased the collective accomplishments of the university community and set the stage for the momentous event. <br><br>\r\n\r\nDr. Catherine F. Solomon, PhD (C), VPA/Board Secretary V, delivered the pronouncement, officially commencing the proceedings. The NEMSU-Cantilan Hugyaw Chorale, under the skilled direction of Mr. Paul Carmel C. Buniel, evoked a sense of pride and patriotism as they performed the Philippine National Anthem, creating an atmosphere of unity and celebration.<br><br>\r\n\r\nMs. Jasmin D. Cubillan, a distinguished graduate and Magna Cum Laude from the BSED-Science program, delivered a heartfelt salutation. She expressed gratitude and recognized the collective achievements of the graduating class, acknowledging the dedication and hard work that led them to this significant milestone.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nAn Audiovisual Presentation by Sen. Francis Joseph \"Chiz\" G. Escudero, Chair of the Senate Committee on Higher Technical Vocational Education, captivated the audience with an enlightening message. Sen. Escudero\'s words of inspiration resonated with the graduates as they embarked on their future paths. He emphasized the importance of the youth, not only as the hope of the nation but also as reliable contributors to its progress and development.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nRamona Liza A. Espenido, MST-SS, Registrar III, took the stage to attest that all graduation requirements had been fulfilled by the candidates, validating their eligibility for graduation. Dr. Juancho A. Intano, the esteemed Campus Director, proudly presented the candidates for graduation, commending their dedication and hard work throughout their academic journey.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nDr. Nemesio G. Loayon, University President III, confirmed the graduates, instilling a sense of accomplishment and pride in their hearts as they officially transitioned from students to alumni. This significant moment symbolized the culmination of their academic endeavors and the beginning of new chapters in their lives.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nA moment of recognition and appreciation followed as Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the University President, assisted by the Campus Director, Dr. Juancho A. Intano, presented a Plaque of Commendation to the Commencement Speaker. This gesture acknowledged the speaker\'s invaluable presence and contribution to the event, highlighting the significance of their role in inspiring and motivating the graduating class.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nJo Mark M. Libre, DPA, CHED Commissioner Chair, NEMSU Board of Regents, conveyed a heartfelt message through an Audiovisual Presentation. The presentation emphasized the value of education and its transformative power. It underscored the potential of the graduates to create positive change and contribute to society, reflecting the theme of the ceremony, \"Decades of Sculpting Better Lives, Envisioning a Better World.\"\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe meritorious graduates who achieved Latin Honors were honored and awarded their well-deserved medals by Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the University President. This recognition served as a testament to their exceptional academic performance and represented the culmination of their hard work and dedication.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nRepresenting Atty. Winston L. Plaza, Director IV - Civil Service Commission Caraga Regional Office, Zandroval B. Laganao, CSCFO of Surigao del Sur Supervising Human Resource Specialist, had the privilege of presenting the Civil Service Commission Eligibility awards to the deserving graduates. This accomplishment added another significant milestone to the graduates\' achievements, further enhancing their future prospects.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n Ms. Jean Vanessa B. Sapuras, the esteemed Magna Cum Laude graduate from the BSED-Mathematics program, delivered a heartfelt speech of gratitude on behalf of her fellow graduates. She expressed profound appreciation for the unwavering support received throughout their academic journey and shared their aspirations for the future. Her words echoed the sentiment of the entire graduating class, inspiring hope and determination among those in attendance.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nDr. Juancho A. Intano, the dedicated Campus Director, extended his acknowledgment and gratitude to all those who contributed to the success of the event. He recognized the efforts of the faculty, staff, and organizers in ensuring a memorable and meaningful graduation ceremony. Their commitment to providing quality education and guidance played a vital role in shaping the graduates\' future.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nMs. Ma. Venus Delilah A. Esquivel, the President of the College Alumni Association, led the alumni in reciting the Alumni Oath and Pledge of Loyalty. This symbolic act represented the graduates\' commitment to uphold the values instilled by their Alma Mater and contribute to its growth and success. It marked the beginning of their lifelong connection to the university and their dedication to supporting its mission.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe NEMSU-Cantilan Hugyaw Chorale, under the talented direction of Mr. Paul Carmel C. Buniel, created a melodious atmosphere by performing the University Hymn. The heartfelt rendition evoked a sense of nostalgia and pride among the attendees, fostering a deep connection to their alma mater.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nWith a profound sense of accomplishment and anticipation for the future, the graduates bid farewell to their Alma Mater during the Recessional March. This poignant moment marked the end of their academic journey at NEMSU-Cantilan and symbolized the beginning of new chapters in their lives.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe Graduation Ceremony of North Eastern Mindanao State University - Cantilan Campus celebrated the remarkable achievements of the graduates and their potential to shape a better world. The event honored the dedication and hard work of the graduates, faculty, staff, and supporters who sculpted better lives throughout the decades. With the theme \"Decades of Sculpting Better Lives, Envisioning a Better World,\" the ceremony encapsulated the institution\'s commitment to providing quality education and fostering future leaders who will create positive change in society\r\n\r\n</span></p>\r\n', 'comm-cantilan-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-06-29 18:20:11', '2023-06-29 18:20:11', '2023-06-29 18:20:11');
