('dd49c7df-3cc3-11ef-9551-a233a240566f', '𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝟏𝐬𝐭 𝐏𝐡𝐢𝐥𝐢𝐩𝐩𝐢𝐧𝐞 𝐇𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐞𝐫 𝐄𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐟𝐞𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐨𝐧 𝐈𝐧𝐝𝐢𝐠𝐞𝐧𝐨𝐮𝐬 𝐏𝐞𝐨𝐩𝐥𝐞𝐬 𝐄𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧', '1st-Philippine-BIGKIS-2024', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Delegation hailed as Champion for Creative Contemporary Dance Performance, 1st Runner Up for Group Vocal Performance, and 2nd Runner Up for Solo Vocal Performance during the BIGKIS: 1st Philippine Higher Education Conference on Indigenous Peoples Education held on July 5, 2024 at Bukidnon State University. ', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Delegation hailed as Champion for Creative Contemporary Dance Performance, 1st Runner Up for Group Vocal Performance, and 2nd Runner Up for Solo Vocal Performance during the BIGKIS: 1st Philippine Higher Education Conference on Indigenous Peoples Education held on July 5, 2024 at Bukidnon State University. \r\n<br><br>\r\nThe NEMSU community is proud of you!\r\n', '1st-Bigkis-Champion.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-07-05 17:48:41', '2024-07-05 17:48:41', '2024-07-05 17:48:41'),
('ddf4a368-1fad-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU - Tandag Campus 39th University Commencement Exercises', 'Tandag-Campus-39th-Commencement-Exercises', 'Attending the event are <b>CHED Comm. Jo Mark M. Libre</b>, Dr. Nelson P. Cabral (University President, Zamboanga Peninsula Polytechnic   State University,) Dr. Rolyn C. Daguil (University President,', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-14.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-13.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/comm-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nNorth Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU - Tandag Campus 39th Commencement Exercises with the theme: \"Decades of Sculpting Better Lives: Envisioning a Better World\". \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nAttending the event are <b>CHED Comm. Jo Mark M. Libre</b>, Dr. Nelson P. Cabral (University President, Zamboanga Peninsula Polytechnic   State University,) Dr. Rolyn C. Daguil (University President, Caraga State University), Atty. Ronnie Azura (Representative of the Senate Committee on Higher, Technical, and Vocational Education chaired by Honorable Senator Francis “Chiz” Escudero), NEMSU BOR Members, Stakeholders, Partners, Key Officials, Faculty, Staff, Parents and Graduating Class of 2023.\r\n <br><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:left\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n#nemsuvision #nemsutouch #presidentofthegrassroots \r\n#NEMSU2023 #GraduationDay #nemsucares #sculptingbetterlives\r\n\r\n</span></p>', 'Screenshot_00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-07-06 17:20:11', '2023-07-06 17:20:11', '2023-07-06 17:20:11'),
('ddfd0e0d-e039-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐌𝐚𝐩𝐩𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐭𝐡 𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐝: 𝐖𝐨𝐫𝐤𝐬𝐡𝐨𝐩 𝐨𝐧 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐑𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐚𝐫𝐜𝐡 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐄𝐱𝐭𝐞𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐀𝐠𝐞𝐧𝐝𝐚 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟒-𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟖', 'Mapping-path-forward-2024', 'In a bold step towards advancing academic excellence and societal impact, the Research and Extension Units of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) recently convened for a 2-Day Workshop on the Assessment and Formulation of the University\'s Research and Extension Agenda for the years 2024-2028. ', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/mapping-2024/mapping-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nIn a bold step towards advancing academic excellence and societal impact, the Research and Extension Units of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) recently convened for a 2-Day Workshop on the Assessment and Formulation of the University\'s Research and Extension Agenda for the years 2024-2028. Held on March 11-12, 2024, at Lizvil Beach Resort in Cagwait, Surigao del Sur, the workshop brought together a diverse group of research and extension personnel, all dedicated to shaping the future landscape of the university\'s units.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Rolly G. Salvaleon, Vice President for Research and Extension, spearheaded the opening program, emphasizing the timeliness of the workshop in aligning the research and extension agenda with the evolving needs of the community. With a focus on collaboration and strategic planning, the workshop aimed to set a clear direction for NEMSU\'s endeavors in research and extension.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe workshop unfolded with an appreciative inquiry approach, led by resource speakers Dr. Cesar Demayo and Dr. Mark Anthony J. Torres. Participants were guided through a journey of defining, discovering, dreaming, designing, and destiny, collectively exploring the essence of the university\'s research and extension agenda. Through reflective discussions, attendees celebrated past achievements, identified present strengths, and envisioned bold aspirations for the future, setting a positive tone for the workshop and instilling a sense of purpose and direction.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Torres introduced the System Mapping and Visual Organizer Frameworks, providing participants with a strategic tool for uncovering existing issues across the university\'s seven campuses. Through interactive exercises, attendees visualized interconnected systems, identifying bottlenecks, gaps, and opportunities for improvement. System maps offered a comprehensive overview of the complex challenges facing each campus, guiding targeted interventions and resource allocation efforts.\r\n<br><br>\r\nBuilding upon insights gleaned from visual organizers and system mapping, participants engaged in the crucial task of identifying thrusts and priorities for the university\'s research and extension agenda. Leveraging an impact and uncertainty assessment framework, attendees evaluated potential initiatives based on their anticipated level of impact and uncertainty. This evaluation process ensured strategic allocation of resources, maximizing NEMSU\'s capacity to address pressing issues effectively.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe two-day workshop on the assessment and formulation of NEMSU\'s research and extension agenda 2024-2028 exemplified the transformative power of collaboration, strategic planning, and collective action. As NEMSU continues its journey towards excellence and impact, it does so with a renewed sense of optimism and resolve, knowing that its collective efforts will shape the future for generations to come.\r\n<br/>', 'mapping-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-12 15:27:03', '2024-03-12 15:27:03', '2024-03-12 15:27:03'),
('df528b15-47bd-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', 'COD Esport Champion', 'local-masts-cod', '<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">NEMSU Cantilan, asintadong nakamit ang kampeonato sa Call of Duty Tournament laban sa kupunang Lianga.</span></p>', '<p style=\"margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">NEMSU Cantilan, asintadong nakamit ang kampeonato sa Call of Duty Tournament laban sa kupunang Lianga.<br><br>\r\n\r\nSamahang Select (Cantilan Campus) pinaulanan ng bala ang Guerilla Squad (Lianga Campus) matapos makapagtala ng 3 - 0 na puntos sa Best of Five Games sa larangang COD Esport, na ginanap sa NEMSU AVC ngayong ika - 31 ng Agosto.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n#TheVanguardPublication\r\n#LocalMASTS2023\r\n</span></span></p>', 'van-cod-00.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-08-31 13:15:13', '2023-08-31 13:15:13', '2023-08-31 13:15:13'),
('dfcaf2e7-f416-11ef-b8b6-a233a240566f', '𝟐𝐧𝐝 𝐎𝐏 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐠𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐠𝐩𝐚𝐝𝐚𝐲𝐚𝐠 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟓: 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝟐𝐧𝐝 𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬', '𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬', 'In preparation for Pagpadayag 2025: The 2nd State of the University Address of Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon, NEMSU OP conducted its 2nd Convergence held last February 17, 2025, to present and validate the university’s key accomplishments in 2024 which also serves as basis for strategic direction for the years to come. The gathering focused on the milestone achievements in Academics, Research, Extension, Infrastructure, Quality Assurance, Budget Report, and Digitalization.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn preparation for Pagpadayag 2025: The 2nd State of the University Address of Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon, NEMSU OP conducted its 2nd Convergence held last February 17, 2025, to present and validate the university’s key accomplishments in 2024 which also serves as basis for strategic direction for the years to come. The gathering focused on the milestone achievements in Academics, Research, Extension, Infrastructure, Quality Assurance, Budget Report, and Digitalization.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe 2nd Convergence marks an essential step in crafting a comprehensive State of the University Address, reflecting NEMSU’s commitment to continuous growth, excellence, and service to its academic community.\r\n', '𝐓𝐡𝐞-𝟐𝐧𝐝-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐞-𝐨𝐟-𝐭𝐡𝐞-𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲-𝐀𝐝𝐝𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-02-21 15:48:41', NULL, NULL),
('e39a0885-5c16-11ee-a632-a233a240566', 'NEMSU fortifies Gender and Development Program', 'GAD-2023', 'In a bid to strengthen the Gender and Development (GAD) program of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU), a GAD mainstream seminar took place at the Audio-Visual Center (AVC) of NEMSU-Main campus, September 22.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/gad23-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn a bid to strengthen the Gender and Development (GAD) program of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU), a GAD mainstream seminar took place at the Audio-Visual Center (AVC) of NEMSU-Main campus, September 22.<br><br>\r\nDr. Jingle M. Luna, GAD Coordinator of the College of Arts and Sciences, underscored the significance of the event in alignment with Republic Act 9710, better known as the Magna Carta for Women.<br><br>\r\n\"Republic Act 7910, also known as the Magna Carta of Women, provides that all departments shall establish or strengthen their gender and development (GAD) focal point system to catalyze and accelerate gender mainstreaming within the agency or the entire government unit.\" Dr. Luna said. <br><br>\r\nIn addition, she eloquently expressed how GAD mainstream be implemented or attributed in all NEMSU\'s programs and projects to further raise GAD awareness. \r\nMeanwhile, Dr. Abundio C. Miralles, Campus Director, stressed the need for a more profound exploration of the applicability and effectiveness of GAD, acknowledging its crucial role in society.<br><br>\r\n\"This social issue requires more in-depth exploration, especially within organizations, to promote its significance and determine its applicability and effectiveness,\" stated Dr. Miralles.<br><br>\r\nNEMSU\'s proactive approach in this regard underscores its unwavering commitment to promoting gender equality and women\'s rights, in full compliance with legal requirements.<br><br>\r\nThe seminar garnered participation from key officials, GAD coordinators, and students representing various campuses of the university.<br><br>\r\n𝘙𝘦𝘱𝘰𝘳𝘵 𝘣𝘺 𝘙𝘩𝘦𝘺 𝘈𝘯𝘵𝘰𝘯𝘺 𝘋𝘦𝘥𝘪𝘤𝘢𝘵𝘰𝘳𝘪𝘢<br>\r\n𝘗𝘩𝘰𝘵𝘰𝘴 𝘣𝘺 𝘒𝘪𝘯𝘨 𝘉𝘰𝘯𝘰 𝘉𝘰𝘳𝘥𝘢𝘴 & 𝘑𝘢𝘷𝘦 𝘈𝘣𝘳𝘪𝘨𝘰<br><br>\r\n#TheVanguardPublication\r\n', 'gad23-00.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-09-23 17:59:11', '2023-09-23 17:59:11', '2023-09-23 17:59:11'),
('e57c153f-f867-11ed-affb-a600064b4626', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU successfully conducted the 2nd Quarter Special Board of Regents (BOR) meeting held at SNSU-Del Carmen Campus Boardroom.', '2nd-Quarter-Special-Board-of-Regents-(BOR)-meeting', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/snsu-bor7.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">The North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU successfully conducted the 2nd Quarter Special Board of Regents (BOR) meeting held at SNSU-Del Carmen Campus Boardroom.  Presided by the good CHED Comm. Jo Mark M. Libre.</p> <br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> It is then attended by resource persons by members of the Office of Solicitor General headed by Justice James L. Cundangan, Hon. Ronnie Azura representing the Office of Hon. Sen. Chiz Escudero as oversight officer, and RD George Colorado from CHEDRO Caraga.</p>', 'snsu-bor0.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-05-15 18:11:02', '2023-05-15 18:11:02', '2023-05-15 18:11:02'),
('e704d5c3-3278-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', '𝗙𝗲𝗹𝗹𝗼𝘄𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽 𝗡𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁 𝗯𝗼𝘄𝘀 𝘂𝗻𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗶𝘁𝘆’𝘀 𝘀𝘂𝗰𝗰𝗲𝘀𝘀', 'Fellowship-Night', 'Gratitude, responsibility, and enjoyment resonated the venue as faculty and staff of North Eastern Mindanao State University rejoiced in celebrating the institution’s 2nd University Day during the Fellowship Night, July 31.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/oath_01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/oath_02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/oath_03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nGratitude, responsibility, and enjoyment resonated the venue as faculty and staff of North Eastern Mindanao State University rejoiced in celebrating the institution’s 2nd University Day during the Fellowship Night, July 31.\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nMarking another milestone for the university, President Nemesio G. Loayon recognized and honored the competence and achievements of students, faculty, and staff.\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n“This is a remarkable occasion for us to come together as a community to honor the achievements of our students, faculty, and staff. . . and the recognition of excellence that we are receiving since from our predecessors,” he highlighted.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nHe then added that those achievements were all because of great commitment and dedication of NEMSU workforce.\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nMoreover, President Loayon led the oath-taking of the newly appointed employees and challenged them to continue the excellence that the institution has been doing. \r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n“We have to reflect, discern on how far we have gone, what are the things we have accomplished and the things we still need to do,” he accentuated.\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nAfterwards, cultural presentation and foam party took the night, making the event more entertaining and lively.\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\nWritten by Niño Nickel Suazo <br>\r\nPhotos by MJ Espinoza & Jave Avrigo', 'oath_00.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-01 08:50:53', '2023-08-01 08:50:53', '2023-08-01 08:50:53'),
('e74fc378-221a-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU LIBRARIANS’ MEETING AND WORKSHOP', 'Librarian-Meeting', '', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>In preparation for the upcoming ISO 9001: 2005 the Library Management of North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) conducted a two days NEMSU Librarians ‘Meeting and Workshop held at Big Times Beach Resort, Lianga, Surigao Del Sur last June 23-24, 2022 spearheaded by the Director of Libraries, Mrs. Aida C. Osorio with the approval of the University President, Dr. Baceledes R. Estal.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe meeting/workshop begun with a prayer via multimedia presentation followed by a welcome address from Ms. Jehoney V. Alboroto, MSLIS Lianga Campus Librarian.\r\nMs. Michelle Ann U. Ortega facilitated the workshop. The agenda were: 1) Revision of Unit Manual; Collection Development Policy Statement; Library Staff Development Plan and ISO documents requirements on the Processes: QOP, SOP, QOM, RR…. The focus of the discussion was the Revision of the Unit Manual. It was agreed that some forms will be deleted. The Context of the Diagram was also tackled during the workshop. Ms. Ortega created the Process Description which the Consultant required during the ISO Training at Grand Monique, Tandag City. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nOn the second day, the meeting/workshop begun with a prayer via multimedia presentation followed by a recap of day 1 by Ms. Relina J. Balili, RL Cagwait Campus Librarian. Thorough discussions were made on the continuation of the meeting/workshop. Important topics were also discussed. \r\nThe meeting ended at 5:00 pm with a photo op.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libmeet02.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/libmeet03.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'libmeet01.jpg', 'Melanie L. Marquez, RL', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-06-24 08:09:53', '2022-06-24 08:09:53', '2022-06-24 08:09:53'),
('e9e7c515-5778-11ee-b55e-a233a240566f', 'Online Legal Consultation', 'Online-Law-23', 'In celebration of the National Law Week 2023 and the 3rd Founding Anniversary of NEMSU College of Law,', '\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn celebration of the National Law Week 2023 and the 3rd Founding Anniversary of NEMSU College of Law, through BULIG-Legal Assistance Center, we are delighted to extend to you FREE ONLINE LEGAL CONSULTATION! <br><br>\r\nThis activity is exclusive only for NEMSU System\'s Employees and Students.\r\nPlease see the attached photo for further reference.\r\n\r\n', 'law-week23-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-09-19 17:33:11', '2023-09-19 17:33:11', '2023-09-19 17:33:11'),
('ea09ff0c-db57-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐋𝐚𝐮𝐧𝐜𝐡𝐞𝐬 𝐁𝐨𝐥𝐝 𝐈𝐧𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐞: 𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐮𝐚𝐥 𝐑𝐞𝐯𝐢𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐖𝐨𝐫𝐤𝐬𝐡𝐨𝐩 𝐁𝐞𝐠𝐢𝐧𝐬', 'Manual-Revision-2024', 'NEMSU commenced its manual revision workshop. Set in Cantilan from February 27 to March 2, 2024, the event gathered its academic leaders from across the system and underscored the university\'s commitment to its endeavor.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/manual-24-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nNEMSU commenced its manual revision workshop. Set in Cantilan from February 27 to March 2, 2024, the event gathered its academic leaders from across the system and underscored the university\'s commitment to its endeavor.\r\nAfter 12 years, the academe embarked on a journey to revise its foundational blueprint, setting the university for growth across student, faculty, and administrative domains. Dr. Miralles, in his welcoming remarks, articulated the gravity of the task at hand, emphasizing the dichotomy between success and failure and the imperative of triumph.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Dela Cerna realigned participants with their roles in the revision process, laying the groundwork for collaborative engagement. Dr. Salvaleon, meanwhile, elucidated the strategic framework guiding the write shop, highlighting the significance of gap analysis, legal compliance, and transparent methodologies.\r\nAs participants immersed themselves in the revision process, focusing on their assigned manuals, the workshop bore witness to a sense of camaraderie and shared purpose. The evening\'s fellowship program provided a respite from the day\'s rigors, fostering an environment of positivity and resilience.\r\n<br><br>\r\nAfter the initial instructions on the first day, each group delved into manual revisions throughout the remainder of the five-day workshop. In his visit, the University President made remarks to ensure that the proposed changes to be embedded in the manuals are aligned with the existing legal provision of the country and the mandates of the Commission on Higher Education and other regulating agencies. The collaborative efforts culminated on the final day, where groups presented their reports to members of the academic community.\r\nFollowing this intensive endeavor, the institution plans to showcase the outputs in a public forum involving stakeholders before submitting them for endorsement to the board.\r\n<br><br>\r\nWith eyes set firmly on the horizon, the university remains steadfast in its mission to effect change through the revision of its foundational documents, signaling a transformative chapter in its history.\r\n<br/>', 'manual24-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-05 08:51:11', '2024-03-05 08:51:11', '2024-03-05 08:51:11'),
('ea2033b0-0b3b-11ee-affb-a600064b4626', 'Benchmarking of the team at the University of Science and Technology of Southern Philippines (USTP) for the College of Medicine on June 2, 2023. The team also looked into its Recruitment and Selection Plan, Faculty Development Plan, among other concerns.', 'BENCHMARK-USTP-Medicine', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp13.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp14.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp15.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/ustp16.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Benchmarking of the team at the University of Science and Technology of Southern Philippines (USTP) for the College of Medicine on June 2, 2023. The team also looked into its Recruitment and Selection Plan, Faculty Development Plan, among other concerns.\r\nThe team is headed by the Vice President for Academic Affairs, Prof. Maria Lady Sol A. Suazo, with the following members:\r\nDr. Roel T. Lim- HRMO III\r\nMs. Eunice T. Prado- HRMA\r\nAtty. Cristian Lee Ramirez- Law Faculty\r\nMs. Leorelie Kim E. Dahan- SAO for Finance\r\nDr. Mariel Sanchez- Midwifery Faculty\r\nDr. Abundio C. Miralles- OSWD Director\r\nDr. Mick Mars P. Silvano- Executive Assistant III\r\nThe University of Science and Technology of Southern Philippines (USTP) is a state university established on August 16, 2016, by Republic Act 10919 through the amalgamation of the Mindanao University of Science and Technology (MUST) in Cagayan de Oro City, Misamis Oriental and the Misamis Oriental State College of Agriculture and Technology (MOSCAT) in Claveria, Misamis Oriental. It is located in Northern Mindanao, the Gateway to Mindanao, which offers a strategic locational advantage for the institution to train and develop students from all the other regions.</span></p>', 'ustp01.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-06-12 15:33:11', '2023-06-12 15:33:11', '2023-06-12 15:33:11'),
('eb12181f-f9e4-11ed-affb-a600064b4626', 'Conducting the Management Review on the compliance of the results/findings during the ISO 9001:2015 Outsource Internal Audit Review and Pre-Assessment Audit', 'ISO 9001-2015', '', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/iso-6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br />\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU is conducting the Management Review on the compliance of the results/findings during the ISO 9001:2015 Outsource Internal Audit Review and Pre-Assessment Audit. NEMSU President Dr. Loayon presided over the meeting with the members of top management. This is aligned with NEMSU\'s commitment to Quality Policy, adhering to international standards for quality and excellent services.</span></p>', 'iso-0.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-05-24 11:30:02', '2023-05-24 11:30:02', '2023-05-24 11:30:02'),
('eb98c7e4-3cba-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Cagwait Campus - Class Opening for A.Y. 2023-2024', 'Class-cag-2023', 'A triumphant start to the new academic year as NEMSU Cagwait kicks off the S.Y 2023-2024 with a', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/cagopen-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝐀 𝐭𝐫𝐢𝐮𝐦𝐩𝐡𝐚𝐧𝐭 𝐬𝐭𝐚𝐫𝐭 𝐭𝐨 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐧𝐞𝐰 𝐚𝐜𝐚𝐝𝐞𝐦𝐢𝐜 𝐲𝐞𝐚𝐫 𝐚𝐬 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐂𝐚𝐠𝐰𝐚𝐢𝐭 𝐤𝐢𝐜𝐤𝐬 𝐨𝐟𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐒.𝐘 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟑-𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟒 𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡 𝐚 𝐫𝐞𝐦𝐚𝐫𝐤𝐚𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐨𝐩𝐞𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐜𝐥𝐚𝐬𝐬 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐢𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐭𝐟𝐮𝐥 𝐨𝐫𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧. 𝐇𝐞𝐫𝐞\'𝐬 𝐭𝐨 𝐚 𝐲𝐞𝐚𝐫 𝐟𝐢𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐝 𝐰𝐢𝐭𝐡 𝐛𝐨𝐮𝐧𝐝𝐥𝐞𝐬𝐬 𝐨𝐩𝐩𝐨𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐧𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐞𝐬 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐨𝐮𝐭𝐬𝐭𝐚𝐧𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐜𝐡𝐢𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬!\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n#NEMSUOrientation <br>\r\n#NewBeginnings\r\n', 'cagopen-00.jpg', 'NEMSU Cagwait Campus', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-14 21:41:52', '2023-08-14 21:41:52', '2023-08-14 21:41:52'),
('ed76b651-e048-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐀𝐒𝐓𝐌𝐌𝐂 𝐆𝐚𝐢𝐧𝐬 𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐭𝐬 𝐟𝐫𝐨𝐦 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔’𝐬 𝐏𝐫𝐢𝐦𝐞 𝐇𝐑𝐌 𝐋𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐥 𝐈𝐈 𝐁𝐞𝐬𝐭 𝐏𝐫𝐚𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐜𝐞𝐬', 'ASTMMC-NEMSU-BEST-Practices', 'North Eastern Mindanao State University welcomes the HR personnel from the Adela Serra T. Memorial Medical Center (ASTMMC) for their Benchmarking Activity on Prime HRM Level II at NEMSU Main Campus New Board Room on March 12, 2024.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/bench-astmmc-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/mapping-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/mapping-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/astmmc-2024/mapping-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nNorth Eastern Mindanao State University welcomes the HR personnel from the Adela Serra T. Memorial Medical Center (ASTMMC) for their Benchmarking Activity on Prime HRM Level II at NEMSU Main Campus New Board Room on March 12, 2024.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Janice V. Pagaran-Alcordo, the Officer-in-Charge Medical Center Chief II, led the ASTMMC HR team and received a warm welcome from key NEMSU officials, including Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the University President; Dr. Abundio C. Miralles, Vice President for Administration and Finance; Dr. Florife Urbiztondo, Chief Administrative Officer; Prof. Evelyn T. Bagood, the Campus Director of NEMSU Main; Engr. Christopher D. Badayos, the Supervising Administrative Officer for Admin, and Mr. Roel T. Lim, NEMSU HRMO III, along with other NEMSU HR personnel.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe focal point of the benchmarking activity is centered around strategic performance management systems and the recognition and rewards framework implemented at NEMSU. The event also facilitated an exchange of best practices, fostering a collaborative atmosphere for the benefit of both institutions.\r\nIn his message, Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon expressed his enthusiasm for the collaboration and benchmarking with ASTMMC. He sees this as not just an event but the inception of a journey towards a partnership for a mutually beneficial future marked by elevated HR management for both NEMSU and ASTMMC.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe cooperative spirit displayed during the benchmarking activity signifies a commendable leap forward in fostering excellence and ensuring continuous improvement in the realm of human resource management.\r\n<br/>', 'bench-astmmc-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-12 16:14:57', '2024-03-12 16:14:57', '2024-03-12 16:14:57'),
('ee56cadc-7f60-11ee-bea4-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU Debate Guilds', 'Debate-2023', 'In a clash of wits and words, the North Eastern Mindanao State University\'s Debate Guild brought back the coveted Roving Trophy with Team NEMSU A, consisting of John Hope Plaza, Jericka Soria, and John Damort Guingguing, who also secured the Top 3 Best Speakers slot in the competition.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐃𝐞𝐛𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐆𝐮𝐢𝐥𝐝 𝐫𝐞𝐜𝐥𝐚𝐢𝐦𝐬 𝐂𝐡𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬𝐡𝐢𝐩 𝐓𝐫𝐨𝐩𝐡𝐲 𝐢𝐧 𝐒𝐈𝐏𝐃𝐂<br>\r\n\r\nIn a clash of wits and words, the North Eastern Mindanao State University\'s Debate Guild brought back the coveted Roving Trophy with Team NEMSU A, consisting of John Hope Plaza, Jericka Soria, and John Damort Guingguing, who also secured the Top 3 Best Speakers slot in the competition.\r\n<br>\r\nSurigao Intervarsity Parliamentary Debate Championship (SIPDC) is a Surigao-based tournament that welcomes debaters all across the province. During the 5th installment of the tournament, NEMSU was able to bag the championship but was unable to sustain it in the subsequent edition due to the lack of competing teams.\r\n<br>\r\nMeanwhile, NEMSU B, composed of Piaa Stanly Samontina, Prince John Bert Buiza, and Reach Chell Javier, also made waves in the competition in the pre-semifinals, bagging several best speaker awards in the process.\r\n<br>\r\nCompeting adjudicators from the Guild also displayed dominance, as Daniel Pedarse, Rysan Engrova, Aubrey Macalde, and Rejonh Kenneth Alabat secured their spots as breaking adjudicators, as well as reaping several Best Judge awards.\r\n<br>\r\nDebate Adviser Mark Jade Burlat expressed his gratitude to the NEMSU administration for the financial assistance and shared that the overwhelming support from family and friends was the reason that fueled their participation.\r\n<br>\r\n\"With the Roving Trophy back to NEMSU again, we will continue our rigorous yet fun trainings, breed new competing teams, and cultivate the culture of debate in the university,\" Mr. Burlat added.\r\n<br>\r\nIt is definitely a huge leap for the Guild from a budding debate organization to an established powerhouse in the Surigao circuit.', 'debate.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-10-31 09:04:23', '2023-10-31 09:04:23', '2023-10-31 09:04:23'),
('ee6b4577-0055-11ef-904a-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐭𝐬 𝐅𝐈𝐍𝐂𝐎𝐌 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐢𝐧 𝐏𝐫𝐞𝐩𝐚𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐒𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐢𝐚𝐥 𝐁𝐎𝐑 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠', 'FINCOM-Meeting-2024', 'In anticipation of the upcoming Special Board of Regents (BOR) Meeting, North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) held a Finance Committee (FINCOM) Meeting on April 17, 2024, at the  New Boardroom, NEMSU-Tandag Campus.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/FINCOM-2024/fin-com-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/FINCOM-2024/fin-com-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/FINCOM-2024/fin-com-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nIn anticipation of the upcoming Special Board of Regents (BOR) Meeting, North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) held a Finance Committee (FINCOM) Meeting on April 17, 2024, at the  New Boardroom, NEMSU-Tandag Campus.\r\nThe session was presided over by the esteemed Chairperson, Engr. Noel M. Ajoc, who serves as the Regional Director of the Department of Science and Technology in Caraga. Alongside Director Ajoc, the meeting convened with the participation of notable members and key officials of the university.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe primary agenda of the FINCOM Meeting was to meticulously deliberate upon administrative matters that had been endorsed by the joint councils during the ACO-ADCO session, which took place in Cantilan on April 12, 2024. These matters were carefully scrutinized, ensuring thorough consideration before eventual submission for approval to the Board of Regents.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe FINCOM Meeting served as a crucial precursor to the impending Special BOR Meeting, which is poised to address significant decisions pertinent to the university\'s future trajectory. \r\n<br><br>\r\nBy meticulously reviewing administrative matters and ensuring alignment with the institution\'s strategic objectives, NEMSU remains steadfast in its commitment to excellence in higher education.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe outcomes of the FINCOM Meeting are expected to shape the deliberations of the forthcoming Special BOR Meeting, further solidifying NEMSU\'s position as a beacon of academic excellence in the region.\r\n<br/>', 'fin-com-00.png', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-04-17 11:43:41', '2024-04-17 11:43:41', '2024-04-17 11:43:41');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `short_description`, `content`, `photo`, `author`, `office_id`, `type`, `is_published`, `date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
('ef1f32b3-db7b-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐁𝐮𝐢𝐥𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐁𝐫𝐢𝐝𝐠𝐞𝐬: 𝐀𝐒𝐒𝐂𝐀𝐓 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐠𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐭𝐡 𝐭𝐨 𝐄𝐱𝐜𝐞𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞 𝐓𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐠𝐡 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐚𝐛𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧', 'PQA-2024', 'In a significant stride towards academic advancement, the Agusan del Sur State College of Agriculture and Technology (ASSCAT) embarked on a collaborative journey with North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) aimed at leveraging their respective strengths through benchmarking initiatives. The visit to NEMSU\'s Main Campus marked the beginning of a promising partnership aimed at driving impactful change and propelling both institutions towards Philippine Quality Awards.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/pqa-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/pqa-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/pqa-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nIn a significant stride towards academic advancement, the Agusan del Sur State College of Agriculture and Technology (ASSCAT) embarked on a collaborative journey with North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) aimed at leveraging their respective strengths through benchmarking initiatives. The visit to NEMSU\'s Main Campus marked the beginning of a promising partnership aimed at driving impactful change and propelling both institutions towards Philippine Quality Awards.\r\nKey officials, including NEMSU President Prof. Nemesio G. Loayon ,Campus Director Prof. Evelyn T. Bagood, and unit representatives warmly welcomed the ASSCAT delegation at the Quality Assurance Office. The atmosphere was one of camaraderie and mutual respect as both parties gathered to discuss the collaborative opportunities ahead.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn his address, Prof. Loayon expressed wholehearted support for the collaboration, recognizing it as a bold step towards harnessing collective strengths. He emphasized the importance of partnerships grounded in shared goals and a commitment to academic excellence. Prof. Loayon assured the ASSCAT delegation of NEMSU\'s unwavering assistance in accomplishing the objectives of their benchmarking initiatives, underscoring the spirit of cooperation that defines this partnership.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe collaboration between ASSCAT and NEMSU signifies more than just an exchange of ideas; it represents a commitment to driving positive change and societal impact through education and research. By navigating partnerships built on mutual respect and a shared vision, both institutions are poised to serve as catalysts for innovation and progress in the field of higher education.\r\n<br><br>\r\nAs ASSCAT and NEMSU embark on this collaborative journey, they stand as examples of the transformative power of cooperation and shared endeavor. Through their joint efforts, they are building bridges that will not only strengthen their own institutions but also pave the way for a brighter future for generations to come.\r\n<br/>', 'pqa-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-06 21:04:23', '2024-03-06 21:04:23', '2024-03-06 21:04:23'),
('ef2a46df-82f1-11ee-bea4-a233a240566f', '𝗠𝗔𝗦𝗧𝗦 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟯: In preparation for the upcoming Mindanao-wide competition, a strategic meeting was held earlier at the Audio Visual Center, NEMSU-Main Campus.', 'Masts-2023-Preparation', '𝗠𝗔𝗦𝗧𝗦 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟯: In preparation for the upcoming Mindanao-wide competition, a strategic meeting was held earlier at the Audio Visual Center, NEMSU-Main Campus.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/masts23-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝗠𝗔𝗦𝗧𝗦 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟯: In preparation for the upcoming Mindanao-wide competition, a strategic meeting was held earlier at the Audio Visual Center, NEMSU-Main Campus.\r\nDr. Shyla O. Moreno, Director of Culture and the Arts, led the session which was attended by NEMSU participants and coaches. Moreover, crucial topics with regards to travel schedules, flow of events, expenses, and finalization of the participants were planned and discussed.\r\n<br>\r\nEmphasizing the meticulous process, the meeting also tackled the rules and measures to ensure the overall success of the participants for the literary, musical, dance, theater, and visual arts competitions. The meeting underscored NEMSU\'s commitment to achieving victory in all categories.\r\n<br>\r\nThe MASTS Culture and Arts Festival is scheduled to take place from November 21 to 25, 2023, in Kabacan, Cotabato City, ensuring an energetic commemoration of culture and artistic excellence with 33 participating universities.\r\n<br>\r\nReport by Roger Bagood<br>\r\nPhotos by Jave Abrigo and Roger Bagood<br>\r\n#TheVanguardPublication', 'masts23-00.jpg', 'The Vanguard Publication', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-11-14 19:33:11', '2023-11-14 19:33:11', '2023-11-14 19:33:11'),
('f0ceb802-e656-11ee-987e-a233a240566f', '𝐓𝐚𝐧𝐝𝐚𝐠 𝐂𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐂𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐥 𝐅𝐢𝐫𝐞 𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐬𝐩𝐨𝐧𝐬𝐨𝐫𝐬 𝐅𝐢𝐫𝐞 𝐒𝐚𝐟𝐞𝐭𝐲 𝐒𝐞𝐦𝐢𝐧𝐚𝐫 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐃𝐫𝐢𝐥𝐥 𝐚𝐭 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐓𝐚𝐧𝐝𝐚𝐠 𝐂𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐮𝐬', 'FireDrill-2024', 'In an effort to promote fire safety awareness and preparedness, the Tandag City Central Fire Station recently sponsored a Fire Safety Seminar and Drill at NEMSU Tandag Campus on March 18, 2024.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/2024/Fire-Drill/drill-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nThe event was attended by the Campus Director of Tandag, Dr. Evelyn T. Bagood, along with other key officials, program coordinators, medical team, faculty and staff, unit heads, and students of the university. The seminar featured a comprehensive discussion on fire safety protocols, prevention measures, and emergency response procedures, delivered by fire officers from the Tandag City Central Fire Station as resource speakers.\r\n<br><br>\r\nOne of the key highlights of the event was a practical demonstration on how to correctly use a fire extinguisher to stop a fire. Participants were taught the proper technique of operating a fire extinguisher, including the PASS method - Pull the pin, Aim the nozzle at the base of the fire, Squeeze the handle, and Sweep from side to side.\r\n<br><br>\r\nFollowing the instructional session, participants actively engaged in a fire drill to put their newfound knowledge into practice. The drill simulated a fire emergency scenario, allowing participants to demonstrate their ability to evacuate the premises safely and efficiently. The participants had the opportunity also to practice using a fire extinguisher in a controlled environment during the fire drill. This hands-on experience allowed them to gain confidence in their ability to effectively extinguish a small fire and prevent it from spreading.\r\n<br><br>\r\nDr. Bagood commended the Tandag City Central Fire Station for its comprehensive and interactive approach to fire safety education. She emphasized the importance of equipping individuals with the necessary skills and knowledge to respond to fire emergencies promptly and effectively.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe successful conclusion of the Fire Safety Seminar and Drill at North Eastern Mindanao State University, which included practical training on using fire extinguishers, underscores the importance of proactive measures in ensuring fire safety in educational institutions and communities. The collaboration between the university and the Tandag City Central Fire Station, with a focus on practical fire safety skills, sets a positive example for promoting fire safety awareness and preparedness in the region.\r\n<br/>', 'drill-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-03-18 17:09:26', '2024-03-18 17:09:26', '2024-03-18 17:09:26'),
('f237fba9-a44d-11ee-9af6-a233a240566f', 'Meeting together with USEP President and Officials regarding the transfer of properties to NEMSU Bislig (formerly USEP Bislig).', 'NEMSU-Bislig', 'Meeting together with USEP President and Officials regarding the transfer of properties to NEMSU Bislig (formerly USEP Bislig).', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/usep-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/usep-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/usep-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n', 'usep-00.jpg', 'NEMSU Pres. Nemesio G. Loayon', 0, 'news', 1, '2023-12-22 11:33:11', '2023-12-22 11:33:11', '2023-12-22 11:33:11'),
('f424dc2b-6c86-11ee-a3fc-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU celebrates its Family Day', 'Family-Day-2023', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University - NEMSU Main Campus celebrates its Family Day with the theme: \"Transforming Public Service in the Next Decade: Honing Agile and Future-Ready Servant-Heroes\" at Arena Blanca Beach Resort, Britania, San Agustin, Surigao del Sur.', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-08.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-09.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-11.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-12.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-13.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-14.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-15.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-16.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-17.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/csc-18.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>', 'csc-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-10-04 08:33:11', '2023-10-04 08:33:11', '2023-10-04 08:33:11'),
('f517f2c3-1f8f-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU - San Miguel Campus 66th University Commencement Exercises', 'SM-Campus-66-Commencement-Exercises', 'Step into a world of celebration and joy as the Graduating Class of 2023 from North Eastern Mindanao State University - San Miguel Campus embarks on an extraordinary journey!', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/sm-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/sm-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/sm-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Step into a world of celebration and joy as the Graduating Class of 2023 from North Eastern Mindanao State University - San Miguel Campus embarks on an extraordinary journey! With the theme \"Decades of Sculpting Better Lives, envisioning a Better World,\" these graduating students have been transformed into exceptional individuals ready to make a positive impact. Their dreams and aspirations shine brightly, illuminating the path to a brighter future. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nToday, amidst an atmosphere of excitement, we gather at the NEMSU Training Center to witness their confirmation as graduates, a moment filled with anticipation and promise. Their hard work, dedication, and growth have paved the way for this significant achievement. As they prepare to embark on their own unique journeys, may these graduates carry the knowledge, skills, and values instilled by NEMSU.\r\n<br><br>\r\n \r\nLet their passion and determination propel them towards making a difference in the world, sculpting better lives for themselves and others. So, let us come together in celebration, honoring the Graduating Class of 2023. Congratulations on reaching this milestone, and may your future be filled with endless opportunities and success as you shape a better world for all!\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:left\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n#NEMSU2023 #GraduationDay #nemsucares #sculptingbetterlives\r\n\r\n</span></p>', 'sm-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 32, 'news', 1, '2023-06-30 17:20:11', '2023-06-30 17:20:11', '2023-06-30 17:20:11'),
('f5af6ef7-4085-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU Academic Community convenes for System-wide Curriculum Enhancement', 'Curr-2023', 'With a focus on streamlining and unifying the course syllabi across programs, executives and faculty members from all campuses of North Eastern Mindanao State University assembled inside the Audio-Visual Center for the launching of the 2-day Curriculum Enhancement, August 17-18, 2023.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nWith a focus on streamlining and unifying the course syllabi across programs, executives and faculty members from all campuses of North Eastern Mindanao State University assembled inside the Audio-Visual Center for the launching of the 2-day Curriculum Enhancement, August 17-18, 2023. <br><br>\r\nDr. Erwin Berry, the Director for Curriculum Development, sparked the discussion as he delivered an overview of the procedures in developing an outcomes-based syllabus, along with the statement of purpose to set the tone for the academic convergence.<br><br>\r\nMoreover, University President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, duly represented by Vice President for Academic Affairs Dr. Maria Lady Sol Suazo, expressed the pivotal role of this activity to ensure that the students can satisfy the expected competencies upon graduation.<br><br>\r\n“The university president, Dr. Loayon, is very much confident that this activity will proceed to the right direction, and this is really a very opportune time for all of us because it will also help us grow professionally,” the VPAA affirmed.\r\nSome of the salient subjects of discussion were the various concerns raised by the teaching faculty, including the universality of teaching methods, the time needed to construct syllabi, and the potential implementation of the new syllabi in the second semester of the academic year. <br><br>\r\nConsequently, one significant solution proposed during the event was the revision and unification of the old curriculum. This approach suggests that rather than starting syllabi from scratch, the university should focus on refining and aligning the current curriculum to meet modern educational standards. \r\nOne unified syllabus per program is expected to be the outcome by the end of the two-day gathering, reshaping the academic experience in the university in favor of a more harmonized curricular foundation.\r\n<br>', 'cur-00.png', 'The Vanguard Publication', 11, 'news', 1, '2023-08-18 12:20:02', '2023-08-18 12:20:02', '2023-08-18 12:20:02'),
('f5b3a486-91e1-11f0-a6c6-a233a240566f', '‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴 𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀 𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮 𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼, 𝘄𝗶𝗻𝘀 𝘀𝗲𝗰𝗼𝗻𝗱 𝗿𝘂𝗻𝗻𝗲𝗿-𝘂𝗽 𝘁𝗶𝘁𝗹𝗲 𝗶𝗻 𝗣𝗮𝗶𝗻𝘀𝗮𝘆𝗮𝘄 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱\r\n‎', '‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼', '‎North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Tandag Campus mentors placed 2nd Runner-Up in Painsayaw (Paindigay sa Sayaw) 2025 after presenting a performance inspired by the traditions of the Sama Badjao community during the opening of the 13th Sangkaan Festival at the Vicente T. Pimentel Jr. Memorial Gymnasium on September 5.', '<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼 6.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n‎North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Tandag Campus mentors placed 2nd Runner-Up in Painsayaw (Paindigay sa Sayaw) 2025 after presenting a performance inspired by the traditions of the Sama Badjao community during the opening of the 13th Sangkaan Festival at the Vicente T. Pimentel Jr. Memorial Gymnasium on September 5.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\n‎With the theme “Pagkabalaan sanan Pagkamalig-on Ipadayon, Para sa Dugang Kalambuan Kanato mga Tandaganon,” the competition featured five participating schools that staged cultural dances showcasing the identity, history, and resilience of the Tandaganon.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\n‎The NEMSU contingent interpreted Sama Badjao heritage through choreography, costumes, and storytelling to underscore the community’s cultural significance in Tandag City.\r\n‎\r\n‎Jacinto P. Elpa National High School (JPENHS) won the championship and a ₱60,000 cash prize, while Tandag District 2 finished as first runner-up.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\n‎Photos by Hans Abordo', '‎𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗴-𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀-𝗦𝗮𝗺𝗮-𝗕𝗮𝗱𝗷𝗮𝗼.jpg', 'Arnold Rivera', 0, 'news', 1, '2025-09-05 11:04:31', NULL, NULL),
('f79c40d8-3cbc-11ee-a66e-a233a240566f', 'Tagbina Campus - Class Opening for A.Y. 2023-2024', 'Class-tag-2023', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University- Tagbina Campus kicked off the new academic year with a spectacular event that left both', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-01.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/tag-open-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n𝗘𝘅𝗰𝗶𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗕𝗲𝗴𝗶𝗻𝗻𝗶𝗻𝗴𝘀 𝗔𝘄𝗮𝗶𝘁 𝗮𝘁 𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨-𝗧𝗖 <br>\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University- Tagbina Campus kicked off the new academic year with a spectacular event that left both freshmen and returning students buzzing with excitement. The campus gymnasium was abuzz with energy as students gathered to attend the opening of classes and a comprehensive re (orientation).<br>\r\nWelcoming both newcomers and familiar faces, the university\'s administration pulled out all the stops to ensure an engaging and informative event. \r\n<br/>\r\n', 'tag-open-000.jpg', 'The Blaze - NEMSU Tagbina', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-08-14 22:41:52', '2023-08-14 22:41:52', '2023-08-14 22:41:52'),
('f8275c69-28ce-11ef-8173-a233a240566f', '𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭 𝐂𝐨𝐦𝐦𝐢𝐭𝐭𝐞𝐞 𝐌𝐞𝐞𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠', 'Management-Committee-Meeting-June-11', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) is convening a Management Committee (MANCOM) meeting', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) is convening a Management Committee (MANCOM) meeting, attended by the University\'s key officials. Presided over by University President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, the meeting is taking place in the New Conference Room.\r\n</p>\r\n', '650x600-Mancom.png', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-06-11 23:17:37', '2024-06-11 23:17:37', '2024-06-11 23:17:37'),
('fd0d6ae8-8ed8-11ef-bdca-a233a240566f', '𝐍𝐞𝐰𝐥𝐲 𝐇𝐢𝐫𝐞𝐝 𝐓𝐞𝐚𝐜𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐍𝐨𝐧-𝐭𝐞𝐚𝐜𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐏𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐨𝐧𝐧𝐞𝐥 𝐨𝐟 𝐍𝐄𝐌𝐒𝐔 𝐓𝐚𝐤𝐞 𝐎𝐚𝐭𝐡 𝐢𝐧 𝐂𝐞𝐫𝐞𝐦𝐨𝐧𝐲 𝐋𝐞𝐝 𝐛𝐲 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐏𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐧𝐭', 'Newly-Hired-Teaching-and-Non-Teaching-Personnel', 'The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) formally welcomed its newest members during the Oath Taking Ceremony held on October 16, 2024, at the NEMSU Main Campus. ', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nCagwait, Surigao del Sur - August 5, 2024, North Eastern Mindanao State University The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) formally welcomed its newest members during the Oath Taking Ceremony held on October 16, 2024, at the NEMSU Main Campus. Presiding over the event was University President Dr. Nemesio G. Loayon, who not only administered the official oath but also delivered a message filled with challenge and encouragement for the fresh members of the NEMSU family.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThe ceremony, held in the university\'s gymnasium, was a testament to NEMSU\'s continued commitment to excellence in education and community service. Dr. Loayon emphasized the critical roles that both teaching and non-teaching staff play in shaping the institution\'s future and urged the newly hired personnel to uphold the values of integrity, innovation, and service.\r\n<br><br>\r\nThis ceremony highlights NEMSU’s ongoing efforts to strengthen its workforce with capable and dedicated professionals, ensuring that the university remains at the forefront of academic excellence and public service.', 'oath-october-00.jpg', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-10-16 19:44:17', '2024-10-16 19:44:17', '2024-10-16 19:44:17'),
('fd3ab59e-2211-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU LIBRARIANS PARTICIPATED IN TREE-PLANTING ACTIVITY', 'tree-plantng-2023', '', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>The North Eastern Mindanao State University (NEMSU) Librarians participated in the Tree Planting Activity (Arbor Day) last June 25, 2022, at Barangay Bahi, Barobo, Surigao Del Sur as part of the celebration of the PRC\'s 49th Founding Anniversary and PRC Week Celebration 2022, with the theme “PRC @49: Forging Ahead Towards PROFESSIONALISM, RESILIENCY, AND COMPETITIVENESS.”\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe participation of the PRC is anchored on PRC Resolution No. 1251 series of 2020 which declares the 25th of June every year as PRC Nationwide Tree Planting Day and makes it a part of the PRC Week Celebration.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nPursuant to Republic Act No. 10912, otherwise known as the “Continuing Professional Development (CPD) Act of 2016”, an act which requires CPD as the mandatory requirement for the renewal of Professional Identification Card of all registered and licensed professionals under the regulation of the PRC each professional who actively participated in the event will be given with six (6) unit points.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/planting02.png\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md6 col-sm-6 col-lg-6\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/planting03.png\" />\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'planting01.png', 'Melanie L. Marquez, RL', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-06-25 08:09:53', '2022-06-25 08:09:53', '2022-06-25 08:09:53'),
('fed63ebc-1fa0-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU - Tagbina Campus 30th University Commencement Exercises', 'Tagbina-Campus-30th-Commencement-Exercises', 'In a momentous event held this afternoon, the University gymnasium was filled with jubilant faces as 508 graduates, along with their proud parents, key officials, administrators,', '\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-02.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-03.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-04.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-05.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-06.jpg\" /></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs4\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive\" src=\"/public_files/images/TAG-07.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">In a momentous event held this afternoon, the University gymnasium was filled with jubilant faces as 508 graduates, along with their proud parents, key officials, administrators, faculty, staff, and esteemed guests, gathered to celebrate the 30th Commencement Exercises.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe occasion was marked by the inspiring words of Engr. Noel M. Ajoc, the esteemed Commencement Speaker. Addressing the graduating class, Engr. Ajoc encouraged them to push beyond their achievements and strive for greater heights. He urged the graduates not to rest on their laurels but to harness their potential and embrace new challenges that lie ahead.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe event was graced by the presence of CHED Commissioner Jo Mark Libre, who joined in the celebration of this significant milestone. Commissioner Libre emphasized the pivotal role played by parents in the success of the graduates, acknowledging them as the bedrock of their accomplishments. His heartfelt remarks resonated with the attendees and underscored the importance of familial support in the educational journey.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nThe 30th Commencement Exercises served as a testament to the hard work, dedication, and perseverance demonstrated by the graduates throughout their academic journey. As they bid farewell to their university years, they embark on a new chapter filled with limitless possibilities and opportunities.\r\n\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:left\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n#NEMSU2023 #GraduationDay #nemsucares #sculptingbetterlives\r\n\r\n</span></p>', 'TAG-00.jpg', 'The BLAZE – NEMSU Tagbina', NULL, 'news', 1, '2023-07-04 17:05:11', '2023-07-04 17:05:11', '2023-07-04 17:05:11'),
('fefb8749-1d7b-11ef-b18a-a233a240566f', '𝗡𝗤𝗔 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝘀𝘁𝗮𝗿𝘁𝘀 𝟮𝗻𝗱 𝗦𝘂𝗿𝘃𝗲𝗶𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁 𝗶𝗻 𝗡𝗘𝗠𝗦𝗨 𝘃𝗶𝘀𝗶𝘁', 'NQA-2nd-Surveillance-Audit-2024', 'To ensure quality standards, the 𝗡𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝗮𝗹 𝗤𝘂𝗮𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝘂𝗿𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 (𝗡𝗤𝗔) 𝗖𝗘𝗢 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗟𝗲𝗮𝗱 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗠𝗿. 𝗥𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗹𝗼 𝗟. 𝗕𝗲𝗿𝗻𝗮𝗿𝗱𝗶𝗻𝗼 conducted the 𝟮𝗻𝗱 𝗦𝘂𝗿𝘃𝗲𝗶𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁 for his 2-Day visit in North Eastern Mindanao State University, on 𝗠𝗮𝘆 𝟮𝟵-𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟰.', '<br>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\nTo ensure quality standards, the 𝗡𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝗮𝗹 𝗤𝘂𝗮𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝘂𝗿𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 (𝗡𝗤𝗔) 𝗖𝗘𝗢 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗟𝗲𝗮𝗱 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗠𝗿. 𝗥𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗹𝗼 𝗟. 𝗕𝗲𝗿𝗻𝗮𝗿𝗱𝗶𝗻𝗼 conducted the 𝟮𝗻𝗱 𝗦𝘂𝗿𝘃𝗲𝗶𝗹𝗹𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁 for his 2-Day visit in North Eastern Mindanao State University, on 𝗠𝗮𝘆 𝟮𝟵-𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟰. \r\n<br><br>\r\nMr. Bernardino presented the Audit Plan to the key officials and participants to provide a clear outline of the audit process, including the objectives, scope, methodology, and timeline. He also emphasized the purpose of the audit and what is expected during the process.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIn an announcement, Mr. Bernardino revealed the identified offices, departments, and colleges of NEMSU that will undergo an Audit examination. \r\n<br><br>\r\nThe surveillance audit aims to keep NEMSU on track of the standardized systems and processes to ensure quality, and efficiency of services to its valued stakeholders. \r\nThe results of the surveillance audit process will be presented tomorrow, May 30, 2024.\r\n<br>\r\n#sanmiguelcampus #nemsusm #NEMSU\r\n', 'iso-2024.png', 'Public Information Office', 0, 'news', 1, '2024-05-29 13:26:18', '2024-05-29 13:26:18', '2024-05-29 13:26:18'),
('ff754994-220b-11ee-816f-a233a240566f', 'NEMSU TAGBINA LIBRARY BOOK DISPLAY', 'TAGBINAlib-BOOK-DISPLAY', '', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>Bringing the bookstore to our library for greater access and participation of our faculty members in the selection and acquisition of books.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nThank you so much to our faculty members for thoughtfully selecting books for your references. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/tagbDisplay02.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/tagbDisplay03.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md4 col-sm-4 col-sm-4\">\r\n  <img alt=\"\" class=\"img img-responsive large\" src=\"/public_files/images/library/tagbDisplay04.jpg\" />\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</span></p>', 'tagbDisplay01.jpg', 'Ronie A. Sajelan, MSLIS', 10, 'news', 1, '2022-03-22 10:09:53', '2022-03-22 10:09:53', '2022-03-22 10:09:53');
